<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/010e8465afbabce5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "unit of count"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/013c664b3610844b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the bfo projection vocabulary on the procedures slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/016f831ddf6437d4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A credible interval: the Bayesian interval estimate whose semantics rest on a POSTERIOR — an interval carrying a stated posterior probability mass that the parameter lies within it, given the prior, the likelihood, and the data. A subclass of math:BayesianResult, so it is held owl:disjointWith the frequentist math:ConfidenceInterval THROUGH the paradigm parents (a single node is never both — that conflation is math:IntervalKindConflation: they share the word 'interval' and nothing else, frequentist coverage versus posterior mass). It names its posterior context through math:hasPosterior (the math:PosteriorDistribution it summarizes), its bounds through math:hasIntervalBound, and its mass through math:credibleMass (a framed math:ProbabilityValue over that posterior); a credible interval naming no posterior or no credible mass is ill-formed (math:IncompleteCredibleInterval)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/019ae5593b1b4496>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "obtain consent"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/01a162718a372423>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Flow"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/01e1217a3b498915>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Declared Terminology Homograph"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/020af9725ad4ad44>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "licensor"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/022c2938bb4e24af>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Denotation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/02598f7a80e62d68>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Names the external view term or pattern related by a logic:Correspondence. This is an endpoint, not an executable logic:putLeg. Grounding correspondences use it to retain the exact gUFO, BFO, OBO, SUMO, OWL, or SHACL term in the shipped carrier without importing that target ontology."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0268d3a819464af6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "linkage"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/026919507de64740>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has grading"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/026b26b426133196>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "on data range"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/026b647f6e6cacf5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Hodge decomposition to its coexact component — the part lying in the image of the adjoint boundary or coboundary operator. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:CoexactComponent (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/029308add3c6ef84>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "archive"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0293b729a3903521>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "in copyright — EU orphan work"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/029f61e8486cdaed>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:ConfidenceInterval (or math:ConfidenceRegion) to its coverage level — a framed math:ProbabilityValue (a 0.95, a 0.99) that is the proportion of such intervals, under repeated sampling, containing the true parameter. Domain a confidence interval or region, range math:ProbabilityValue (stated in prose). The coverage is a property of the PROCEDURE, never a posterior mass; a confidence interval naming no confidence level is ill-formed (math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval). Its counterpart on the Bayesian side is math:credibleMass, which the two must never be collapsed onto one another."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/02a969baf547a592>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates an interval (a math:ConfidenceInterval, math:CredibleInterval, math:PredictionInterval, or math:ToleranceInterval) to one of its bounds — a lower or an upper endpoint of the interval. Domain an interval kind, range the bound object (stated in prose). A two-sided interval names its lower AND its upper bound (two math:hasIntervalBound edges); a confidence interval that does not name its bounds is ill-formed (math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/02c65bb2263166ac>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — music / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/031fa2adac251d0c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The entity whose existence is recorded by this EntityExistence. Functional: an EntityExistence concerns exactly one entity (constitutive of the situation's identity)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0337caea19573e25>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Datalog projection-surface registry entry — DOCUMENTARY-ONLY, never an enforceable gate. Per Principle 17, Datalog is one of the generated lossy projections logic: enumerates, but Datalog rule/fact syntax is NOT RDF: it cannot be hand-authored as triples inside a TTL slice, so no Datalog construct can ever appear as a real triple predicate or object here. Its gmeow:vocabularyCountKind is \"countKindNonRdfSurface\", which the shared counter resolves to an always-empty enumeration, making its residue structurally 0 by construction rather than by an unenforced policy. gmeow:vocabularyNamespace is a stable documentary marker IRI under the gmeow: authority — not a dereferenceable external vocabulary namespace and never matched against any real triple — chosen precisely because it can never collide with an authored predicate or object. No counter-example fixture claims this vocabulary reds."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0348bcf02628bd18>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a sheaf to one of its compatible restriction maps between stalks."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0355cab14abdaf97>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Sheaf Cohomology"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/036c006fb2e011bf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "source endpoint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/03ab6d85fd0c8225>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The logic: core slice that subsumes a guarded projection vocabulary — the Principle 17 witness that the vocabulary is a generated lossy projection of logic:, not an independent authoring surface. Every guarded vocabulary points here at the logic slice. It is NOT a gmeow:vocabularyPreservation judgment (that names the preservation polarity) and NOT the vocabulary's own namespace: it is the canonical source the vocabulary is a projection OF."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/03bcdc37b9abfea3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Non-increasing (weakly decreasing) monotonicity: x < y entails f(x) ≥ f(y) for all points x, y of the domain — the function never rises. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:monotoneNonIncreaseLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), the non-strict counterpart of math:strictMonotonicityLaw."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/03f31866df3fcf11>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A prediction: a model's forecast value for the outcome at a given input — a point prediction, distinct from the math:PredictionInterval that bounds its uncertainty and from the math:Residual that is the gap between it and the observed value. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, deliberately PARADIGM-NEUTRAL (models predict in both paradigms); it names what it predicts through math:predictionTarget. Held apart from math:Estimate (a value of a parameter or estimand) — a prediction is a value of the OUTCOME for a case, not of a parameter of the model."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/03f8e462e80276a6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates an inference result or a math:HypothesisTest to the math:EffectSize accompanying it — the standardized magnitude of the effect the result concerns, alongside its significance. Domain a result object or a math:HypothesisTest, range math:EffectSize (stated in prose). Naming the effect size as an object is what lets 'how big is the effect', not only 'is it significant', be answered — a test with a p-value but no effect size reports distinguishability without magnitude."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/03f9f495ee3dc7b9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The relation used inside a reified logic:Formula to test a term's lexical form against a regular-expression argument. It lowers to SPARQL REGEX and, with an explicit regex-dialect residue, to sh:pattern; it is not an exact-preservation claim because the regex dialects differ."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/040c63aae1a85b77>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The abstraction variable of a closed-form function — the x in f(x): relates a math:ClosedFormFunction to the math:VariableDeclaration that is its formal argument. Domain math:ClosedFormFunction, range math:VariableDeclaration (typically a math:FreeVariableDeclaration, since the argument is free in the body; stated in prose). Every math:ClosedFormFunction names exactly one; a closed form without a formal argument does not say over which variable it abstracts and is ill-formed (math:UnboundClosedForm). It is the one declaration the function is a function OF, distinguished from the fitted math:functionParameters it is tuned by."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/040d8f088e929016>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Constraint Sugar"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/04530df4da0cee77>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has Laplacian"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/047c8ea80c5af0da>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The unary prefix GMN named-key form `boundary` for math:BoundaryOperator; the partial sign remains non-executable display notation because it is ambiguous with partial differentiation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/04879ec78e22452b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Estimand to the missing-data policy under which it is defined — the intercurrent-event and missing-data handling strategy (a treatment-policy, hypothetical, or composite strategy; a declared math:MissingnessMechanism the target rests on) that fixes what the estimand means when data are incomplete. Domain math:Estimand, range the missing-data policy (stated in prose). One of the six framing coordinates; the same treatment effect under a treatment-policy strategy and under a hypothetical strategy are distinct estimands. Distinct from math:missingnessMechanism, which declares the mechanism a variable's absence follows — this frames the estimand's policy for it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/048ff871bcec13a7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Hamiltonian system or smooth state space to the closed nondegenerate two-form that frames its Hamiltonian dynamics."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/053c4cd6342b7974>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Compact sugar for a path-value type-membership constraint (P4): a logic:onClass target, a logic:valuePath predicate, and a required logic:valueClass. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) → ∀v. P(this,v) → D(v). Frontend-only authoring shortcut."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0579833c0f5716bf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "documentation floor — Exemplified"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/057aebc76f5f987c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "copyright"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0586015ed3006503>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A hypothesis test: the object that binds a math:NullHypothesis (math:nullHypothesis) and a math:AlternativeHypothesis (math:alternativeHypothesis) and a test statistic (math:testStatistic), and PRODUCES a math:PValue (math:pValue) — the structured frame within which a p-value's P(T ≥ t | H0) is well-defined. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; naming its null, its alternative, and its statistic as first-class objects is what keeps a test's meaning inspectable rather than folded into a procedure name."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/059513359f6509b7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has stalk"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/05c12cea4fc56eb9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Ill-Framed P-Value"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/05c20be6e875eb44>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The opinionated uplift advice the axis emits when a slice falls short — the next-best-action text, which MUST cite the SLICE_GUIDE section or Constitution principle it discharges and MUST NOT reference a development ticket or issue number (process linkage lives outside the repo). It is NOT the finding message alone: it is the doctrine-anchored remediation the advisor ranks and offers."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/05e843c67f49e6e8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "accept tracking"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0618ac9eca87b433>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "grounding"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/06362092a966a011>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "provenance-honesty floor — Maximal"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/06c33cdb20976a9f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has copyright"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/06d46a6a37657e04>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Do not infer an omitted index from RDF statement order, which has no semantic ordering."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0710706580d81923>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "diagnostic for"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0760380fbacb1cf2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has data subject"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/07705bb6c5955561>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Compact sugar for a cross-node co-occurrence / inequality constraint (P5): a logic:onClass target and two roles (logic:roleA, logic:roleB) that must, per logic:crossMode, either 'co-occur' (be present together) or 'differ' (never bind the same value). Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint whose integrity is the bi-implication (co-occur) or the join + inequality (differ, via the logic:termEqual filter relation). Frontend-only authoring shortcut."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/077b8159eb6807cf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for logic:iff: `iff`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/079895af6e3a2a8b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A Laplacian built from cellular-sheaf coboundary maps and inner products, measuring incompatibility of local data."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/07e035ff9999e230>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "term regular expression"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/07e70aea37b871ca>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A randomization scheme: the first-class rule by which units were assigned to conditions — simple, blocked, stratified, cluster, or adaptive randomization, with its allocation ratio and any constraints. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the assignment mechanism a math:ExperimentalDesign uses, so how randomness entered the assignment is recorded structure rather than an implicit assumption. Holding the scheme as an object is what lets a design's exchangeability and its analysis's warrant be traced to the mechanism that generated the assignment."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0812b45acc240dbd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "with restrictions"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/083f112f71f96146>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "elapsed time"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0898bd8ec3aa109f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Compactification to the original unbounded space it embeds — the space whose points at infinity the compactification adjoins as a boundary. Domain math:Compactification, range a math:TopologicalSpace or math:Manifold (stated in prose). Every compactification names exactly one; a compactification without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/08be0fce7a86ad93>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the gts slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/090451def162c032>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "policy void on conflict"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0930492144c8cf4a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The translation-coverage-axis score floor to earn the Exemplified tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/09597e6cc244d437>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has rights statement"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/096bd67529c51fcb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — procedures / bfo"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/099621dbad86404a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "ex:noDeprecatedCode a logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Submission ; logic:forbiddenPredicate ex:deprecatedCode ."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/09ab52f06342c973>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "database right"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/09eb698996be14a2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: logic:iff to iff"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/09f8c3f46434d2d7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — epistemics / bfo"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0a2cb305979c247f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "equivalent property"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0a599d4c9caf04f7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Trademark"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0a640890cda74199>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Surprisal"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0ab05dd1848e412a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "SPDX license id"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0abe8d6fe0623aba>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "intervention condition"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0b33bfacb4dde0cc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A sheaf morphism transporting local data between stalks along an inclusion or incidence relation, subject to identity and composition laws."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0b5e0004f17fc4c8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Rights Statement"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0b718963436c1ecf>
