<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0d4858c6f2d12d78>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An observation unit: what a single row of a sample or dataset denotes — the entity a measurement is taken on (a person, a household, a visit, a firm-year). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix through math:observationUnit. Naming the unit explicitly is what makes the grain of the data first-class, so a person-level and a household-level analysis of the same study are never silently conflated."@en .

