<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0f4de4f39aac12f1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Incomplete Persistent-Homology Analysis"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0f5d0e0f0d1e2e04>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A statistical population: the complete collection of units an estimate is meant to refer to — the target of inference, the who-we-care-about. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named as the referent of a math:Estimate or math:Sample through math:population and operationalized by a math:SamplingFrame through math:samplingFrame. Held strictly apart from the frame and the sample so coverage and selection bias are evaluable: the population is who the estimate speaks about, never merely who was measured. An estimate that names no population it refers to is underspecified."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0f7f05df671d48ed>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A cross-validation result: the out-of-sample performance estimate a resampling scheme (k-fold, leave-one-out, repeated, nested) produces for a fitted model — a held-out score with its resampling structure, distinct from an in-sample fit statistic. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the math:FittedModel it evaluates through math:diagnosticFor, so a validated score carries which fit it estimates the generalization of. It is the held-out counterpart to an in-sample math:InformationCriterion, and a math:ModelComparison may weigh either."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0fe75aa001b3efff>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A concrete realization of a form: text (through lang:surfaceText) with a declared script (lang:inScript), encoding (lang:encoding), Unicode normalization (lang:unicodeNormalization), and collation locale (lang:collationLocale). The only stratum where byte identity means anything: two surface forms with different normalization are different surface forms of possibly the same form. A surface either realizes an analyzed form through lang:realizes or is typed lang:UnanalyzedProse — never silently either — and declares how far it has been analyzed through lang:analysisLevel. It may carry a lang:SurfaceAnchor locating it in a source document. Re-encoding or re-normalizing a text creates new surface forms but no new forms."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0fe9686b16424fcc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Incomplete Vector-Symbolic Operation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0ff8414274903a89>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:PValue is ambiguous because it does not carry the frame that makes P(T ≥ t | H0) well-defined: it names no test (neither a math:testStatistic nor the math:HypothesisTest whose math:pValue it is), or no math:nullHypothesis, or no math:nullDistribution, or neither a math:tailDefinition nor a math:alternativeSidedness — or it carries an math:alternativeSidedness outside the six lawful math:Sidedness values. A p-value with a null and a statistic but no tail or sidedness is still ambiguous, because whether the extremity is one-tailed, two-tailed, or mid-p changes the value; such a p-value is ill-formed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/0ffb256e5e6a81a2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A vector space equipped with a declared quadratic form, including its scalar field and degeneracy properties. It is not a bare vector space without that form."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1006251efd8fcc11>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "−∞"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/10302a17765de9fe>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "and (ordered)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/103a33de21f09a0f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The signature (p, q) of a real quadratic space, metric tensor, quadratic form, or Clifford algebra: the counts carried by math:signaturePositive and math:signatureNegative. Structured, not an opaque string — Riemannian is (n, 0), Lorentzian is (1, n−1) or (n−1, 1), and Cl(p,q) uses the same ordered sign counts. The sum p + q equals the carrier dimension; the object is shared rather than re-minted for Clifford semantics."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/10755ff3cd26533a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A homogeneous Clifford or exterior basis element formed as an ordered product of distinct basis generators. It is not an arbitrary multivector or a sum of blades."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1089bc4186908a6a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Incomplete Information Measure"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/108a2a9a2c762d7c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The non-negative integer grade of a homogeneous basis blade."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/109aa9801326e1da>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "license text"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/10b76e0c98bc33b3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Cross-Validation Result"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/10d64061d7e94c6b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "print"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/10de343665dd06c8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "equivariant map"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/10eb6b3bd30bb266>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "test statistic"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/10f01ecc68c4c0e7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Sidedness"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/10f6bfb86bc5655d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: survey to srv"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/110294297ac757ea>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Expressive and Declarative Ontology Alignment Language (edoal:) vocabulary guarded by the projection-vocabulary ratchet — a generated lossy projection of logic: (Principle 17), part of the alignment stack alongside FnO and SSSOM. Its hand-authored constructs are counted by TYPED AXIOM (gmeow:vocabularyCountKind \"countKindTypedAxiom\": distinct triples whose predicate or object IRI falls in edoal:'s namespace). Its declared gmeow:vocabularyAlignmentPredicate set exempts genuine by-reference bridging to an EXTERNAL edoal: object from the residue; an internal gmeow-to-gmeow triple under the same predicate stays in the residue."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1128ebdb040beeb5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "restriction map"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/115ac8e9150f50af>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "blade grade"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/11d6cd155f9408e4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "literal value"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/12136ac263d2e145>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the bfo projection vocabulary on the epistemics slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1241a74e771bab22>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The testing-axis score floor to earn the Linked tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/124dc5c9db51b453>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "non-decrease: x < y entails f(x) ≤ f(y)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/124fed16aa5bb016>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "diverges to +∞"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1271f810200657ab>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A statistical hypothesis: a first-class claim about a population, a parameter, or a data-generating process that a math:HypothesisTest weighs — the object that makes 'what is being tested' inspectable rather than folded into a method name. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; its two testing roles, the tested default (math:NullHypothesis) and its complement (math:AlternativeHypothesis), are its principal subclasses."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/128621915ba48720>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "term in value set"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/12a96f1d36069527>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Canonical extensional equivalence between two properties. It is not a related-property hint; it lowers to owl:equivalentProperty only when the projection preserves the full relation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/12ddadccab1bdfe8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Vector-Symbolic Operation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/133c3ffcbe90dc30>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A closed-world integrity constraint requiring entries in one gmeow:GmnDictionary that share a gmeow:gmnDictionaryEntryAlias to name the same gmeow:gmnDictionaryEntryTerm; one alias never reads back as two terms."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/134352fd436f019d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the documentation slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/13857dfc3cec56ef>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "moral rights"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/13a03e42d1c4b0eb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix to the math:ObservationUnit a single row denotes — the entity each measurement is taken on. Domain a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix, range math:ObservationUnit (stated in prose). Naming the unit fixes the grain of the data, so a person-level and a household-level view of the same study are never silently conflated."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/13cef95144e99e97>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "non-affinity"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/13dd37fe5d93b18b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "annotate"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/14010ac142a8ebca>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Glossary Term Inconsistency"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/142d4dca7390fc13>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Exterior Algebra"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/148131374276bf23>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Spinor"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/14b5de387d05aad9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "One by-reference alignment/bridge predicate IRI this vocabulary exempts from its residue when a matching triple's object resolves to an EXTERNAL (non-gmeow:) namespace — NON-functional, since a vocabulary typically exempts several bridge predicates (rdf:type, rdfs:subClassOf, owl:equivalentClass, rdfs:seeAlso, and the SKOS mapping predicates). Per Principle 5, foundational alignment by reference is \"MORE is always BETTER\" and must never be punished as a second source of truth; an INTERNAL gmeow-to-gmeow triple under the same predicate is NOT exempted (it stays in the residue as a genuine second source of truth). It is NOT gmeow:vocabularyNamespace (which selects candidate triples) but a filter over which of those candidates the counter then subtracts."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/14cca4637e61e13e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Betti Summary"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/14d3ecefbe4c6aa1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "reconstruction of"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/14e3a93a7617c59b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Rule"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/151fea395502acc8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "copyright not evaluated"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1527caaed652b1a8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — concepts / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1543770db8dfffbf>
