    ontolex:writtenRep "Fisher Information"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/15fb5292ba72251c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Unframed Effect Size"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1617f040f5f0a1b3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "ex:contactRoute a logic:DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Contact ; logic:anyOf ex:email, ex:phone ."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1641f6e25e5a4046>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a vector-symbolic operation to the math:Basis fixing the coordinates of its vector space, so the operand and result vectors have unambiguous components and the binding law is reproducible. Domain math:VectorSymbolicOperation, range math:Basis (stated in prose). The basis is part of the operation's frame, never implicit; an operation missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/168e3ef5e2c0767f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "file format"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/16fbdb4b02e81021>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the bfo projection vocabulary on the sensory-environment slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1716f08c97286fe5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A degree-indexed collection of Betti numbers for a declared complex, space, filtration stage, or persistence result. It is not one unscoped Betti number."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1736e64339c8d47c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A one-sided alternative: the extremity is measured in a single, unspecified-here direction of the sampling distribution's tail."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/17a1cec01012631d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A cell complex whose cells are simplices and which is closed under taking faces, with intersections occurring along common faces. It is not an arbitrary cell complex: simplex cells and face closure are required."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/17a492a420f364bf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "date/time"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/180a063ade49f0c7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — notation / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1822c690911fb80d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Direct-Sum Decomposition"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/18373bce4020c079>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "anticommutation verified"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/183b13f18756f96c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Estimator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/187087995e91c728>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "boundedness"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/187f5f38e141b5df>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Sampling Distribution"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/18cdf5ff6bb87fa7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Sheaf Section"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/18e5f33419920669>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "usage info"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/18eeb29a6f9f3347>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Measure Evaluation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/19c2caaa19caa46b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Zigzag Persistence"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/19cab63f737fe55b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a persistent-homology analysis lacks its input, filtration, or persistence-summary output."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/19e2449928c173ae>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An analysis plan: the pre-specified plan a result claims to follow — the primary and secondary endpoints, the estimand, the model, and the decision rule fixed BEFORE the data were seen. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject carrying its version through math:analysisPlanVersion (a version literal or a version object) and named by the inference run that ran it through math:usedAnalysisPlan, so pre-registered versus post-hoc is data, not lost context. A result that names the plan and its version it followed is one whose analysis-was-pre-specified claim is auditable rather than asserted."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/19f9f757a7d25eb9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The linkage-axis score floor to earn the Exemplified tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1a11c38ba94c2ba7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A sample: the units actually drawn and measured — the thing we have, drawn from a math:SamplingFrame through math:sampleOf and referring to a math:StatisticalPopulation through math:population. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject whose rows denote a math:ObservationUnit through math:observationUnit and whose columns are recorded as math:StatisticalVariable through math:statisticalVariable. Held apart from the population it stands in for so the layer estimates coverage rather than conflating who-we-measured with who-we-care-about."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1a3edcb3742de550>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Unframed Operator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1a805992d3bce6a4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Interval to the math:EndpointInclusion of its upper end — math:closedEndpoint (the upper endpoint is a member, the square bracket of …, b]) or math:openEndpoint (the upper endpoint is excluded, the round bracket of …, b). Domain math:Interval, range math:EndpointInclusion (stated in prose). The upper inclusion is required and never silently omitted; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1ad8b9bd83f803e3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "inverse of"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/1ae520d57df23804>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the temporal slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

