<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/20facfd8b0efc9a9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An information criterion: a penalized-fit score for a fitted model that trades goodness-of-fit against complexity — an AIC, a BIC, a WAIC, a DIC, a leave-one-out score. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the math:FittedModel it scores through math:diagnosticFor, so a criterion value is never a bare number detached from the fit it penalizes and the model comparison that reads it. It is the per-model score a math:ModelComparison contrasts, held as its own object rather than an attribute buried in a fit summary."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2120747a1e5bed7f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Incomplete Hodge Decomposition"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/214a7b433222d44f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "prose floor — Grounded"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/217103ef20dbd245>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "copyleft"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/218c30a61581bbf9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "conformal factor"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/21950db38cebba05>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Morph Feature"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/21d5d6b6f54bc604>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "target outcome"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/21d9faf97e86d742>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Type I error rate: α, the probability that a test rejects a true null — the false-positive rate a significance threshold controls. A subclass of math:FrequentistResult; a frequentist operating characteristic defined against the sampling behaviour of the test under the null, distinct from the observed p-value it bounds."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/21e1927d78ebdd3d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:modalForceCounterfactual: `cf`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/22140c7048a3b4ef>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Simple Standard for Sharing Ontological Mappings (sssom:) vocabulary guarded by the projection-vocabulary ratchet — a generated lossy projection of logic: (Principle 17), part of the alignment stack alongside FnO and EDOAL. Its hand-authored constructs are counted by TYPED AXIOM (gmeow:vocabularyCountKind \"countKindTypedAxiom\": distinct triples whose predicate or object IRI falls in sssom:'s namespace). Its declared gmeow:vocabularyAlignmentPredicate set exempts genuine by-reference bridging to an EXTERNAL sssom: object from the residue; an internal gmeow-to-gmeow triple under the same predicate stays in the residue."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/227c18c3c5a47b18>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "field of scalars"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/227ce1d063efeb02>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A dimensionality-reduction analysis that approximates geodesic distances on a neighborhood graph before embedding them in a lower-dimensional space."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/229a5f806e57d3f6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "grant use"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/22a507b4aeb034a4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Requires every declared logic:TermCarrier to carry a logic:termIndex. It is not the list-level ordering check: uniqueness and zero-based contiguity are verified across all sibling carriers by the typed-IR frontend."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/23019cc1ec11eea2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "delay period"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/230a92e09fdaa640>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Maximal"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/230cd478d0d90f21>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the gufo projection vocabulary on the kernel slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2347c03aaeb5d1fd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:GmnCodebook: `gcb`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/23ba61c7faee25ed>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a surprisal to the single outcome whose declared probability under its distribution it takes the negative logarithm of. Domain math:Surprisal, range math:MathematicalObject (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/23c390077ed98ac6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep """The slice-quality rubric module — the ontology-resident, data-driven rubric the gmeow-dev slice-quality advisor binds to. Quality axes, the lattice tier ladder, per-tier score thresholds, advice text, read-scope coeffects, and dated exemptions are all individuals here; Rust ships only a closed set of measurement primitives the axis descriptors name (the Profile rubric-as-data pattern). Grades form a bounded lattice grounded in logic:QualityValue: the roll-up tier is the UNWEIGHTED meet of the per-axis grades, the ratchet is the lattice order, and the scalar tier is a lossy projection of the full per-axis grade vector.

This slice is its own self-application capstone: it must itself score Maximal on the rubric it defines, and its rationales name no test artifact — it is the exemplar of the provenance-honesty rule it introduces."""@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2474e8549c10743e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "null hypothesis"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/24759a2f7b0ecc9b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "play"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/249237233a9a5424>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "information unit"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/24bf9675259d2faf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Clifford Module Decomposition"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/24c1a526b9027f34>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Non-affinity: the function is NOT an affine map — its graph is not a straight line, so there exist three domain points, one an affine combination of the other two, whose graph points fail to be collinear. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:nonAffinityLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), which witnesses the collinearity failure existentially, mirroring the existential/negation shape of math:connectednessLaw."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/252f4d6947a1a875>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "mark text"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/253506b1754fbdb8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "recurring time interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/253a9f6f54172621>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "paraphrase form"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/257dca591a6b6fc2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — standpoint / bfo"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/25ae8af7e1858c2e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Mapper construction to the source metric space it samples — the point cloud (or space) with a declared distance function over which the filter function and the clustering rule are defined. Domain math:MapperConstruction, range math:MetricSpace (stated in prose). The source is part of the construction's frame, never implicit; a construction missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/25dcdb7eef5a416b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Clifford module decomposition to the embedded base-algebra summand."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/25ee3d6c43110f3b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The prose-quality-axis score floor to earn the Exemplified tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/261a0deb224de007>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "in copyright — non-commercial use permitted"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2678a75ef5c6975e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:PiecewiseFunction declares no math:hasPiece (min-count 1) — a piecewise function is defined BY its pieces, so one with none says nothing about what it computes and is ill-formed. Distinct from math:UnframedFunction (a function missing its domain/codomain, which a piecewise function inherits): this failure is the missing-piece gate specific to the piecewise ladder."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/26a5450548f7d04d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:EffectSize to the math:StatisticalContrast whose magnitude it measures — the comparison between conditions (a difference, a ratio, an odds ratio) the effect size quantifies the size of. Domain math:EffectSize, range math:StatisticalContrast (stated in prose). This is the SAME shared math:StatisticalContrast object a math:Estimand targets through math:targetContrast — one modeled contrast referenced by both the estimand's target and the effect size's magnitude, never two near-synonym contrasts — so the effect size and the estimand talk about the same comparison. An effect size naming no contrast is uninterpretable (math:UnframedEffectSize)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/26e677d562fe37b1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "licensee"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/27040bfa2be596e8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — learning / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/27130bc46bdf87ab>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A Bayes factor: the ratio of the marginal likelihoods of two models (or hypotheses) under the data — the Bayesian measure of the evidence the data provide FOR one model OVER another, the update factor from prior odds to posterior odds. A subclass of math:BayesianResult, one of the paradigm-exclusive Bayesian result kinds held owl:disjointWith math:FrequentistResult; it is the Bayesian counterpart to a frequentist test's evidence summary, never a p-value, and is read as a ratio of evidences rather than a tail probability under a null."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/27491a6ed5366a5f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "logic constraint member"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/276f5b9fe24af28c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The provenance-honesty-axis score floor to earn the Linked tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/27db6e2ab454bbcd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Conformal Compactification"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/27f13df717cd102e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The defining law of math:strictlyIncreasing as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared strictly increasing, if x < y and f takes value u at x and v at y, then u < v. The order-preserving mirror of math:strictMonotonicityLaw."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/280765dfea146659>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection vocabulary — DOLCE (dul)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2872179787f6c39c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The axis for documentation completeness: a narrative docs thesis and the docs-pipeline coverage dimensions, consuming the per-slice documentation-maturity standard as-is. It is NOT prose quality (how well strings read) — this measures whether the documentation surfaces exist. The documentation-maturity tier and multi-format panels remain exempt until their producers land."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/28b2faaff403d28e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The documentation-axis score floor to earn the Exemplified tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/28cdcb11ac65d9ff>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the ai slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/28df5537124c973c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "recovery-loss contract"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/28e303e4307ba3ad>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "registration number"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/29d0fc741b73e55a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The GMEOW Slice-Quality Rubric Module — classes, properties, and individuals of the GMEOW super-vocabulary that make per-slice quality a queryable, reasoned, data-driven rubric."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2a2679b8e6a7f692>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Type II error rate: β, the probability that a test fails to reject a false null under a specified alternative — the false-negative rate. A subclass of math:FrequentistResult; a frequentist operating characteristic defined against the sampling behaviour of the test under the alternative, the complement of math:StatisticalPower (1 − β)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2a5633a2e0aa8409>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:modalForceNecessary: `nec`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2af14acfadf7064b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis threshold"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2af939655a4fcb85>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The audited named-key ruling for the tilde notation of math:Reversion."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2b281606ef5052ea>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A model assumption: a first-class condition a math:StatisticalModel or math:FittedModel posits about the data-generating process — normality of errors, homoscedasticity, independence of observations, linearity, proportional hazards. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a model through math:modelAssumption, so an assumption is an object that can be checked (by a diagnostic), cited (by a result), or reported violated, rather than left implicit in the choice of model. A model whose assumptions are stated as objects is one whose validity conditions are queryable rather than folded into a method name."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2b933244cf1740c2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "over sheaf"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2bd24bd09957d005>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Canonical relation subsumption: every pair related by the subject property is related by the object property. It is not a label hierarchy; it lowers to rdfs:subPropertyOf."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2bf03b5bb2a7295e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A reified per-slice, per-vocabulary committed residue ceiling — the maximum ungrounded-residue count a named gmeow:ProjectionVocabulary may measure for a named slice, enforced by the make-check gate as a LOWER-ONLY monotonic ratchet (the value may fall but never rise), the exact inverse polarity of gmeow:AxisFloorCommitment. It pairs one gmeow:ceilingSlice, one gmeow:ceilingVocabulary, and one gmeow:ceilingCount into a single ratchet cell. It is NOT a gmeow:AxisFloorCommitment (that is a raise-only score floor, not a count) and NOT a measured count (that is computed live by the shared residue counter): it is the committed maximum a slice's measured residue for a vocabulary may never exceed, lowered only after a genuine measured migration grounds constructs out of the residue."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2c04e68a02a27491>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "absolute position"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2c10b3c9791f052e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "decomposes flow"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2c170c2dbe05c35b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "analysis-plan version"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2c22dec7c9980194>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "translation coverage"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2c38adb542750191>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An algebra decomposed into grade-indexed components whose multiplication respects the declared grading law. It is not an arbitrary direct-sum decomposition: multiplication must respect grades."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2c56fae3dba8ccac>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "use count"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2c7246f9ea1848b5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:VectorUnbinding to the key (cue) math:Vector supplied to retrieve a bound factor — the other operand of the original binding, or its inverse under the declared binding law. Domain math:VectorUnbinding, range math:Vector (stated in prose). Without the key there is nothing to probe the bound vector with, so an unbinding missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2cc0c4f092785a33>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:LimitResult to its math:LimitOutcome — math:convergesFinitely, math:divergesToPositiveInfinity, math:divergesToNegativeInfinity, or math:divergesWithoutLimit. Domain math:LimitResult, range math:LimitOutcome (stated in prose). The outcome is required; a result without a declared outcome is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2cea38696b00abdb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Prose Quality"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2cef1749864070db>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 named-key binding for math:HodgeLaplacian: `hlap`, which distinguishes the Hodge operator from other capital-delta conventions."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2d109b0277a7b0e9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The audited structured-constructor ruling for the wedge notation of math:ExteriorProduct."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2d2311b2208473d6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "information floor — Exemplified"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2d3b685cb1ef9c9c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — inhabitation / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2d494df8d4943a5e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Rule"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2d541757118c1931>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "derive / modify"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2d5a329407f598fa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "multiple-comparison family"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2dc687d4faa0b1b8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "convexity"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2dcd013154d326e0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:CredibleInterval does not carry the structure that makes it a Bayesian interval estimate — its posterior context through math:hasPosterior (the math:PosteriorDistribution it summarizes) or its posterior mass through math:credibleMass (a framed math:ProbabilityValue over that posterior). A credible interval with no posterior, or with no credible mass, cannot state a posterior probability that the parameter lies within it, and is ill-formed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2df8347067f3676d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A missingness indicator: the companion variable or flag marking, per observation unit, whether a math:StatisticalVariable's value is present or absent — the R_i of the missing-data literature. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject attached to the variable it flags through math:hasMissingnessIndicator. A variable carrying a missingness indicator has values that encode absence, so an analysis depending on it must declare the math:MissingnessMechanism (MCAR/MAR/MNAR) it assumes, or it is ill-formed (math:ImplicitMissingness)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2e089e135969c318>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A statistical contrast: the modeled comparison notion between conditions — a difference, a ratio, an odds ratio, a hazard ratio of an outcome between a treatment and a reference condition. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the comparison as a first-class object. This is the SINGLE shared contrast object that both a math:Estimand's target comparison (math:targetContrast) and an effect size's contrast reference — one modeled object, never two near-synonym classes for 'the difference being estimated' and 'the difference an effect size measures'. Holding the contrast once, shared, is what keeps the estimand's target and the effect-size's scale talking about the same comparison."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2e2c9d952c8fc34c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Symplectic Form"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2e4b9f9fefc2c19d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "less than or equal to"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2e63063821948134>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "upper endpoint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2e6e3f34924b4871>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A reified source-form-to-target-form pairing — the atom of a translation. Names its source form through lang:translationSource, its target form through lang:translationTarget, and the sibling unit it aligns with through lang:translationOf, and it carries the law-spine of the crossing by pointing — through lang:translationCorrespondence — at exactly one logic:Correspondence node. That Correspondence, not the unit, holds the logic:preservationKind, the logic:morphismClass, the logic:correspondenceRelation, the logic:mnemomorphic witness enumerating any untranslatable residue, the logic:hasDeterminacy, and any logic:hasLawClaim. A unit whose target is inadequate is marked through lang:translationGap; the enumerated residue itself lives on the carried Correspondence's mnemomorphic witness, never on the unit."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2e8acd4ef57cb01c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:PiecewiseFunction to one of its math:FunctionPiece parts. Domain math:PiecewiseFunction, range math:FunctionPiece (stated in prose). A piecewise function names one or more pieces (≥ 1, unbounded — a function has at least one piece, and may have arbitrarily many); a piecewise function with no piece is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedPiecewiseFunction)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2e98862a2f286f3a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A family of intervals representing the same persistent-module decomposition encoded by feature birth and death lifetimes. It is not a persistence diagram, although the two may encode equivalent interval data."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2ed2f48ebac36ded>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "relative position"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2edce623bca1fd52>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "no copyright — contractual restrictions"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2f4177c0e6dda004>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "constraint operator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2f556b5bed04df03>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "information floor — Maximal"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2facda5422700096>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "function parameter"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/2fb93da6ab590ffd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "translation floor — Maximal"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3023ce8a01646db0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The axis reads only the target slice's own module, examples, and tests — no dependency or merged graph. The tightest coeffect."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3055a7ba4750516e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The inclusive maximum number of logic:onProperty values belonging to the qualifying logic:onClass or logic:onDataRange. It does not count fillers outside that qualifier; it lowers to owl:maxQualifiedCardinality."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/306e2bacb339179e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Unbound Closed Form"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3095a3a16f293cfb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "split/join verified"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/309e9024743d927b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection vocabulary — SSSOM"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/30d5984969501c87>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Vector Field"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3126c6cf85817c69>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The inclusive minimum number of logic:onProperty values required by an unqualified logic:Restriction. It does not filter fillers by class or datarange; it lowers to owl:minCardinality."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/316de68cf6aa4e51>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "attribution url"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3172ff15a4ba4e93>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Incomplete Dimensionality-Reduction Analysis"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3179687276046bd2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Grapheme"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/31a28f20fbb65ae5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Implication Antecedent Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/31c1036836c364f4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The signed extended real line ℝ̄ = ℝ ∪ {−∞, +∞}: the real number system with its two poles adjoined. A math:NumberSystem individual, sibling to math:realNumbers and math:complexNumbers, not a class — it reuses the number-system machinery rather than a parallel one, relating the reals as a subsystem (math:realNumbers math:subsystemOf math:ExtendedRealLine) and adjoining the two extended-real points math:PositiveInfinity and math:NegativeInfinity as its members (each math:inNumberSystem math:ExtendedRealLine). Because math:NumberSystem is a subclass of math:Set, the system IS the set of its points, so it can be the codomain a signed divergent field — an extended-real-valued function whose value may run off to either pole — ranges over. Distinct from ℂ: ℝ̄ compactifies the ordered line with two signed ends, it does not close it algebraically; a value in a signed-extended-real slot is a finite real, +∞, or −∞ (math:MalformedExtendedReal otherwise)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/31d070d7c924da69>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Smoothness (C^∞ / real-analyticity): the function has derivatives of EVERY order. Unlike its siblings math:nonAffinity, math:convexity, and math:boundedness — each backed by a real first-order logic:Formula — smoothness is genuinely SECOND-ORDER: it quantifies over the infinite family of all derivatives, which is not first-order axiomatizable. So it is NOT faked as a first-order law but backed by the honest recorded boundary math:smoothnessBoundary (logic:expressivenessBoundary logic:SecondOrder, logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported), referenced through math:definingLaw and rdfs:seeAlso. This exercises the explicit expressiveness-boundary arm: a real boundary carried in the loss ledger, never silent prose."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/31f42afc3c058298>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "missingness mechanism"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/31f8352f23e3be8f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "sampling frame"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/31f968d55298a6ae>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "formal argument"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/327fd5d3db0cf6c9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "proprietary"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/329c963a40552ae2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Kullback–Leibler Divergence"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/33a99d03f91d5857>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Persistence Diagram"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/341952b44daf1baa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A closed-world integrity constraint requiring two gmeow:GlossaryEntry members of one gmeow:Glossary that share a gmeow:glossaryConcept to carry the same gmeow:glossaryTranslation; one sense never reads back as two divergent translations across batches. The structural dual of lang:GmnDictionaryAliasInjectivityConstraint: alias->term injectivity there, concept->translation functional-dependency here."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/342b10a05a60810d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Type I Error Rate"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/349a2468655aeba7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A mathematically framed quantity measuring uncertainty, dependence, divergence, or information relative to declared distributions, logarithm base, and units."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/34dee3d99a424f0b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "glossary sense"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/34ea9b4684ea8032>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the kernel slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3508cffd8a7a0d7c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The degree-minus-one operation on a chain complex whose square is zero and whose homology records cycles modulo boundaries. It is not a generic derivative or an untyped geometric boundary operation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3599149000fe4366>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A topological-data-analysis activity that computes homology across a declared filtration and emits persistence summaries; it is the method, not the filtration itself."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/35e41db26720078f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Function (or a math:FunctionPiece) to the math:Interval over which its math:hasBound ε holds. Domain math:Function or math:FunctionPiece, range math:Interval (stated in prose). Together with math:hasBound it grounds the boundedness law math:boundednessLaw: |f(x)| ≤ ε for every x in this interval. A bound stated without the interval it holds on is incomplete — the boundedness claim is scoped to a region, never global by default."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/35f887f93aa69871>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Incomplete Cellular Sheaf"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/360d34d8994a02bc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:methodStreaming: `strm`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/362e04fd2a42499f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Canonical class disjointness: no individual may instantiate both class expressions. Distinct from logic:disjoint, the mereological relation between individuals; lowers to owl:disjointWith."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/365918ebb9019e6a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "in copyright — rights-holder unlocatable"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/368438c3c1e78beb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when one node is typed BOTH a math:CalibrationDiagnostic and a math:StabilityCalibrationRecord — the STATISTICAL sense of calibration (a model's predicted probabilities against observed frequencies) conflated with the TOPOLOGICAL sense (a credence calibrated against a bottleneck stability bound over a math:PersistenceLifetime). They share the word 'calibration' and nothing else. Because math:CalibrationDiagnostic ⊑ math:ModelDiagnostic ⊑ math:MathematicalObject and math:StabilityCalibrationRecord ⊑ math:MathematicalObject both descend from math:MathematicalObject, the disjointness is NOT entailed by their parents and is asserted DIRECTLY (math:CalibrationDiagnostic owl:disjointWith math:StabilityCalibrationRecord); the native DL coherence gate forces any individual typed both to owl:Nothing, and the paired SHACL shape (math:CalibrationSenseConflationShape) surfaces the same conflation as a finding so a consumer selects on the specific class, never on the shared token."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/36dfb9a9f3d0f66b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection floor — Linked"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3708e68e57caded6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a quadratic space or Clifford algebra to the quadratic form governing its metric relation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/373c03aeacd89253>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A mid-p tail: the p-value uses the mid-p correction, counting half the probability of the observed value in the tail to reduce the conservativeness of an exact discrete test."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/376558ae4e1157a7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A topological space assembled from cells by attaching each cell boundary to lower-dimensional cells. It is not merely a partition or mesh: cell dimensions and attaching maps are constitutive."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3776a85b46a2a759>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: logic:forall to fa"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/37e107641511b225>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Clifford anti-involution that reverses the order of basis generators in every blade. It is not grade involution; its grade-dependent signs arise from order reversal."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/37ed98f8e32053ba>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "recovered operand"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/37fe7f67dd09ca18>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Persistent-homology analysis over a sequence whose structure maps may point forward or backward, permitting additions and removals. It is not ordinary forward-only persistence."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/38490815b0b95acc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The unary prefix GMN named-key form `hlap` for math:HodgeLaplacian; capital delta remains non-executable display notation because it is overloaded across several operator families."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3852e41260680a0d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An ordered real interval: the intensional set { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper } of the points of the extended real line between two ordered endpoints. It names BOTH its endpoints — the lower through math:lowerEndpoint and the upper through math:upperEndpoint — and BOTH its endpoint inclusions — whether each end is included (a closed, square-bracket end) or excluded (an open, round-bracket end) — through math:lowerInclusion and math:upperInclusion. A bounded end names a finite numeric literal; an unbounded end names a pole (math:PositiveInfinity or math:NegativeInfinity) as its endpoint, and such an infinite end is always open (∞ is a limit point of ℝ̄, never a member). The inclusion is NEVER silently omitted: [0, 1) is the half-open unit interval and (0, 1) is the open one, and which is meant is data, not convention — an interval missing an endpoint or an inclusion is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval). It is NOT the statistics math:ConfidenceInterval, which is a frequentist estimator carrying a coverage level and a point estimate, not an ordered subset of the line; a math:Interval is the pure order-theoretic set, the external anchor being the OpenMath interval1 content dictionary."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/38a0596e674237c5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The declared, deterministic rule applied to the inverse image of each cover element to partition it into clusters — for example single-linkage clustering at a fixed distance threshold (math:clusteringThreshold). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the rule as a first-class object so a Mapper's node set is reproducible, never the output of an unspecified clustering step. A Mapper construction whose clustering rule is omitted or left to convention is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/38c6106303a04495>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — model-serving / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/38fdc1f38e23abab>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has quadratic form"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/391bf0309b95b94e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Closed-Form Function"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3954884d472fa4e5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "spatial coordinates"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/396c080f98b97e35>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Conflict Strategy"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3977a86b11280677>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The effective residue ceiling for any slice that carries no explicit gmeow:ProjectionCeilingCommitment against this vocabulary — 0 for every guarded vocabulary, so a slice's FIRST ungrounded use of a previously-absent vocabulary reds the gate rather than silently passing. It is NOT a per-slice gmeow:ceilingCount (that overrides this default when an explicit commitment exists): it is the vacuous-case floor that closes the net-new-vocab loophole without materializing hundreds of explicit zero-ceiling individuals."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3984a39db16f470a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The exact scalar square of a declared Clifford basis generator under the algebra's signature convention."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/399dce33a0d58590>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A sampling distribution: the distribution of a statistic under repeated sampling — the law the value of a test statistic would follow across replications of the study. A subclass of math:Distribution, so it names its math:distributionFamily and math:distributionParameterization like any distribution; it is the natural range of a p-value's math:nullDistribution, the distribution of the statistic UNDER the null against which the observed value is placed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/39a1f83cc4aaa7d6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Do not attach logic:termLiteralDatatype to an IRI, variable, or sequence-marker carrier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/39c198c255bf8f5e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
