<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3b289a94b001240d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for lang:Translation: `xl`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3b5715481a3b765b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Statistical Power"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3b6451351f46fda3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A unit policy: how the values of a math:StatisticalVariable are dimensioned and encoded — the unit of measure, rounding, and coding convention the recorded numbers follow. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the convention so a value is never a bare number without the policy that gives it meaning. Distinct from the missing-value encoding, which is carried by math:MissingValueCode; the unit policy governs the present values, not their absence."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3b9bcc0006191e6a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Clifford Anticommutation Witness"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3b9f163eda1bbc70>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Persistent-homology analysis over a filtration indexed by a partially ordered parameter space of dimension greater than one. It is not a collection of unrelated one-parameter persistence runs."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3bf956e179649ed4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — sexuality / bfo"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3bfedc93541b77ce>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Equivariant Map"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3c202a56bae76ff6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:ModelDiagnostic to the method it applies — a residual-analysis procedure, a goodness-of-fit test, an influence measure, a reliability-curve or expected-calibration-error binning for a math:CalibrationDiagnostic. Domain math:ModelDiagnostic, range the diagnostic method object (stated in prose). The method is a first-class object, not an opaque label, so a diagnostic's procedure is queryable alongside the fit it evaluates; a diagnostic naming no method is ill-formed (math:UnanchoredDiagnostic). Held apart from math:usesProofMethod (a proof's strategy) and math:estimator (an estimate's procedure): this is the method a diagnostic applies over a fit."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3c4603d62869c6c3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "absolute temporal position"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3c4b2aed91276245>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — standpoint / dul"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3c4fbea046c8c241>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "boundedness: |f(x)| ≤ ε for every x in the interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3c65b3b5b6c055e1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The defining law of math:strictlyDecreasing as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared strictly decreasing, if x < y and f takes value u at x and v at y, then u > v. math: expresses the law; logic: owns reasoning over it. A sibling of math:continuityLaw in the same first-order style; the monotonicity a strictly-decreasing piece carries, backed by a real law rather than a bare token."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3c8f0627c31a9e66>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The binary infix GMN named-key form `lcon` for math:LeftContraction; the contraction sign remains display notation because the named key is cheaper under the pinned BPE."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3cbcd4a910640493>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — lang / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3ccab2f2f11486b4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Compact sugar for a forbidden-pattern constraint (P7): a logic:onClass target and a logic:forbiddenPredicate (optionally pinned to a logic:forbiddenValue). Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) → ¬∃b. forbidden(this,b) (or the pinned-value form ¬ forbidden(this, value)). Frontend-only authoring shortcut."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3cd6c48ebdc487b8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A scalar function on a symplectic state space whose symplectic gradient generates the Hamiltonian flow."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3ce5ca4494c61ccf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The headline axis: per-layer, per-concept grounding on the triad — foundation stereotypes, mediates relations, OWL characteristics as logic axioms, framed quantities on math, reified denotation and lang forms on lang, and detection of domain twins of triad terms. It is NOT mere annotation presence (that is the information axis) — it measures whether concepts are thin domain layers over thick grounding references (Principle 19; SLICE_GUIDE §4)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3d026164055a8433>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "disjoint with"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3d03ad8109d8395e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A model comparison: a first-class object weighing two or more fitted models against one another — a likelihood-ratio test, an information-criterion difference, a cross-validated score comparison, a Bayes-factor model choice. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; it names the math:FittedModel objects it evaluates through math:diagnosticFor (the same anchoring edge a diagnostic uses to point at a fit), so 'which model, and how it compared' is an answerable object rather than an implicit preference. Making the comparison first-class is what keeps model selection auditable rather than read off a single reported number."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3e16c1cdef17aa09>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "conditions of access"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3e3bbcce36c678fb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The data-quality dimension for translation coverage — the fraction of a slice's localizable literals carrying audited translations, measured per-language by per-literal-class, with full coverage requiring English, French, and Mandarin."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3e5938e70e83f173>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The read-breadth coeffect an axis is granted — an open value vocabulary of individuals from slice-local through the whole merged closure. It bounds what the primitive may READ, never what it may advise (advice is single-slice at every scope). It is NOT a projection target and NOT an advice scope."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3e5eb67badd0477c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "effect-size contrast"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3e62da7792de56be>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:Estimate is ill-formed because it does not fix what it estimates or how: it names neither its estimand through math:estimatesEstimand nor its estimated parameter through math:estimatedParameter, or it names no estimator through math:estimator. An estimate is the structured result object of the process / result / claim separation, not a bare number; it must reference its estimand and/or its model parameter and the procedure that produced it. An estimate missing its target or its act is underspecified."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3eae9a4ac8dc02c0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis-floor commitment — math / axisMaximalLinkage"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3eb84162ad2fa343>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A null hypothesis (H0): the tested default a math:HypothesisTest presumes and a p-value is computed under — the no-effect or no-difference claim whose sampling behaviour frames the test statistic. A subclass of math:Hypothesis, named by a test through math:nullHypothesis and by a math:PValue as the hypothesis its P(T ≥ t | H0) is conditioned on."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3ed8fdf30bbf87ee>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "concurrent use"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3f0e516085ed8d86>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "measure result"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3fc0d574c943b46a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "equivariant under"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3fdfcc99493f8029>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The axis reads the whole merged, reasoned closure — required for inferential centrality and domain-twin detection — while still emitting advice about the target slice alone."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/3fe2116b71a934b2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Links an entity to the event that brought it into existence — the general form of birth (person), founding (organization), minting (currency), or realization (reference frame). Non-functional: competing standpoint-indexed creation claims coexist, none privileged. A Person's birth event is ALSO typed gmeow:eventTypeBirth (co-equal value, not a subclass)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/400125247746e655>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "patent"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/403fa0eb5201ca0d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "provenance honesty"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/40592a13f260241d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Rendering"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/408812a292e5538f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Calibration Diagnostic"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/40a91ea606e44cd0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Grade Projection"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/40e05e16a4e0c526>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "analysis input"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/411055aaee2301f6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when an analysis that depends on a math:StatisticalVariable whose values encode absence — a variable carrying a math:MissingnessIndicator through math:hasMissingnessIndicator (or referencing a math:MissingValueCode) — declares no math:MissingnessMechanism through math:missingnessMechanism, and so assumes an MCAR/MAR/MNAR mechanism implicitly rather than stating it. The validity of every missing-data method is conditional on which mechanism holds; leaving it implicit is ill-formed. Primary gate: the SHACL-SPARQL requirement (math:ImplicitMissingnessShape) that a variable with a declared missingness indicator name its math:MissingnessMechanism."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/411649d66a07cec7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "statement about"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/417817e7d5a2e1fa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for logic:and: `and`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/41d019e892a0180c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "exemption reason"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/41f336d719a6173d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The grounding-axis score floor to earn the Linked tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4236ce0d5e61d59e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Quality Tier"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/42401c8621382d41>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Quadratic Form"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4261cc0c42550a48>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "target dimension"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/42fe3169e50b63c3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The simplicial complex at a scale whose simplices are finite point sets with all pairwise distances at most that scale. It is not a Čech complex: pairwise distance bounds do not require one common ball intersection."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/430ada1375be9533>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "ex:minimumMembers a logic:AggregateConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Team ; logic:aggFunction \"COUNT\" ; logic:aggPath ex:member ; logic:aggComparator \">=\" ; logic:aggCompareTo 2 ."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/431d66d37363ad82>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Estimand to the intervention or exposure condition it conditions on — the treatment, policy, or exposure whose effect the estimand quantifies (a do-condition, an assigned arm, a hypothetical intervention). Domain math:Estimand, range the intervention condition (stated in prose). One of the six framing coordinates and the causal hinge of the estimand; without a declared intervention condition an average treatment effect is not well-posed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/43478e9fe817d86b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "GMEOW Slice-Quality Rubric Module"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4348061884c592c4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Unbacked Analytic Property"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/434adbc444d002d2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — diagnostics / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/437eedcea8445047>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:PValue to the multiplicity adjustment applied to it — a Bonferroni, Holm, or Benjamini–Hochberg correction. Domain math:PValue, range the adjustment object (stated in prose). Naming the adjustment as an object is what makes 'was this p-value corrected for multiplicity, and how' answerable rather than implicit."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/43c10d6e03ae08d4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Metric Space"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/43e7f5e61c6af6b8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The audited named-key ruling for the capital-delta notation of math:HodgeLaplacian."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/43fdea21320b59c4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "stalk over cell"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/441ab704ce291b44>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Canonical inverse-relation declaration: P(x,y) holds exactly when Q(y,x) holds. It is not property equivalence because the argument order reverses; it lowers to owl:inverseOf."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/443d44bdee95201f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The outcome of a limit that grows without bound: f runs off to the positive pole, so the math:LimitResult carries math:PositiveInfinity as its math:limitResultValue. The case lim_{x→a} f(x) = +∞ — a definite point on the extended real line ℝ̄, never a finite literal."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/44c2e6f56b00115f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has interval bound"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/44d06a53fc15c65a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "ex:contactChoice a logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Contact ; logic:choicePredicate ex:email, ex:phone ; logic:choiceMode \"exactly-one\" ."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4504ecaba105453e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "vocabulary default ceiling"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/451d80f1826eedb4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Clifford Extension"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/451e229acd34f0eb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Constraint Logic"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4527fdb3b4f7dbdb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has missingness indicator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/453c56f9f43b743f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Logarithm Base"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/45430280c72e3909>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:RecoveryLossContract to the exact math:RationalValue of its recovery-loss bound — 0/1 exactly when an exact algebra makes the operation invertible, and a stated positive rational otherwise — carried as an exact numerator/denominator pair, never a decimal. Domain math:RecoveryLossContract, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/46162f128efe5ad5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A joint probability distribution over two or more random variables, from which each marginal is recoverable. A subclass of math:Distribution; a mutual information is taken over a joint distribution, whose divergence from the product of its marginals it measures."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4627ff4d6c893836>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Fisher information to the parametric likelihood model whose score-function curvature it measures. Domain math:FisherInformation, range math:Distribution (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/465773e5f7716660>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Variable Role"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/465ed561c48a1bb1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the model-serving slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/46670d92fbcf0ad7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A finite class expression whose members are named by a logic:oneOf RDF list. It lowers to an OWL nominal (owl:oneOf) and remains first-class in logic: even when a weaker target profile cannot carry nominals."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/466d1d967147e0e7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "copyright status"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/469d31006bbc2476>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 named-key binding for math:DirectSumDecomposition: `ds`, cheaper than the fragmented circled-plus display sign."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/46b2530912cde8de>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "product context"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/46da7f1ba4ba67d9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Exemplified"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/477af2adbf213087>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "event"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/47af544d2821af50>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "include"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/47c74e0f7551a513>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "smoothness: an honest recorded second-order boundary (no first-order formula)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/47c95df306cf9f40>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Literal Datatype Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/47d586ba8723b0fa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Compact sugar for a choice-group cardinality constraint (P1): a logic:onClass target, a set of logic:choicePredicate predicates, and a logic:choiceMode ('exactly-one', 'at-most-one', or the 'exactly-one-of-N' alias of 'exactly-one'). The compiler expands it into a canonical logic:Constraint whose integrity is the XOR / at-most formula over the ∃-requiredness of each predicate. Frontend-only: it is not a new node kind, only an authoring shortcut."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/483756725eaae020>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Provide one head, the positive and optional stratified-negative body atoms, and any explicit guards or aggregate specification."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/485e54760e35302c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "prediction target"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4884d35664f633f9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed raise-only measured-score floor for the axisMaximalGrounding quality axis on the math slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured score falls below it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/48de74e2c9efd339>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the rights slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/490419f5625691ad>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Privacy Notice"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/49616966d4b3862e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "vocabulary count kind"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/49bde8a0eb5fc54c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "greater"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/49d913b14f61f001>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "expired"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/49de5c545020528f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The recovery-loss (fidelity) contract of a vector-symbolic operation: a first-class mathematical object carrying the exact math:RationalValue loss bound (through math:lossBound) on the discrepancy between a recovered operand and the original — 0/1 exactly when an exact algebra makes the operation invertible, and a stated positive rational otherwise. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject. Recovery is approximate unless an exact algebra proves otherwise, so the contract is constitutive: an unbinding whose fidelity is left implicit cannot claim invertibility, and a vector-symbolic operation missing the contract is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/49dfad5da31ef3e1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Use whenever an RDF argument or quantifier-binding carrier is reconstructed as a typed IR term."@en .

