<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4c1472ae3f205cd6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed raise-only measured-score floor for the axisFlagshipCounterExampleDepth quality axis on the math slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured score falls below it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4c2e7be841efff16>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The value a convergent or pole-divergent math:LimitResult evaluates to — a finite numeric literal for a math:convergesFinitely outcome, or the extended-real pole math:PositiveInfinity / math:NegativeInfinity for a math:divergesToPositiveInfinity / math:divergesToNegativeInfinity outcome. Domain math:LimitResult, range a finite numeric literal or a pole individual (stated in prose). Like math:totalMass and math:extendedRealValue, it is an rdf:Property, not an owl:ObjectProperty or owl:DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal (the finite value) and an individual (a pole): neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the extended-real range without a DL contradiction. Optional and absent on a math:divergesWithoutLimit result, which has no point of ℝ̄ to name; present and in agreement with the outcome otherwise (math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4c95130bbc65e904>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dual-licensed"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4ccb5a7210ecbd9f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Do not collapse IRI, variable, literal, and sequence-marker values into a shared string field; their kinds affect formula meaning."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4cdc35ac8b3734aa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "extract"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4ce5a8450c51f417>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "industrial design right"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4d25f73a365e5f9e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The directed expected log-density ratio from one declared probability distribution to another, not a symmetric distance."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4d3dcbb0022a24fa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Observation Unit"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4d9c1505cfaa196f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Restriction"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4e0372e7e6146402>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the agentic slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4e1bd9cb52fe7db6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:EffectSize to the math:MeasurementScale it is expressed on — the standardization (a standard-deviation scale for a Cohen's d, a correlation scale, a log-odds scale for an odds ratio) that fixes how its magnitude is read. Domain math:EffectSize, range math:MeasurementScale (stated in prose). The same math:MeasurementScale first-class object the variables layer uses; an effect size naming no scale is a magnitude with no units of comparison, uninterpretable (math:UnframedEffectSize)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4e420750b64acbc4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A closed endpoint: the endpoint is a member of the interval — the square bracket of [a, …) or (…, b]. The case where lower ≤ x (or x ≤ upper) admits equality; only a finite endpoint can be closed, since an infinite pole is never a member of ℝ̄."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4e56e669bd2e53a2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Use for productive Horn, existential-rule, or stratified-negation derivations."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4e5fe142d443c175>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis dimension"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4e898512a23e4c9e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for lang:Denotation: `den`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4f28cf69b6561064>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The boolean result of exactly checking the named distinct-generator anticommutation witness."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4f5904da7a874d80>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Links a logic:Enumeration to the RDF list of its named members. It is not an open suggestion list; it lowers to owl:oneOf, and members may be IRIs or literals according to the enumerated expression."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4f5adffb77ff92c8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "information floor — Grounded"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4f6f3d825de633b6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a dimensionality-reduction analysis lacks its input, target dimension, or output embedding."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4f956dbc4f410467>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: computational model to cmp"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4fa21dc7a54fecf5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Fisher information to the model parameter with respect to which the log-likelihood score and its expected curvature are taken. Domain math:FisherInformation, range math:DistributionParameter (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4fdad92fa28f0303>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The linkage-axis score floor to earn the Maximal tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4ff1ff7ef676e85f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An exact tail: the p-value uses the exact (typically discrete) tail probability rather than a continuous approximation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/4ff3d0d79ecc2c7b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a cellular-sheaf stalk to the cell of the base complex to which it is assigned."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/502f6d91dd514ddc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Joint Distribution"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/506d4607ae9cee15>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The number system an operator's result lies in — the target of its signature. Domain math:ArithmeticOperation, range math:NumberSystem (stated in prose). Every math:ArithmeticOperation names exactly one; an operator without its codomain is unframed (math:UnframedOperator). The declared target may be wider than the operator's domain — a real even root or a real logarithm lands in ℂ, so math:Root and math:Logarithm frame math:realNumbers → math:complexNumbers honestly rather than pretending the result stays real."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/50a16764afb0f872>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A dated record that an axis or sub-metric is not yet measurable because its owning producer is genuinely unlanded — a first-class, gate-checked, self-cleaning artifact, NOT a silent descope. Every exemption carries the reason, the date it was minted, and the Rust symbol whose appearance in the repo makes it STALE; the completeness gate requires an axis or an exemption for every projection target, and the staleness gate reds the moment the exempted producer resolves."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/50b719e35683d16f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "industry"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/50c308a96ee0e248>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a cellular sheaf lacks its base complex, stalks, or restriction maps."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5135d3bbe1a80a73>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A survey design: the declared sampling scheme that makes a math:Sample analyzable as more than a simple random sample — the stratification (math:Stratum), clustering (math:Cluster), and weighting (math:SamplingWeight) under which the sample was drawn. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject binding the design elements into a first-class object, so design-based estimation and variance are queryable. A design-based estimate that treats a stratified, clustered, weighted sample as a simple random sample misstates its uncertainty."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/514d101e29346c57>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Information Measure"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5172558c9ae728a1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Datarange"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/517ba7002d77d866>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "one-sided"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/51bb0cc53a89aac2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The axis (or the axis a sub-metric belongs to) this exemption covers. It is NOT the producer symbol (that is gmeow:exemptionProducer)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/51dd16fb29011803>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Prediction Interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/520de36aeb664497>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The meaning assignment from `ds` to the class math:DirectSumDecomposition; it deliberately carries no executable grapheme."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/520e4adad7a61007>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Logical Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/52167990dddce6e7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A graded sequence of modules connected by boundary maps whose consecutive composite is zero. It is not a graded collection alone: the square-zero boundary law is constitutive."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/52322b1d818875bf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "the GMN left-contraction key `lcon`"@en .

