<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/55c88b10a7baf15e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — gts / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/55eef419c18b6b22>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "operator codomain"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/563b732d474a34b0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Do not use the constraint to infer that a consequent semantically entails its antecedent."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/56529ca8e3a279c9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A Bayesian inference result: the family of result objects whose semantics rest on a posterior obtained by updating a prior with a likelihood — a posterior distribution, a credible interval, a Bayes factor, a posterior probability, and the operational MCMC diagnostics. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject and one of the two inference-paradigm result families, held owl:disjointWith math:FrequentistResult so a single result is never read as both Bayesian and frequentist. The paradigm axis is a PARTIAL classification: only paradigm-exclusive kinds are placed under it, so a paradigm-neutral object (a math:Estimate, a math:Residual) is left free of either family rather than forced into one."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5654525fcacd820c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "vocabulary alignment predicate"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/56568e72d2f7e53d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Implication Consequent Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/565bc60d22aeafda>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A model diagnostic: a first-class evaluation of a fitted model — a residual plot's summary, a Q–Q assessment, a heteroscedasticity or influence measure, a goodness-of-fit statistic. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject that names the math:FittedModel it evaluates through math:diagnosticFor and the diagnostic method it applies through math:diagnosticMethod, so 'what was checked, on which fit, by which method' is queryable rather than folded into a plot's caption. A diagnostic anchored to neither its fitted model nor its method is ill-formed (math:UnanchoredDiagnostic)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/56a3b507d1bb82b6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "unbinding key"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/56c607ee4374e379>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "provenance-honesty floor — Exemplified"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/56dbd21babe206fc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A calculated record that names two distinct Clifford generators and verifies that reversing their geometric-product order negates the result."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/56f464f73e649156>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Clifford involution that negates odd-grade components and preserves even-grade components."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/57139bbb29fc2490>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "generator index"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/57194a4bcad662f8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "vocabulary preservation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/573028f30ec55841>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The lang:Sense a glossary entry carries — the middle corner of the OntoLex Frege triangle, the entry's lexeme's way of meaning. Functional: one sense per entry. Domain gmeow:GlossaryEntry, range lang:Sense. The sense lang:evokes the entry's gmeow:glossaryConcept, so synonymy is derived (two distinct senses evoking one concept), never a flat sense-to-sense edge. The projection mints the sense from the (gmeow:glossaryTerm, English-source-skeleton) pair and INDEPENDENTLY of target language: two distinct terms sharing one source skeleton (a class and its property twin) mint two distinct senses that both evoke the one concept, while the SAME term's renderings across languages (fr, zh) collapse onto one sense (one way of meaning, many language renderings). The consistency invariant still groups on gmeow:glossaryConcept, not on the sense."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/57c8f5f76d5509eb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Constant monotonicity: f(x) = f(y) for all points x, y of the domain — the function's value never changes. The degenerate limit of both weak sorts. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:constantMapLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), which requires any two of the function's values to be equal."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/57f190d8ab29ad7d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: logic:and to and"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/57f378b78ff0a643>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The information-axis score floor to earn the Exemplified tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/581afc0462e34a7f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "permission wins"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/58602c91521d26cb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "license family"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/586a21d3c76001a2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dependency-closure scope"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/588fa3bd7a61be55>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a representation record to the explicit morphism realizing the representation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/589067855d6761d7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The sidedness of a p-value's alternative and tail: the enumerated value fixing HOW the extremity of the test statistic is measured — one of math:oneSidedAlternative, math:twoSidedAlternative, math:greaterAlternative, math:lessAlternative, math:exactTail, or math:midPTail. A closed value type carried through math:alternativeSidedness; the sidedness is part of what makes a p-value unambiguous, because the same statistic and null yield different values one-tailed, two-tailed, or under a mid-p correction. A value outside the six is not a lawful sidedness and marks the p-value ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/58d27b4a86b0fc45>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Form"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/58e03dcdad6ae2cb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:MeasureEvaluation does not name all three of the measure it evaluates (math:evaluatedMeasure), the measurable subset it evaluates over (math:measuredSubset), and the resulting mass (math:measureResult). An evaluation μ(A) is the mass one named measure assigns one named subset; without the measure, the subset, and the result it does not say which measure, of which subset, gave which value, so it cannot be compared against another evaluation and is ill-formed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5998c9dc34f85768>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection vocabulary — gUFO"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/59c4a30191d0e8e9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the bfo projection vocabulary on the gender slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/59cc60efcc76aa47>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The provenance-honesty-axis score floor to earn the Maximal tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/59d00762cbbac082>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A node with both logic:relation and logic:not violates this constraint because it cannot be both an atom and a negation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/59fb441911ebd1ce>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The short CURIE prefix of a guarded projection vocabulary (e.g. \"sh\", \"gufo\", \"bfo\") — the join key gmeow:ceilingVocabulary uses to bind a ceiling commitment to its vocabulary. It is NOT the namespace IRI (that is gmeow:vocabularyNamespace) and NOT a display label: it is the stable short key the counter and the ceiling ABox both key on."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5a07f0cd958ffcaa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "p-value"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5a09740819835b30>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the dul projection vocabulary on the standpoint slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5a518478c5e53a0e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:methodRemoteSensing: `rmt`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5a74c22fb8084fa3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:CredibleInterval (or math:CredibleRegion) to its posterior mass — a framed math:ProbabilityValue (a 0.95) that is the posterior probability, given prior and data, that the parameter lies within the interval. Domain a credible interval or region, range math:ProbabilityValue (stated in prose). The mass is a POSTERIOR probability over the math:PosteriorDistribution the interval summarizes (math:hasPosterior), never a procedure's coverage; a credible interval naming no credible mass is ill-formed (math:IncompleteCredibleInterval). Its frequentist counterpart is math:confidenceLevel, held strictly apart from it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5a83aa40896735d0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "index"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5a84f4755c41a60f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "watermark"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5abe8fff2a87f080>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "give"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5b45587ffa01cf68>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "absolute spatial position"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5b5fc97b66cffda4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:MetricTensor, math:QuadraticSpace, math:QuadraticForm, or math:CliffordAlgebra to its shared math:MetricSignature (p, q). Range math:MetricSignature (stated in prose). Structured, not an opaque string, so metric and Clifford consumers read the same exact sign convention."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5bae20c4238d2df7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has trademark"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5bae783dee863ee9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "right generator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5bda230898ff007d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The nerve simplicial complex of a family of equal-radius balls, with a simplex for each subfamily having nonempty total intersection. It is not a Vietoris–Rips complex: a common intersection, not merely pairwise proximity, licenses a simplex."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5c2081df49e8d07c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Exempts the GMN dialect-projection sub-target of the projection axis: the GMN projection surface is a separate program and is not yet a landed pipeline projection target. The projection axis still measures every landed projection surface."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5c296f1c83ea4ea7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "spatial region"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5c4497d55d14d7f2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "homograph source"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5c5593f4a7324fab>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "the GMN coboundary-operator key `coboundary`"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5cc98cb118c667b7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Rust symbol whose appearance in the repo makes this exemption STALE — the trigger the staleness gate watches. Once the symbol resolves, the exemption must be removed and the axis built, so an exemption can never become permanent optionality."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5d209bfe8fbab303>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed raise-only measured-score floor for the axisOptimalTesting quality axis on the math slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured score falls below it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5d3b8eb8dd824343>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A first-order differential operator built from Clifford multiplication and a compatible connection on a spinor bundle."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5d6cb1c957ed9f36>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:AnalyticProperty resolves to no defining law — it carries no math:definingLaw edge to a real first-order logic:Formula (math:nonAffinityLaw, math:convexityLaw, math:boundednessLaw) nor to an honest logic:expressivenessBoundary record (math:smoothnessBoundary). A monotonicity or analytic-property claim MUST be backed by a real law or a recorded boundary, never a bare flag; a bare analytic-property token is unauthorable by construction. Enforced by the guarded-existence logic:Constraint math:AnalyticPropertyBackedConstraint (every math:AnalyticProperty requires a math:definingLaw), lowered to a SHACL sh:sparql constraint."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5da0ba9e4fc32ae0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:methodExpertJudgement: `exj`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5dd08e5c1ee330c3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Exterior Product"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5dd83bda7daf6a4a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "trademark"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5dd999679474c67c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The expected curvature or score variance of a parametric likelihood with respect to a declared parameter."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5e01415764accd96>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed raise-only measured-score floor for the axisReasonerDerived quality axis on the math slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured score falls below it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5e238a11bb557f5b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Guarded Implication Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5e5025fea6982ffa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has prohibition"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5e56f5648d05d981>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Prolog projection-surface registry entry — DOCUMENTARY-ONLY, never an enforceable gate. Per Principle 17, Prolog is one of the generated lossy projections logic: enumerates, but Prolog clause syntax is NOT RDF: it cannot be hand-authored as triples inside a TTL slice, so no Prolog construct can ever appear as a real triple predicate or object here. Its gmeow:vocabularyCountKind is \"countKindNonRdfSurface\", which the shared counter resolves to an always-empty enumeration, making its residue structurally 0 by construction rather than by an unenforced policy. gmeow:vocabularyNamespace is a stable documentary marker IRI under the gmeow: authority — not a dereferenceable external vocabulary namespace and never matched against any real triple — chosen precisely because it can never collide with an authored predicate or object. No counter-example fixture claims this vocabulary reds."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5e7ed288b28e57a8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "slice-local scope"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5e8acc3ca2237499>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A sampling weight: the design weight attached to an observation unit — the number of population units it represents under the math:SurveyDesign, the reciprocal of its selection probability adjusted for non-response and calibration. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the weight as a first-class object so a weighted estimate is analyzable as more than a simple mean. A weight is part of the design, never an intrinsic property of the measured value it scales."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5ec505e5b2fadad2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "two-sided"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5ec87bc51d066724>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: gmeow:GmnEnvelope to genv"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5ee33361aa19da09>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a sheaf to a local or global compatible section."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5f00ce6d25b13d61>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed raise-only measured-score floor for the axisProvenanceHonesty quality axis on the math slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured score falls below it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5f072a2b7a89f9bc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A posterior probability: the probability of a hypothesis or a parameter event AFTER the data, P(H | data) — the direct Bayesian answer a frequentist p-value is so often mistaken for. A subclass of math:BayesianResult, one of the paradigm-exclusive Bayesian result kinds held owl:disjointWith math:FrequentistResult; its magnitude is a framed math:ProbabilityValue over a posterior. It is a probability of the hypothesis given the data, the inverse of a p-value's P(data as extreme | null), and the two are never conflated."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5f07ba9befcecb5c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Limit Result"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5f1f09db8b4fc862>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The linkage-axis score floor to earn the Grounded tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5f5a3930bb84a632>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 named-key binding for math:BoundaryOperator: `boundary`, which disambiguates chain boundaries from partial differentiation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5f9e9fb0f38aef4f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The projection-axis score floor to earn the Exemplified tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5fa23d1c50cf7baf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "GMN candidate: exterior product"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5fb699da11feac8c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Simplicial Complex"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5fdfb386dc5a45ea>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "reasoner floor — Exemplified"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5fe326c95c7f249e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "output nerve"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/5ff877e556332fcc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — documentation / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/600745da2a93c2e3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The grounding-axis score floor to earn the Maximal tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/600d38cd504f1b25>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Survey Design"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/60143cdc486acb91>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Slice-Quality Rubric"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/603426415efc58f2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the exact math:RationalValue of the inner product ⟨coexact, harmonic⟩ of its coexact and harmonic components. Orthogonality of the two components makes this value exactly zero, carried as the exact pair 0/1. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/604d57d4418ae2e0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a dynamical or Hamiltonian system to the mathematical space containing its states."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/605b00e75dab2855>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "the GMN Hodge-Laplacian key `hlap`"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/60a082a2f19cb940>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The outcome a math:Limit runs to, carried by a math:LimitResult through math:limitOutcome: one of math:convergesFinitely (the limit exists and is finite), math:divergesToPositiveInfinity (x → a drives f off to +∞), math:divergesToNegativeInfinity (off to −∞), or math:divergesWithoutLimit (no limit exists — the value oscillates or otherwise fails to settle). The outcome is what distinguishes a convergent limit from divergence to either pole or an absent limit, and is required on every math:LimitResult."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/60b1e994a366dc79>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:StatisticalPopulation to the math:SamplingFrame that operationalizes it — the concrete list or procedure standing in for the population. Domain math:StatisticalPopulation, range math:SamplingFrame (stated in prose). The frame is what makes under- and over-coverage first-class: the gap between the population and the frame it names is precisely the coverage the layer can evaluate."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/60bde8cf39887314>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a vector-symbolic operation lacks a required frame component — the math:VectorSpace it composes in, the math:Basis fixing its coordinates, its operand vectors (two or more for a binding or bundling; the bound vector, key, and recovered operand for an unbinding), its capacity descriptor, or its recovery-loss (fidelity) contract. A vector-symbolic operation is defined only relative to a complete, declared frame; a bare binding, bundle, or unbinding whose capacity or recovery-loss contract is implicit is ill-formed, because without the capacity the superposition-crosstalk limit is unstated and without the loss bound the operation cannot claim invertibility — recovery is approximate unless an exact algebra proves otherwise."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/60d855071eb11d83>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a sheaf to one of its local stalk objects."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/614f1169bd87972a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Names the datarange qualifying a cardinality restriction. It is not the base datatype of a logic:Datarange expression; it lowers to owl:onDataRange."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/61515f4b92135c9f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Convexity: the function lies on or below its chords — the midpoint of the graph over any two points is at least as high as the graph at the midpoint of those points. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:convexityLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), authored in the honestly-expressible MIDPOINT-convexity form f((x+y)/2) ≤ (f(x)+f(y))/2: the full λ-chord inequality f(λx+(1−λ)y) ≤ λf(x)+(1−λ)f(y) quantifies over the continuum of weights λ and needs scalar arithmetic on the values, so the midpoint form (reifying the midpoint as an uninterpreted relation, never an invented arithmetic function symbol) is the faithful first-order fragment; the λ-general residue is disclosed, not faked."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/615ab691ace676bc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Coboundary Operator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/619a5aae57458ee5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The tier a threshold pairing gates — the rung the axis earns when its measured score meets the paired floor. It is NOT the floor (that is gmeow:thresholdFloor)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/61a1224cb9f09d29>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The variadic relation used inside a reified logic:Formula to test whether its first term is a member of the remaining finite value-set arguments. The SHACL lowering realizes it as an sh:in list and the procedural SPARQL lowering as FILTER IN; it binds no term and is never interpreted as an RDF membership assertion."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/61ab6e0d7eb51312>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The prose-quality-axis score floor to earn the Maximal tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/61f64ffdc86d63ce>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Grounded"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/61fe0484685f1d45>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An open endpoint: the endpoint is excluded from the interval — the round bracket of (a, …) or (…, b). The case where lower < x (or x < upper) is strict. An unbounded end at a pole (math:PositiveInfinity or math:NegativeInfinity) is always open, because the pole is a limit point of the extended real line, never a member."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6200628d26836379>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Grading"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/624749cb228ebade>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "logic:RelationalCore a logic:ConversionTarget ."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/628bb70e854e60cd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "reference distribution"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/62d13d3c5519b1ec>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Use when reconstructing typed literal terms from their lexical and datatype components."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/631491961436e798>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:StatisticalModel or math:FittedModel to a math:ModelAssumption it posits — normality of errors, homoscedasticity, independence of observations, linearity. Domain a math:StatisticalModel or math:FittedModel, range math:ModelAssumption (stated in prose). Naming assumptions as first-class objects is what makes a model's validity conditions checkable, citable, and reportable-as-violated rather than implicit in the choice of model."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/633992433f9a02aa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Limit to the math:LimitResult recording what it evaluates to — its outcome and, for a finite convergent limit, its value. Domain math:Limit, range math:LimitResult (stated in prose). Optional: a math:Limit may name only its expression, point, and mode and leave the evaluated result unstated; where the result is stated, it is a math:LimitResult, never a bare literal, so the outcome is explicit."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/636a6950ffbf321d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "direct type guard"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/638caef5085d5f0d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A measurable subset: an element of the math:SigmaAlgebra of a math:MeasurableSpace — one of the subsets closed under complement and countable union that the σ-algebra collects, and so the kind of subset a math:Measure can assign mass to. It is the individual argument A of an evaluation μ(A): where a math:MeasurableSpace is the whole ground (X, Σ) a measure acts over, a measurable set is one measurable piece of it, the band or region whose mass a math:MeasureEvaluation reads off. Shared with the probability charter, where a measurable set is an event."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/63dfccdbdd4cfdbd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "rule target"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/645d20fd1799a800>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint record can require exactly one of two predicates without being treated as either operand of the formula it compiles."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/64ad7f166c5f0e7d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "commercialize"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/64cfaf58346a207d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Endpoint Inclusion"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/64d77fcb067a45f8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Boundary Operator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/65210d4fefda13e1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a Hamiltonian system lacks its smooth state space, symplectic form, Hamiltonian function, or generated Hamiltonian flow."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/655493682210040c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a lang:Paraphrase to the produced restatement form. Domain lang:Paraphrase, range lang:Form (stated in prose). The source side is lang:paraphraseOf; keeping both roles explicit makes the form-to-form crossing and its relator mediation queryable without treating the reified paraphrase record as a form."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/656eaa1049b89880>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Canonical extensional equivalence between two class expressions. It is not similarity or close matching; it lowers to owl:equivalentClass only when the selected projection can preserve the claim."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/65845fef711f55b8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "target contrast"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/65891587430780fe>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection vocabulary — Notation3 (documentary-only)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/65af0fece0c80dd0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the exact math:RationalValue of the inner product ⟨exact, harmonic⟩ of its exact and harmonic components. Orthogonality of the two components makes this value exactly zero, carried as the exact pair 0/1. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/65bc01221abd7183>
