    ontolex:writtenRep "piece domain"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6a53a4002ef38b02>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "operation capacity"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6a7bec24f959aa54>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Exempts the multi-format documentation max-info panels sub-metric of the documentation axis: the panels are measured for adoption as they land, and their producer is not yet in-repo."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6aa1858c089c77be>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A variable role: the analytical part a math:StatisticalVariable plays in a model — outcome, predictor, covariate, weight, stratum, cluster, or offset. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the role a variable holds rather than an intrinsic property of the column, so the same measured variable can be an outcome in one model and a predictor in another without changing the data. A variable's role is a first-class object so a model's structure is queryable, never read off a naming convention."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6ac4162af0f88bf4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Hodge decomposition to its harmonic component — the part lying in the kernel of the applicable Hodge Laplacian, orthogonal to both the exact and coexact parts. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:HarmonicComponent (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6ac8776ec163f4de>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The vector-space or module decomposition of an extended Clifford algebra into an embedded base-algebra summand and the new-generator multiple of that summand; it is not an algebra direct sum."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6b44cfb5c3a76efb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "rendition resolution"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6b5d035a3d7f691a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "copyright undetermined"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6bb0e65225a228d0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A derived variable: a math:StatisticalVariable that is the declared result of a math:DataTransformation over other variables, rather than a directly measured column. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject (and, in role, a statistical variable) whose provenance is the transformation that produced it — an expression AST, not an opaque new field — so a log-income or a standardized-score is traceable to its inputs and operation. A derived column with no declared transformation is an unexplained field, not a derivation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6bb91533dff0c225>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A compactification: a structured record embedding an unbounded space in a bounded (compact) one as a dense subset, so the points the original space runs off toward are adjoined as a boundary at infinity. It names FOUR roles — the original unbounded space through math:originalSpace, the embedding/map through math:compactifyingMap, the resulting bounded space through math:compactifiedSpace, and the boundary added at infinity through math:boundaryAtInfinity. It is NOT any one construction — not the one-point (Alexandroff) versus Stone–Čech distinction per se — but the general structured record every such construction instantiates; a compactification missing any of the four roles is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6c59460263ca9c2d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The testing-axis score floor to earn the Grounded tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6c62793ec08ed916>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A formula node with a consequent formula but no antecedent formula violates this constraint."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6c965672e0995c5c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "cancelled"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6caee40e2bc5adb5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Recovery-Loss Contract"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6cbcf9a53105e480>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The English source literal a glossary entry renders — the @x-gmeow-english value the catalog msgid carries. Functional: one source per entry. Domain gmeow:GlossaryEntry, range xsd:string. The consistency invariant groups on the entry's gmeow:glossaryConcept (a sense the projection mints from this source), so one source normally maps to one concept and thus one translation, while a declared homograph splits one source across distinct concepts."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6d05b3fcf191d0e6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis-floor commitment — math / axisMaximalInformation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6d3b51a4c77e8c99>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A canonical logic: class-expression restriction: a constraint over one logic:onProperty together with one or more value or cardinality constraints. OWL's owl:Restriction is a generated dialect form of this construct, not the canonical authoring term."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6d4a3258d7b7859e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Term Carrier Value Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6d5d4ac3d8952877>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 named-key binding for math:CoboundaryOperator: `coboundary`, which disambiguates the cochain operator from other delta notations."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6d91099f6375dbc3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Metric Signature"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6def5b7ddec5b4b3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The estimated minimum number of coordinates needed to describe a dataset or manifold at a declared scale and under a declared estimator."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6e72f6c83cf85ab7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Universal time-bounded existence facility: ontic existence-over-time for any gmeow:Entity, distinct from suppression (a display contract). Every entity may carry creation and destruction events, an existence interval, and supersession links. Revised forward, never deleted (Principle 10). Reuses the events module (gmeow:Event + EventType value vocabulary), the temporal module (TimeInterval / TimeScopedRelation / validFrom / validUntil), and the standpoint module (accordingTo / contested claims). Flat-first, reify on demand."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6ebaa21e9973a444>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The capacity descriptor of a vector-symbolic operation: a first-class mathematical object carrying the exact math:RationalValue bound (through math:capacityBound) on how many representations may be bound or superposed into one vector before recovery degrades below the operation's recovery-loss contract. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject. Capacity is declared, never an implicit consequence of dimension; a vector-symbolic operation missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation), because the point at which superposition crosstalk overwhelms retrieval is then unstated."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6ebc8746cd35ea59>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Sign System"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6ef15efb0b036ad3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Underspecified Compactification"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6ef1ca91c40b5706>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Vector Binding"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/6f0b6d27de043761>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a direct-sum decomposition to one of its explicitly identified summands."@en .

