<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7044fb327b075abd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A cluster: a group of observation units selected together as a primary sampling unit under a multi-stage math:SurveyDesign (a school, a census block, a clinic). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the cluster as a first-class object, so the within-cluster correlation that inflates variance is analyzable rather than ignored. Distinct from a math:Stratum: strata partition the frame for independent sampling, whereas clusters are the units sampled at a stage."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7077b2fb87f280be>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "exact component"@en .

