    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Hamiltonian System"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/711e0cac4b054b80>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The prose-quality sub-axis that flags any saRationale or comment-class rationale literal naming a test artifact (a test function, a .rs or .py path, or a 'Mirrors …' framing) as a category error — a test is evidence that an axiom holds, never the reason why. Advisory only. It is NOT a hard gate and NOT the general prose axis: it targets exactly the test-is-not-a-rationale anti-pattern and offers a strip-clause uplift (SLICE_GUIDE §6.6)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/712df1abd1669784>
