<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/73d579f79f516ea3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A stratum: a mutually exclusive subgroup of a math:SamplingFrame within which sampling is carried out independently under a stratified math:SurveyDesign. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the stratum as a first-class object, so stratified variance estimation is possible rather than a design detail lost to a flat weight. Strata partition the frame; a unit belongs to exactly one, distinct from a math:Cluster, which groups units for multi-stage selection."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/740f538af98bb813>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Intrinsic Dimension"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/74128958e09ff83a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The convergent outcome: the limit exists and is a finite value, carried by the math:LimitResult through math:limitResultValue as a finite numeric literal. The case lim_{x→a} f(x) = L for a finite L."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/748ae39d9be936b0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The binary infix GMN named-key form `ds` for math:DirectSumDecomposition; the circled-plus sign remains display notation because the named key is cheaper under the pinned BPE."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/74ab623c516bfc88>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "trademark mark"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/74edb2365b5a1bf2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The minimum measured score (a decimal in 0.0–1.0) the axis must reach to earn the paired tier. It is NOT a percentage-with-units and NOT the tier rank: it is the normalized floor the primitive's score is compared against."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7535b05df242a8c5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A parameterized family of transformations describing the evolution generated by a vector field or dynamical system."@en .

