<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/759f63edc3006a55>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A declared extension from a base Clifford algebra to one with an additional generator, recording both signatures and the embedding convention."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/75b137a1ae43e0fb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Use when validating canonical RDF formula trees before parsing, canonicalization, or projection."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/75ea5a83771e3d6d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Clifford extension to the Clifford algebra obtained after adjoining the declared generator."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7606eba86cc8b802>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The translation-coverage-axis score floor to earn the Linked tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/76511eba15810f97>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The axis reads the target slice together with its declared dependency closure — enough to resolve inherited terms and cross-slice test placement, but not the whole ontology."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/76696253b5df2662>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "on property"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7694f69e8d61db22>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "provenance-honesty floor — Grounded"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/769c24687af49561>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis-floor commitment — math / axisOptimalTesting"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/76f43a94bd3a324f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "non-increasing"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/770657231cc56754>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Use when validating the ordered pair that encodes material implication."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/77440a082b478387>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Prediction or a math:PredictionInterval to the target it forecasts — the outcome, unit, or future observation the prediction speaks about. Domain a math:Prediction or math:PredictionInterval, range the target object (stated in prose). Naming the target is what keeps a prediction a forecast ABOUT something (a new case's outcome) rather than a bare number, and distinguishes it from an estimate of a parameter."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/775d1a0104e04715>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Model Comparison"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/776391d56d9fe0ac>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A per-tier score floor for this axis — the decimal grade the axis must reach to earn a given tier. Thresholds are DATA, not code: tuning a floor or adding a tier's floor is a slice edit and regenerate, never a Rust change. It is NOT the measured score (that is computed by the primitive) and NOT the tier ladder (that is gmeow:QualityTier)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/77a199a3ce6c56fd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "less"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/77b8ec52782b7dec>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A typed morphological feature-value pair — Number=Plur, Tense=Past — carrying a key drawn from a feature inventory (lang:featureKey, a lang:FeatureKey individual), a value drawn from that inventory (lang:featureValue, a lang:FeatureValue individual), and optionally a layer (lang:featureLayer, as in the UD Number[psor] convention). Morphological content is carried this way, never as an unparsed feature string; the inventory aligns to Universal Dependencies' universal features and extends past them where a language demands it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/77e28f06706289f5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The projection-axis score floor to earn the Grounded tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/77e59e9226c39b15>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "copyright holder"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/780d0bf1665c773a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The prose-quality-axis score floor to earn the Linked tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/785c059e8a403d55>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An information measure of uncertainty in a declared probability distribution, with the logarithm base and units forming part of its frame."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/78c5610a2c83214e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "operator domain"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/78c749191d7c826f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The reasoner-derived-axis score floor to earn the Grounded tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/78df48b1f62538c9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has analytic property"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/78fa47a534d36d61>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The data-quality dimension for maximal linkage — mapping presence at honest rungs, authority links, and correspondence-calculus adoption over a slice's alignment surface."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/79cedda4e69cf812>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "tier rank"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7a2f0f33073132f5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "extension generator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7a3e2382b852519e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "upper inclusion"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7a6dbfa7abe48670>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A statistic: any function of the data — a summary computed from a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix (a sample mean, a variance, a test statistic, an order statistic). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the computed quantity as a first-class object, distinct from the math:Estimator (the procedure) and from the math:Estimand (the target it may estimate). A statistic used as an estimator estimates an estimand; a statistic used as a test statistic drives a hypothesis test — but the object is a function of the data either way, never conflated with the frame it is used in."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7a718595c6d6c005>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has bound"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7ac5c66ea8a072b0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Names the canonical source term or pattern related by a logic:Correspondence. This is an endpoint, not an executable logic:getLeg: a term-level correspondence can name both endpoints while carrying no transaction program. Single-valued when present and paired with exactly one logic:targetEndpoint."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7af532b1bcf077dc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:StatisticalVariable to the math:MissingnessIndicator flagging, per observation unit, whether its value is present or absent. Domain math:StatisticalVariable, range math:MissingnessIndicator (stated in prose). Carrying this indicator is the detectable mark that a variable's values encode absence, which obliges an analysis depending on the variable to declare its math:MissingnessMechanism through math:missingnessMechanism (else math:ImplicitMissingness)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7b070d6b3b608076>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has creation event"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7b1358935bad9232>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The flow generated by a Hamiltonian function through a declared symplectic form."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7b471c12e370c88b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "When logic:antecedent is present, require one resource-valued logic:consequent before constructing Formula::Implies."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7b6296f5a5381af7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "ceiling slice"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7b6f94efb7b63a12>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Information Entropy"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7b7b2126d3aed80a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Cover to one of its math:CoverElement members — a single overlapping set of the covering family. Domain math:Cover, range math:CoverElement (stated in prose). Enumerating the cover elements is what makes a cover deterministic: the family is listed explicitly, not summarized by a resolution and gain."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7b8d8756adc46128>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "next policy"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7bca758792ca6d0a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A cover of a space: a finite family of overlapping sets (its math:CoverElement members, named through math:hasCoverElement) whose union contains the covered space. In a Mapper construction the cover is taken of the filter function's codomain, and the overlaps between adjacent cover elements are what create the edges of the output nerve. The cover is declared and finitely enumerated, never an implicit resolution parameter; a Mapper construction missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7bd50825793bde9d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7bd8cababf6bf1fb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A grapheme: a member character of a script's repertoire — a Latin letter, a Cyrillic letter, a Han character. Declares the script it belongs to through lang:inScript; the owning script lists it through lang:hasGrapheme. A grapheme not in its script's repertoire is ill-formed. Below the morph in the stratification; a repertoire element rather than a sign-system-scoped form."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7be1ba5f64e9fcab>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The kind of monotonic behaviour a function (or a math:FunctionPiece) exhibits over an ordered domain — one of math:strictlyIncreasing, math:strictlyDecreasing, math:nonIncreasing, math:nonDecreasing, or math:constant. An OPEN vocabulary of math:NamedIndividuals (never an owl:oneOf enumeration), so a new monotonic sort joins by minting an individual. Each kind is NOT a bare token: it resolves through math:definingLaw to a real first-order logic:Formula stating what the kind MEANS as an ordering condition on the function's values — math:strictMonotonicityLaw for math:strictlyDecreasing, math:strictIncreaseLaw for math:strictlyIncreasing, and so on — so 'this piece is strictly decreasing' is a quantified statement over the reified real/value signature, not prose. A function names its monotonicity through math:hasMonotonicity."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7be53f1631936e32>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has permission"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7beabb6870a20330>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The non-negative integer dimension requested as the output dimension of a dimensionality-reduction analysis."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7c84546bfc337c8e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Estimate"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7cdc9ed3a3e6a2be>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Statistical Variable"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7d0d270675274961>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "generates flow"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7d38c97b3ec7e724>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The gUFO upper-ontology vocabulary guarded by the projection-vocabulary ratchet — a generated lossy down-projection of the logic: UFO+ foundation (Principle 17; logic: terms are authored standalone, carrying no gUFO parentage, precisely because gUFO is a projection of logic:, not its ground). Its hand-authored constructs are counted by TYPED AXIOM (gmeow:vocabularyCountKind \"countKindTypedAxiom\": distinct triples whose predicate or object IRI falls in gufo:'s namespace). Its declared gmeow:vocabularyAlignmentPredicate set exempts genuine by-reference foundational bridging (Principle 5, \"MORE is always BETTER\") to an EXTERNAL gufo: object from the residue; an internal gmeow-to-gmeow triple under the same predicate stays in the residue as a genuine second source of truth."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7d39f6220e52ffe0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "on datatype"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7d436d95d93b0259>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Glossary term-consistency constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7dc0b7e5a2f89067>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "domain"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7dd33dfb32f3c74d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the epistemics slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7ddfb71930c573be>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The inclusive minimum number of logic:onProperty values belonging to the qualifying logic:onClass or logic:onDataRange. It does not count fillers outside that qualifier; it lowers to owl:minQualifiedCardinality."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7efc9d8fefad959e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Calibration-Sense Conflation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7f5483e4a7c8f3dd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A reified pairing of a tier with the score floor an axis must reach to earn it — the data that turns a measured decimal into a tier grade. It is NOT the axis and NOT the tier: it is the (tier, floor) cell of the rubric's threshold table."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7f760cdba4da211e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A confidence region: the MULTIVARIATE generalization of a math:ConfidenceInterval — a region in parameter space whose frequentist coverage under repeated sampling is a stated proportion, for a vector-valued parameter (a joint region for two or more coefficients). A subclass of math:FrequentistResult, held owl:disjointWith the Bayesian math:CredibleRegion through the paradigm parents. Its coverage is a procedure property, carried through math:confidenceLevel, never a posterior mass; it is the region-valued sibling of the confidence interval, not a credible region."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7fb1554b8f154e10>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The slice's concepts are grounded on the triad (logic/math/lang) and carry their annotation coat — but are not yet richly linked, projected, or exemplified."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7fde8f1227d3edac>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "module base summand"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7fe82538c13395dd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "system device"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7fec875198dfaa73>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The grounding-axis score floor to earn the Grounded tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/7fff26e69ce271eb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a cellular sheaf to the cell complex on which its stalks and restriction maps are indexed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8004ebbf64d380c2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Clifford involution"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8023fc641e944de1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "bound on interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/80392254891725c5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The component of a Hodge decomposition lying in the kernel of the applicable Hodge Laplacian."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/80412f995ab4f4ee>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Maximal Grounding"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/804236ee641bb33f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "right operand"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/80c8f6724c86d429>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates an information measure to the probability distribution it is taken over — the P of an entropy, surprisal, cross entropy, or divergence, or the joint distribution of a mutual information. Domain math:InformationMeasure, range math:Distribution (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8121c558c35b8d2c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A productive Horn or stratified-negation derivation whose logic:head is entailed when every positive logic:body atom holds, every logic:negatedBody atom is absent in its declared closure, and every guard succeeds. It is not a general logic:Formula or an integrity logic:Constraint: constructs outside the rule fragment remain formula trees and are carried as projection residue rather than approximated."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/814ff9ceb6ffe211>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The meaning assignment from `hlap` to the class math:HodgeLaplacian; it deliberately carries no executable grapheme."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8151857e935e9f2f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Prediction"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/816ed48224fb0130>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Estimand to the time or horizon it is defined at — the follow-up time, the landmark, the period over which the outcome and contrast are evaluated. Domain math:Estimand, range the target time (a time point, interval, or horizon, stated in prose). One of the six framing coordinates; a five-year survival difference and a one-year survival difference are different estimands over the same population and contrast."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/81812be61dfd0c06>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the bfo projection vocabulary on the places slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/81a18eb1727ba3bd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed raise-only measured-score floor for the axisMaximalLinkage quality axis on the math slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured score falls below it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/81a9b0337e806af8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "equal to"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/81b4605139886ab1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Reasoner-Derived"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/81f52420193420a3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: logic:Closed to closed"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/825a4b8ef0f36a9a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a gmeow:Glossary translates one term two different ways across batches: two gmeow:GlossaryEntry members sharing one gmeow:glossaryConcept carry two DIFFERENT gmeow:glossaryTranslation values. The terminology is then not consistent — one sense reads back as two divergent renderings — which the functional-dependency invariant (lang:GlossaryTermConsistencyConstraint) forbids. The structural dual of lang:GmnDictionaryAliasCollision: an alias reading back as two terms there, a sense reading back as two translations here. A genuine homograph is NOT this failure — it is projected onto distinct concepts through a lang:DeclaredTerminologyHomograph and so never shares a concept."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/82b42bb10f30c3c7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "converges finitely"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/82cd5832cc56bca4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Clifford anticommutation witness to the generator occurring on the left in its forward product."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/82cf365b5df8352d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Vector Unbinding"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/82f74badb6170eba>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:methodSurvey: `srv`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/83022e298bfbea9e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "is OSI approved"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/831df3a4bcc70d7d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Names the base datatype constrained by a logic:Datarange. It is not the qualifier of a cardinality restriction; it lowers to owl:onDatatype."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/83228c17db026588>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "harmonic component"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/83586a539e075d09>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the boundary operator whose image is the exact component and whose adjoint's image is the coexact component. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:BoundaryOperator (stated in prose). The operator is constitutive of the decomposition — the exact/coexact split is defined relative to it; a decomposition whose boundary operator is omitted or wrongly typed is ill-formed (math:IncompleteHodgeDecomposition)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/837c3fa550d8a0d8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "rule assignee"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/83882daef2df923e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Use for a supported closed-world validation pattern whose canonical expansion is deterministic."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/838cb596af4cfab6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "exact–harmonic inner product"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8442486f372fbaf6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A legal output language for a lowering: every emitted construct must inhabit this target, while anything it cannot express remains explicit flagged residue. It is not a logic:ProjectionTarget, which requests a presentation of an answer; a conversion target instead delimits the IR or dialect into which canonical content may be legalized."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/844b983d1e6febf9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the exact math:RationalValue of the residual norm of its reconstruction — the signal minus the sum of its exact, coexact, and harmonic components. The Hodge decomposition theorem makes this residual exactly zero, carried as the exact pair 0/1, never a decimal; a non-zero residual would witness a failed reconstruction. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/847404348edd224b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The defining law of math:boundedness as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declaring a magnitude bound ε (math:hasBound) that holds on an interval I (math:boundOnInterval), if x lies in I and f takes value v at x, then |v| ≤ ε. math: expresses the law; logic: owns reasoning over it. It is the near-zero plateau's defining VALUE property — a bound on the function's magnitude — distinct from measure dominance (a bound on an integral); the bound is scoped to a region, never global by default."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/847c651bd3703664>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "range"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8485b50aef7a5332>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "qualified cardinality"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/849c7dd4e7a7a5fe>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "capacity bound"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/84dc356e43a1b288>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Existential restriction value: at least one value reached through logic:onProperty belongs to the named class or datarange. It does not constrain every filler; it lowers to owl:someValuesFrom."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/84f0df83a3c4e6f7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Cover Element"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/85f0781bfb493d82>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:FunctionPiece to the math:MathematicalExpression giving its behaviour on its piece-domain — the closed form the function takes on that cell. Domain math:FunctionPiece, range math:MathematicalExpression (stated in prose). At most one; it is optional because a piece may carry qualitative analytic behaviour (math:hasMonotonicity, math:hasBound) instead of an explicit expression, but a piece never carries two conflicting expressions."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8629fac848b4b49e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Do not use this constraint to limit how many operands a selected constructor carries; arity is a separate typed-IR invariant."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/869309781469d9e7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Measurable Set"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/86c1814daff11a7f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Use for each ordered atom argument and each ordered quantifier binding."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/86c740f815923a97>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a graded algebra or module to the explicit grading that decomposes it into homogeneous components."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/86e48fd1fa718fdb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A missingness mechanism: the declared assumption about WHY values are absent that an analysis of incomplete data rests on — recording whether the missingness is MCAR (missing completely at random, absence independent of all data), MAR (missing at random, absence explained by observed data), or MNAR (missing not at random, absence depends on the unobserved value itself). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the mechanism as a first-class object, because the validity of every missing-data method (listwise deletion, multiple imputation, weighting) is conditional on which of MCAR/MAR/MNAR holds. An analysis that depends on a variable encoding absence but declares no mechanism assumes one implicitly, which is ill-formed (math:ImplicitMissingness)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/871f90672438cc63>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Sampling Weight"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/876d673394321aae>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The unary additive-inverse operator (−x): the single-operand negation that flips a value's sign, so a term like x⁻ᵖ is math:Exponentiation applied to x and math:Negation applied to p. Distinct from binary math:Subtraction (which takes two operands); −x is math:Negation(x). Signature ℝ̄ → ℝ̄ over the signed extended real line: it carries the two poles, mapping math:PositiveInfinity to math:NegativeInfinity and back, so −(+∞) = −∞ is stated rather than undefined. OpenMath arith1 unary_minus."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8793f0893f062051>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The guarded projection vocabulary a ceiling commitment caps — the named gmeow:ProjectionVocabulary whose measured ungrounded residue for the committed slice must hold at or below gmeow:ceilingCount. It is NOT the slice (that is gmeow:ceilingSlice) and NOT the ceiling integer (that is gmeow:ceilingCount): it names which guarded surface the ceiling applies to."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/87a21f2f3de09a0d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "vsa operand"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/87bc1d87fa5d5f20>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Assign one contiguous zero-based index and one of the four exclusive term-value predicates."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/87e782a1e0f8f8d2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "missing-data policy"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/87ec4b540d11df8e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The numeric-literal leaf of an expression AST: the expression node denoting a specific math:Number — the 1 in (1 − x), the constant 2 in 2·x, the exponents in a closed form. It carries its value through math:literalValue, which points at a well-formed math:Number (situated in a number system through math:inNumberSystem). Distinct from a bare RDF literal: a math:NumberLiteral is an expression node (a subclass of math:MathematicalExpression), so it can fill a math:slotExpression, whereas a raw literal cannot. Distinct too from a math:MathematicalConstant such as π: a constant is a named exact number object, while a NumberLiteral is a syntactic leaf of a formula that names the number it denotes. See MATHEMATICS-NUMBERS-AND-SETS.md for the number-system grounding its math:literalValue rests on."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8842eed055eeb4a6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "system"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8864de069ee4958d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Require one non-negative integer index on each carrier, then validate the sibling index set as 0 through n minus 1."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/88654f6f3e609b2e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection vocabulary — SHACL (sh)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/888557816c8bdff7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:LimitResult does not name its math:limitOutcome, or carries a math:limitResultValue that disagrees with the declared outcome — a finite (non-pole) value is expected for math:convergesFinitely, math:PositiveInfinity for math:divergesToPositiveInfinity, math:NegativeInfinity for math:divergesToNegativeInfinity, and NO value for math:divergesWithoutLimit. A structured limit result must say which of convergence or the three modes of divergence it is, and its value must agree with that outcome; anything else is ill-formed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/888e43925e18ea33>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the diagnostics slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/88928050658b7b28>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A sheaf on a cell complex assigning a stalk to each cell and a compatible restriction map to each face relation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/88fa37255c4e7591>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "over basis"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/89141a39327c1655>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "registered (®)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/89419c7348562753>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The data-quality dimension for reasoner-derived inference — how much non-trivial entailment a slice's axioms contribute to the closure, measured by the native reasoner rather than by text heuristics."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/894aee8781adb83d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis-floor commitment — math / axisProvenanceHonesty"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/89571fdde19c8722>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Clifford extension to the lower-generator Clifford algebra being embedded."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8986aa173a36c276>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Names the property constrained by a logic:Restriction. It is not an assertion using that property; it lowers to owl:onProperty."@en .

