<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8cefbdb9f6b01093>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The outcome of a limit that does not exist: f neither settles to a finite value nor runs to a single pole — it oscillates (as sin(1/x) at 0) or otherwise fails to converge. The math:LimitResult carries NO math:limitResultValue, because there is no point of ℝ̄ to name; asserting a value here is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8d055aa4e96ab10b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: math:BoundaryOperator to boundary"@en .

