<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8ddbbb81ec24c28e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A guarded, logic:-subsumable lossy-projection surface the projection-vocabulary ratchet caps. Per Principle 17, OWL, SHACL, gUFO, BFO, DOLCE, and the alignment stack (SSSOM, EDOAL, FnO) are generated lossy projections of logic:; each such surface is named here once, ontology-resident and data-driven, rather than hardcoded in Rust. It carries the vocabulary's namespace(s), the logic: core it is subsumed by, how its hand-authored constructs are recognized (gmeow:vocabularyCountKind), the default ceiling a slice with no explicit commitment is held to, its loss-ledger preservation judgment, and the by-reference alignment predicates the ratchet exempts. It is NOT a gmeow:ProjectionCeilingCommitment (that is the per-(slice,vocabulary) ratchet cell) and NOT a gmeow:Slice: it is the guarded vocab itself, the dogfooded guard list the gate's shared counter iterates."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8de9107081522550>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The lower endpoint of a math:Interval — the left end of { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }. Domain math:Interval, range a finite numeric literal (a bounded lower end) or the pole math:NegativeInfinity (an unbounded-below end) (stated in prose). Like math:totalMass and math:extendedRealValue, it is an rdf:Property, not an owl:ObjectProperty or owl:DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal (the finite endpoint) and an individual (a pole): neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the extended-real range without a DL contradiction. Every math:Interval names exactly one; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8e27838022916b20>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "documentation floor — Maximal"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8e30aff1ee841145>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Glossary Entry"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8e4ce08b8d9c1ad5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Path Value Type Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8e53b6c3068e6824>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "glossary source"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8e7d6e71ba5449c7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The graded alternating algebra generated by a vector space under the exterior product. It is not a Clifford algebra: repeated generators vanish and no quadratic-form contribution is retained."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8e96a8dbe71bb6b1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "decomposed object"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8eb73c1b2b9fa9ba>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:Interval does not name both of its endpoints (math:lowerEndpoint and math:upperEndpoint) and both of its endpoint inclusions (math:lowerInclusion and math:upperInclusion). An ordered interval is { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }; without both endpoints and both inclusions, whether [0, 1], [0, 1), or (0, 1) is meant is undetermined. Endpoint inclusion is never silently omitted, so an interval missing an endpoint or an inclusion is ill-formed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8f1a6bfc3eee0ec8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "stream"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8f1e4671cc0fc211>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "over vector space"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8f3103237a48d27d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The loss-ledger preservation judgment a guarded vocabulary's projection from logic: carries — for every currently-guarded vocabulary, logic:SoundUnderApproximation (the projection never overclaims a derivation, but may miss canonical answers logic: itself would derive). It is NOT gmeow:vocabularySubsumedBy (that names the logic: core the vocabulary projects FROM): it names the polarity of guarantee the projection itself makes, joining the ratchet's ontology-resident vocab registry to the same loss-ledger vocabulary every other GMEOW projection uses."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8f4a2777336a697a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Names the math:MeasurableSet a math:MeasureEvaluation assigns mass to — the A in μ(A). Domain math:MeasureEvaluation, range math:MeasurableSet (stated in prose). Every evaluation names exactly one; naming the subset is what lets two evaluations of one measure over different subsets be compared, so an evaluation without its subset is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8f6c771317db65e8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Trademark Status"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8f77f3c5ee2ae30b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis-floor commitment — math / axisReasonerDerived"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8f9617eb7cc41607>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The grade-lowering product selecting the grade-difference component of a Clifford product under a declared contraction convention. It is not a symmetric inner product: operand order and the contraction convention matter."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/8fdc67a1b087ce52>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "target endpoint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/902d3838e1bd1c8a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a vector space, quadratic space, module, or algebra to the explicitly declared field of scalars over which its operations are interpreted."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9086c30301381a89>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The inclusive maximum number of logic:onProperty values permitted by an unqualified logic:Restriction. It does not filter fillers by class or datarange; it lowers to owl:maxCardinality."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/90c2393fa80d60aa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The GMEOW term (class, property, or individual IRI) whose localizable literal a glossary entry renders. Functional: exactly one term per entry. Domain gmeow:GlossaryEntry, range any GMEOW term (deliberately unconstrained — a glossary renders across the whole slice vocabulary, not one rdf:type)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/90d14964ef6705f4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Sample to the math:SamplingFrame it is drawn from — the operational list the units were actually selected out of. Domain math:Sample, range math:SamplingFrame (stated in prose). A sample is drawn from a frame, not directly from a population; this edge is what lets selection bias be traced to the frame rather than assumed away."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/913974dfc12673c3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Grade Involution"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/91c1f724d99c428f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:VectorBinding or math:VectorBundling to one of the operand math:Vectors it composes — a factor of a binding or a summand of a bundle. Domain a math:VectorBinding or math:VectorBundling, range math:Vector (stated in prose). Binding and bundling each take two or more operands; an operation declaring fewer is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation), because a single operand is nothing to combine."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/91c301ba7da2d8d3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a vector-symbolic operation to the math:RecoveryLossContract stating the exact fidelity of retrieval — loss 0/1 when an exact algebra makes it invertible, a stated positive rational otherwise. Domain math:VectorSymbolicOperation, range math:RecoveryLossContract (stated in prose). Recovery is approximate unless an exact algebra proves otherwise, so the contract is constitutive; an operation missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/921338e2c69524cf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A closed nondegenerate differential two-form on a smooth even-dimensional manifold."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9235bf888127dd43>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has section"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/924a515afbe191cf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "glossary translation"@en .

