    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "generator square"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/92eb250681586438>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Names the math:Measure a math:MeasureEvaluation reads — the μ in μ(A). Domain math:MeasureEvaluation, range math:Measure (stated in prose). Every evaluation names exactly one; an evaluation without the measure it evaluates does not say whose mass it reports and is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/93280b790569d259>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Hypothesis"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/93632702745473a2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The documentation-axis score floor to earn the Maximal tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/938f36b0f2f238b4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "translate"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/93e427db6c345bb4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An implication node with an antecedent atom but no consequent formula violates this constraint."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/93e8d895ccf2f36e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A tunable parameter of a closed-form function — one of the A, B, C, p, q that fix a particular curve within the family: relates a math:ClosedFormFunction to a math:VariableDeclaration that is a fitted parameter. Domain math:ClosedFormFunction, range math:VariableDeclaration (stated in prose). Unconstrained cardinality (0..n): a curve may have no parameters or many. A parameter is held fixed while the math:formalArgument varies, which is exactly what distinguishes the argument the function is OF from the parameters it is tuned BY; both enter the math:definingExpression as math:VariableExpression leaves."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/93f8b055123facae>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "One slice's terminology glossary for one target language: the term-grain view of that slice's translation catalog, gathering a gmeow:GlossaryEntry per localizable literal the slice authors. A glossary is scoped by exactly one gmeow:glossarySlice and exactly one gmeow:glossaryLanguage, and holds zero or more entries through gmeow:glossaryEntry. It is a DERIVED object — projected from the slice's i18n/*.po catalog, never hand-authored — so it can never drift from the catalog that is its one canonical source. Within one glossary the term↔translation relation is a single-valued function per sense: no gmeow:glossaryConcept reads back as two divergent gmeow:glossaryTranslation values (lang:GlossaryTermConsistencyConstraint, the functional-dependency dual of the GMN alias bijection)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9402a2f9931e75bf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Clifford module decomposition to the summand obtained by left multiplication with the new extension generator."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/94057fe8e812a205>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the bfo projection vocabulary on the observations slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9408bb5743f9a67f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the bfo projection vocabulary on the standpoint slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/94411a4799311b48>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "used analysis plan"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/945970be8a334043>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The SHACL vocabulary (sh:) guarded by the projection-vocabulary ratchet — a generated lossy projection of logic: validation obligations (Principle 17). Its hand-authored constructs are counted by STRUCTURAL ROLE (gmeow:vocabularyCountKind \"countKindShape\": typed sh:NodeShape/sh:PropertyShape plus subjects of sh:path/sh:sparql/sh:rule), so an anonymous nested sh:property block in module.ttl is caught, not only a typed top-level shape in shapes.ttl. It carries no by-reference alignment predicate: a SHACL construct either carries a RESOLVABLE logic:formalizes/logic:grounds back-ref (grounded, excluded from the residue) or is counted in full."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/946f24ba2a917e9e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for logic:exists: `ex`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/94dbab54559d8a2e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed raise-only measured-score floor for the axisMaximalInformation quality axis on the math slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured score falls below it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/94fec56ab9b79ec8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "permissive"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/95206a9d519beccf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "GMN candidate: boundary operator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/953cce28dbf21122>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Basis Blade"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/954c2a21b09b9fa1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has duty"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/956cbdb2e2413df5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An estimator: the estimation PROCEDURE — a rule that is a function of the data (ordinary least squares, maximum likelihood, the method of moments, an inverse-probability-weighted estimator) — held strictly apart from the estimate it produces and the estimand it targets. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; an estimate names the estimator that produced it through math:estimator, so a produced value is never a bare number without the procedure that computed it. The estimator is the map from data to a value; the math:Estimate is one output of applying it, and the math:Estimand is the quantity it aims at — three distinct objects, never collapsed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/95c85a7d3b513b86>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "threshold tier"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/95c8ab465c547681>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "greater than"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/95edd9d115330f4b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The degree-plus-one operation on a cochain complex, dual to a boundary operator, whose square is zero. It is not an arbitrary delta operator: the cochain grading and square-zero law are required."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/95f1b64e77e7c1fa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:AnalysisPlan to its version — the identifier fixing WHICH revision of the pre-specified plan a result followed. Domain math:AnalysisPlan, range a version literal (a SemVer-like string or release label) or a version object (stated in prose). It is an rdf:Property, not an owl:ObjectProperty or owl:DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal and an individual: neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the version without a DL contradiction (mirroring math:totalMass). Naming the version is what distinguishes a plan followed pre-registration from a later-amended one, so pre-registered versus post-hoc is data."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/95f81fc4aab0baf7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "asset version"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/95fad664446b4e83>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "score parameter"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/960830857f70cf8d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "maximum cardinality"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/96138faf07b397b2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Do not place two value kinds on one carrier or infer its position from Turtle serialization order."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9624a4c53cab3e3f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the inhabitation slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9629669e9b903243>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "One IRI namespace under which a guarded vocabulary's hand-authored constructs are recognized — NON-functional, because a vocabulary may be authored under aliased namespaces (DOLCE's canonical dul: namespace is one such alias set). A candidate triple's predicate or object IRI counts toward the vocabulary if it starts with ANY asserted gmeow:vocabularyNamespace. It is NOT the short prefix (that is gmeow:vocabularyPrefix): it is the full IRI stem the counter matches against."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9636135b22ba71de>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:HypothesisTest or a math:PValue to the math:NullHypothesis it presumes. Domain a math:HypothesisTest or math:PValue, range math:NullHypothesis (stated in prose). The tested default H0 a p-value is computed under; a p-value naming no null hypothesis is ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/968f446aba1afe7a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "testing floor — Grounded"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/96e48f19e824a254>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A sign system: the system of signs a form belongs to — a natural language (English), a formal language (Turtle, GTS), a notation (IPA), a gestural language (a signed language), or a tactile system (Braille). A first-class individual, never a subclass ladder and never a bare tag: it is distinguished by a lang:SignSystemKind (through lang:signSystemKind) and a lang:Modality (through lang:modality), and it may align to a BCP-47 tag, an ISO 639 code, a Wikidata QID, or a MIME type — but the GMEOW term remains the local source of truth and external identifiers name alignments, not identity. Every lang:Form names exactly one through lang:inSignSystem."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9705204f6e03a6d9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The act of assigning meaning to a form — a gmeow:Activity with an agent or method (a person, an NLP engine, a compositional rule run), inputs (the form through lang:interpretedForm, the context, an anchor through lang:anchorsIndexical where deixis needs resolving), and provenance. Its results are lang:Reading objects through lang:producedReading. This is the process of the observation spine's process/result/claim separation, and it is NEVER typed as a gmeow:Observation: the act is disjoint from the claim about its readings."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/971ed2f07fd322a1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "state space"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/975ced5659c8e173>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "no copyright — other known legal restrictions"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/97ad99933966de5c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Clifford Algebra"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/97c842cc7edd2db2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "recipient"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/97f8e131d014efb3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: logic:exists to ex"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/98107736017ba917>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The axis for the quality of human-facing prose: definitions that state boundaries (the three-NOTs bar), examples that are worked triples, substantive non-template usage advice, and rationales that explain why. It carries the provenance-honesty sub-dimension. It is NOT information presence (the information axis) — this judges how well the present strings read (SLICE_GUIDE §6.2/§6.6/§6.7)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/98b2f25f124819fa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The data-quality dimension for the quality of human-facing prose — boundary-stating definitions, worked examples, substantive non-template usage advice, and rationales that state the reason (SLICE_GUIDE §6.2/§6.6/§6.7)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/98da3bf6cc2c5624>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Function Ontology (fno:) vocabulary guarded by the projection-vocabulary ratchet — a generated lossy projection of logic: (Principle 17), part of the alignment stack alongside EDOAL and SSSOM. Its hand-authored constructs are counted by TYPED AXIOM (gmeow:vocabularyCountKind \"countKindTypedAxiom\": distinct triples whose predicate or object IRI falls in fno:'s namespace). The intentional carve-out path dsl/mappings/transforms.fno.ttl is the one hand-authored FnO catalog the shared counter still scans and measures like any other slice-owned surface — it is not a scanning exemption, only an authoring one. Its declared gmeow:vocabularyAlignmentPredicate set exempts genuine by-reference bridging to an EXTERNAL fno: object from the residue."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/98eb9a354b2c314a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The boolean result of an exact round trip through a declared Clifford extension split and join."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/98ebe6f3be73e69f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Reconstruction Map"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/98f6ecc9e7620a35>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis context scope"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9919735d924664d2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The expected negative log likelihood assigned by one declared distribution to outcomes drawn from another."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/995f1a54850373f6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Strictly increasing monotonicity: x < y entails f(x) < f(y) for all points x, y of the domain. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:strictIncreaseLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), the order-preserving mirror of math:strictMonotonicityLaw."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9978a1e947d97c0b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:ModelDiagnostic does not anchor itself to what it evaluates and how — it names no math:FittedModel through math:diagnosticFor, or no method through math:diagnosticMethod. A diagnostic is an evaluation OF a fit BY a method; missing either its fitted model or its method, it is a floating number rather than a checked property of a model, and is ill-formed. Primary gate: the SHACL-Core requirement (math:UnanchoredDiagnosticShape) that a diagnostic name both its fitted model and its diagnostic method."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/99cce35dfba921a0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "existence interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/99ffa13c3c7eb2eb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Composed Form"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9a2e6497207f9e3f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:GmnEnvelope: `genv`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9a6f84bbb50259e1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An orthogonal decomposition of a chain, cochain, or flow into exact, coexact, and harmonic components under declared inner products."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9a760c645f478b3a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A missing-value code: the sentinel a math:StatisticalVariable uses to encode an absent value (a coded NA, a −99, an empty cell), named as a first-class object rather than left as a magic number that a naive analysis would treat as data. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; a variable that references a missing-value code declares that its values encode absence, which is what obliges it to name the math:MissingnessMechanism an analysis depending on it rests on (else math:ImplicitMissingness)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9a80b6297065b875>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The unit in which an information measure's magnitude is expressed, paired with its logarithm base — the bit (base 2), the nat (base e), or the hartley (base 10). The three canonical units are the named individuals math:bit, math:nat, and math:hartley."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9a9cda3e2b2d2ab1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Isomap Reduction"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9b0d388b0680ddec>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a vector-symbolic operation to the math:VectorSpace it composes distributed representations in — the ambient space whose vectors are bound, bundled, or unbound. Domain math:VectorSymbolicOperation, range math:VectorSpace (stated in prose). The space is part of the operation's frame, never implicit; an operation missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9ba10490b2195f78>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Stratum"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9bd048a7e3d6e474>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "uses initialization"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9c4be55b5b9dfded>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix to a math:StatisticalVariable it records — a column of the data, as a first-class object carrying its role, scale, unit policy, and missing-value encoding. Domain a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix, range math:StatisticalVariable (stated in prose). A variable is never a bare column name; this edge names the object that carries its analytical structure."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9c4cbca1f76ccd51>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:modalForceActual: `act`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9c77558cb0962ea9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "acquire license page"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9c8c68fdc60ce8c9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "exactly one"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9ca415c178f1eaa4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "display"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9cf68d7bfef0ded3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Cross Entropy"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9d078cc73687e19e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A composed form: a phrase, clause, sentence, paragraph, section, or text as a tree over indexed slots. Declares its level through lang:compositionLevel, its constituents through lang:formSlot, and its head where headedness is analyzed through lang:formHead. Constituent order is carried by lang:FormSlot individuals with integer lang:slotIndex, never by RDF list ordering — two encodings of one form must be one form. Code-switching is compositional: the composed form belongs to its matrix system while embedded constituents carry their own."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9d3983f11e85b3fc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Constraint Operator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9d3afbface97f742>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "linkage floor — Maximal"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9d477241f9458b65>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Formula Constructor Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9d59164c1c776a44>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The data-quality dimension for rationale provenance honesty — whether a rationale states the ontological reason an axiom holds rather than naming a test artifact as its justification. A test is evidence that an axiom holds, never the reason why, so a test-naming rationale is a category error the advisor flags (SLICE_GUIDE §6.6)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9d5e435c27ee76fc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Sheaf Stalk"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9d6dc4748f10c7e6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "GMN candidate: grade projection"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9dc1040283ffbc1e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Boundedness on an interval: the function's absolute value stays within a declared bound ε over a declared interval — the near-zero plateau's defining VALUE property, |f(x)| ≤ ε for every x in the interval. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:boundednessLaw (rdfs:seeAlso). It is the VALUE property (a bound on the function's magnitude), distinct from measure dominance (a bound on an integral); the bound ε is named through math:hasBound and the interval it holds on through math:boundOnInterval."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9e0dec5f68366644>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The structured evaluation μ(A) of a measure on a named measurable subset, reified as a first-class object: it names the measure through math:evaluatedMeasure, the subset through math:measuredSubset (a math:MeasurableSet), and the resulting mass through math:measureResult (a finite non-negative number or math:PositiveInfinity, NEVER math:NegativeInfinity — a measure is non-negative). It is NOT the whole-space math:totalMass, which is the measure of the ENTIRE space μ(X): a measure evaluation is the measure of a NAMED subset A ⊆ X, so distinct subsets of one measure can be evaluated and compared side by side — the Lebesgue mass of a two-ball μ(B²) against that of a three-ball μ(B³), or the probability of one event against another. Naming all three of measure, subset, and result is what makes μ(A) a queryable datum rather than a display string; an evaluation missing any of the three is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9e0f59eee8e9b2d8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis-floor commitment — math / axisMaximalProjection"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9e2f8ded00e1b955>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Hamiltonian Function"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9ea1be1fec2483d9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The axis for maximal linkage with explicit correspondence-calculus adoption: mapping presence and rung honesty (exactMatch vs closeMatch, the five axes kept apart), live authority links, SKOS lift, and the fraction of the alignment surface routed through the correspondence calculus with an executed law discharge and a loss-ledger judgment. It is NOT projection (that measures output surfaces) — this measures the honesty and calculus-adoption of the links themselves (Principle 17)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9ee4425188cec457>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when one resource is typed BOTH a math:ConfidenceInterval and a math:CredibleInterval — frequentist coverage under a sampling procedure conflated with Bayesian posterior mass. They share the word 'interval' and nothing else: a confidence interval's level is a property of the procedure, a credible interval's mass is a posterior probability, and the two are held owl:disjointWith through their paradigm parents (math:ConfidenceInterval ⊑ math:FrequentistResult, math:CredibleInterval ⊑ math:BayesianResult, math:FrequentistResult owl:disjointWith math:BayesianResult). The disjointness is thus ENTAILED rather than directly asserted; the native DL coherence gate forces any individual typed both to owl:Nothing, and the paired SHACL shape (math:IntervalKindConflationShape) surfaces the same conflation as a finding."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9effc32bd2b91a34>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Missingness Mechanism"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9f248971daae8ef8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "coexact component"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9f633414d7539e57>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The positive integer position of a Clifford generator in the algebra's declared ordered basis."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9f75fd83d9afb900>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Linked"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9f8afa6a4dfa5567>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates an information measure to the exact math:RationalValue of its computed magnitude in its declared unit — carried as an exact numerator/denominator pair, never a decimal, so a reference calculation such as the Shannon entropy of a uniform two-outcome distribution is recorded as exactly 1/1 bit. Domain math:InformationMeasure, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9f9c569d40a51882>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Exact Component"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9fafee2ce34a8930>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Axis Threshold"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9fbdb5cc0ffd9bbc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has piece"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9fc1af6a5cbf8ec2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "reflexive property"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/9fdf33a273841ae0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — temporal / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a077157c2f5d8f00>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 named-key binding for math:Reversion: `rev`, which distinguishes the Clifford involution from other tilde operators."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a080a39e8fca05e4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "GMN dictionary (version 3)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a0a5639f3cc39714>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "boundary at infinity"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a0a94becbb0c7d84>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The upper endpoint of a math:Interval — the right end of { x ∈ ℝ̄ | lower ⋚ x ⋚ upper }. Domain math:Interval, range a finite numeric literal (a bounded upper end) or the pole math:PositiveInfinity (an unbounded-above end) (stated in prose). Like math:totalMass and math:extendedRealValue, it is an rdf:Property, not an owl:ObjectProperty or owl:DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal (the finite endpoint) and an individual (a pole): neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the extended-real range without a DL contradiction. Every math:Interval names exactly one; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a0ae6f5e9f9bcb1d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The declared logarithm base that fixes the scale of an information measure — base 2 (bits), base e (nats), or base 10 (hartleys). The base is a frame component of every information measure, never an implicit default; the three canonical bases are the named individuals math:logBaseTwo, math:logBaseE, and math:logBaseTen."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a0db2bc916e47eac>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Non-decreasing (weakly increasing) monotonicity: x < y entails f(x) ≤ f(y) for all points x, y of the domain — the function never falls. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:monotoneNonDecreaseLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), the non-strict counterpart of math:strictIncreaseLaw."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a0fee29ab2e5af0d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — sensory-environment / bfo"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a15a6dc6b6838b4d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Notation3 (N3) projection-surface registry entry — DOCUMENTARY-ONLY, never an enforceable gate. Per Principle 17, N3 is one of the generated lossy projections logic: enumerates, but N3's log:-rule surface (formulae, {}-quoted graphs, N3 built-ins) is NOT plain RDF triples: it cannot be hand-authored inside a TTL slice's triple surface, so no N3-rule construct can ever appear as a real triple predicate or object here. Its gmeow:vocabularyCountKind is \"countKindNonRdfSurface\", which the shared counter resolves to an always-empty enumeration, making its residue structurally 0 by construction rather than by an unenforced policy. gmeow:vocabularyNamespace is a stable documentary marker IRI under the gmeow: authority — not a dereferenceable external vocabulary namespace and never matched against any real triple — chosen precisely because it can never collide with an authored predicate or object. No counter-example fixture claims this vocabulary reds."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a1652ec5e605d009>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The lang:TranslationUnit carrying the law-spine of a glossary entry's crossing — the attachment point of the entry's logic:Correspondence, its logic:preservationKind, and any lang:translationGap or logic:mnemomorphic residue. Functional: one unit per entry. Domain gmeow:GlossaryEntry, range lang:TranslationUnit. The glossary reuses the translation corpus's honest preservation judgment rather than minting a second grade."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a16802ac58a77578>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "prohibition wins"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a16ebeb90a235d44>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The defining law of math:nonDecreasing as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared non-decreasing, if x < y and f takes value u at x and v at y, then u ≤ v — the function never falls. The non-strict counterpart of math:strictIncreaseLaw."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a17e205dfb1c40d1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The slice a projection-ceiling commitment is committed against — the named slice whose measured ungrounded residue for gmeow:ceilingVocabulary the ceiling guards. It is NOT the vocabulary (that is gmeow:ceilingVocabulary) and NOT the count (that is gmeow:ceilingCount): it is the subject slice the ratchet cell pins, the direct counterpart of gmeow:floorSlice."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a191236668837222>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "LogicalConstraint member-count constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a199ad508ea0620c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A meaning assignment as a reified record — the Peircean triad made structural (sign, object, and the interpreting context that connects them), never a bare triple from form to target. Reification is what makes disagreement, revision, and ambiguity representable. Every denotation names its form (lang:denotedForm, a non-surface form), its kind (lang:denotationKind), its target (lang:denotationTarget), and its context (lang:denotationContext); lang:viaSense routes it through a sense where the head lexeme is ambiguous. Disjoint from lang:Form and lang:Sense — the reference corner of the Frege triangle is not a form and not a sense."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a1ba431ffc90848f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — pipeline / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a1c1c63df74165fc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Links an entity to the event that ended its existence — the general form of death (person), dissolution (organization), destruction (place), or retirement (frame, software). Non-functional: competing standpoint-indexed destruction claims coexist. A Person's death event is ALSO typed gmeow:eventTypeDeath. Suppression (gmeow:displayable false) is a display contract; destruction is an ontic fact — the entity is retained, merely marked as no longer extant."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a1e8bc97cd750418>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The structured result of a math:Limit — what the limit evaluates to: its outcome through math:limitOutcome (one of math:convergesFinitely, math:divergesToPositiveInfinity, math:divergesToNegativeInfinity, or math:divergesWithoutLimit) and, for a finite convergent limit, its value through math:limitResultValue. It is NOT the limit expression itself (the math:Limit binding lim_{x→a} f(x), which names math:limitOf and math:limitPoint) — it is the evaluated result that limit runs to. A convergent result carries a finite value; a result diverging to a pole names that pole (math:PositiveInfinity or math:NegativeInfinity) as its value; a result diverging without a limit (an oscillating or otherwise non-existent limit) carries no value at all. A result missing its outcome is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedLimitResult), as is one whose value disagrees with the declared outcome."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a203a6ebbe741e87>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An ordinal grade on the slice-quality ladder — the bounded lattice of maturity a slice can reach. An open value vocabulary of individuals (never subclasses): new tiers are minted as individuals with a fresh gmeow:tierRank. It is NOT a physical quality kind, NOT the coarse gmeow:sliceTier (core/grounding/extension placement), and NOT a per-axis dimension — it is the rung a slice occupies after its per-axis grades are combined by the lattice meet."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a21d410598899c62>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: lang:MorphemeBoundary to mb"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a2499fe9a51fd14d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Left Contraction"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a2739161de5ad801>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Universal restriction value: every value reached through logic:onProperty belongs to the named class or datarange. It does not assert that any filler exists; it lowers to owl:allValuesFrom."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a27f83b11edba686>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A function assigning a scalar to each point of its declared domain."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a2d5b65805b4c9a9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "is accessible for free"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a382a2a2e6472f76>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "base algebra"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a3aaa1d8cb45bf60>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a divergence or cross entropy to its reference (second) distribution Q — the model distribution against which the primary distribution P is scored. Domain math:InformationMeasure, range math:Distribution (stated in prose). The direction P→Q is fixed, so a Kullback–Leibler divergence is not symmetric."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a3e777ca2db48743>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection vocabulary — Datalog (documentary-only)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a42baf486d0cb88f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Effect Size"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a452cb47623da638>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A closed-world integrity constraint: a gmeow:LogicalConstraint combines at least two gmeow:logicConstraintMember constraints."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a4946b1352d89425>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: logic:or to or"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a4aaad2db7b73c50>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The associative Clifford product combining inner and exterior contributions according to the declared quadratic form. It is not the scalar product or exterior product alone."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a4b2de7176da0748>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Hodge boundary operator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a4c0dcf7e1cdacb5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Incomplete Clifford Algebra"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a4c337cb63d96d50>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "superseded by"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a4e0de8a629ec51e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "alternative sidedness"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a5038e89fca8c7af>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A group representation whose kernel is trivial, so distinct represented group elements induce distinct transformations."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a507220ee4805131>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A vector-symbolic operation superposing several representations into a similarity-preserving aggregate."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a51f9a74341f5055>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The composition of grade involution and reversion in a Clifford algebra. It is not reversion or grade involution alone."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a59402512de1a4d6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 named-key binding for math:LeftContraction: `lcon`, cheaper than the fragmented contraction display sign."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a59680a04d6abdee>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "cardinality"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a6a625ebd96e8ee1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A metric space (X, d): a set X together with a distance function d that is non-negative, zero exactly on the diagonal, symmetric, and satisfies the triangle inequality. Every metric space induces a topology (the metric balls form a basis), so it is a subclass of math:TopologicalSpace, but the distance function is constitutive and not recoverable from the topology alone. It is the source over which a Mapper construction's filter function and clustering rule are defined; a point cloud sampled with a declared metric is a metric space."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a6aa9d0a074b26de>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "GMN candidate: direct sum"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a6b257e4e81c013c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a gmeow:Glossary to one of its term-grain renderings. Domain gmeow:Glossary, range gmeow:GlossaryEntry. Non-functional: a glossary holds zero or more entries."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a6ee9d98048d67e4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A guard-only relation inside a reified constraint formula selecting direct instances of a class while excluding instances reached only through subclasses. It is not a data-triple relation; the SHACL lowering consumes it to build a subclass-excluding sh:SPARQLTarget SELECT."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a70b033fe3b105cc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Projection Vocabulary"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a7be3245b9015a0d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Credible Interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a7f0269b5401fcd8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A one-sided 'less' alternative: the extremity is measured in the lower tail (the parameter falls below its null value)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a7f9c7c62f87a51e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "convexity (midpoint form): f((x+y)/2) ≤ (f(x)+f(y))/2"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a80d3f8ce1b9fb09>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has limit result"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a86522ce3d323385>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Incomplete Mapper Construction"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a8855a8faeb0d0a9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Analytic Property"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a88ad8ad166a3500>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Do not encode disjunction, strong negation, or an unstratified negative cycle as a Horn rule."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a8ac0035235f90d8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A sequence of real-valued functions derived from persistence intervals that places persistent-homology summaries in a statistical function space. It is not a raw barcode or diagram: it is their function-valued transform."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a8c10d8e002b689d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "trademark status"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a8c450d502716a92>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A one-sided 'greater' alternative: the extremity is measured in the upper tail (the parameter exceeds its null value)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a91e913371fba40c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "not equal to"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a939890de3dab420>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Requires every logic:TermCarrier to carry exactly one term-value kind: IRI, variable, literal, or sequence marker. It does not constrain the carrier's ordinal; logic:termIndex and list-level contiguity are checked independently."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a93bd08c03753d34>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "glossary term"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a98b0c76308e38d7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis producer"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a9b399bdff4d4cc8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Prohibition"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a9b417751a87e6ca>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Glossary"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a9c229f99c6cb100>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The creation event associated with this existence record. Optional: an EntityExistence may record only an interval when the creation event is unknown."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a9c9dc24a8510e8b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "existence creation event"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/a9f3f6dea79a24e5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "copyright year"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/aa00260f6a9f0de0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A measurement scale: the level of measurement a math:StatisticalVariable is recorded on — nominal, ordinal, interval, ratio, count, or compositional. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming which arithmetic and comparisons the values license, so a nominal code is never averaged and a compositional part is never treated as a free real. The scale is a first-class object carried by the variable, so scale-appropriate analysis is checkable rather than assumed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/aa13db09c1bd2058>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Compactification to the resulting bounded (compact) space — the image the embedding lands in together with the adjoined boundary at infinity. Domain math:Compactification, range a math:TopologicalSpace (a math:Interval for a compactified half-line) (stated in prose). Every compactification names exactly one; a compactification without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/aa2d530786925359>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A homogeneous degree-two scalar-valued function on a vector space, with its associated bilinear form determined when the scalar characteristic permits. It is not its associated bilinear form."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/aa66d44147bd1ee0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Information Criterion"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/aac9f93d0a2dcdd9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "strictly increasing"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/aad8fc19a462c36b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — standpoint / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ab0d6c9d4af23bf9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "uninstall"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ab4609e10068d72c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "equivalent class"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/abc56114d154179f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for logic:or: `or`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/abd19fc860aa505b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the standpoint slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/abd91c7a08e76015>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "over distribution"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/abdb778c05f7222f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A statistical variable: a measured or derived quantity recorded across the observation units of a sample — not merely a column name but an object carrying its math:VariableRole, its math:MeasurementScale, its math:UnitPolicy, its missing-value encoding (math:MissingValueCode / math:hasMissingnessIndicator), and, where derived, the math:DataTransformation that produced it. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a math:Sample or math:DatasetMatrix through math:statisticalVariable. A variable whose values encode absence but names no math:MissingnessMechanism an analysis rests on is ill-formed (math:ImplicitMissingness)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ac2b24ada66f5332>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A confidence interval: the frequentist interval estimate whose coverage is a property of the PROCEDURE under repeated sampling — an interval constructed so that, across replications of the study, a stated proportion of such intervals contain the true parameter. A subclass of math:FrequentistResult, so it is held owl:disjointWith the Bayesian math:CredibleInterval THROUGH the paradigm parents (a single node is never both — that conflation is math:IntervalKindConflation). It names its bounds through math:hasIntervalBound and its coverage through math:confidenceLevel (a framed math:ProbabilityValue over the sampling procedure); an interval missing its bounds or its level is ill-formed (math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval). It is NOT a statement of posterior probability that the parameter lies in the interval — that is the credible interval's semantics, which this class must never be read as."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ac37fa6048cc755f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "measured subset"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ac488dd386af9dd4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The annotation predicate whose literal a glossary entry renders (e.g. \"rdfs:label\", \"skos:definition\"), in CURIE form. Functional: one predicate per entry. Domain gmeow:GlossaryEntry, range xsd:string."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ac58712688a9c1c0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "symplectic form"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ac6a3a3460749f94>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Multiparameter Persistence"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/aca13cad96b076cd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A calibration diagnostic: the STATISTICAL sense of calibration — how well a fitted model's predicted probabilities match observed frequencies over held-out data, measured by a reliability curve, a Brier-score decomposition, or an expected-calibration-error binning. A subclass of math:ModelDiagnostic (a calibration diagnostic IS a model diagnostic), so it names the math:FittedModel whose probabilities it checks through math:diagnosticFor and the method it applies through math:diagnosticMethod. It is held owl:disjointWith math:StabilityCalibrationRecord — the TOPOLOGICAL sense, which calibrates a credence against a bottleneck stability bound over a math:PersistenceLifetime: the two share the word 'calibration' and nothing else, one calibrating a model's probabilities against data and the other a credence against a stability guarantee, so a consumer selects on the specific class, never on the shared token. Because both descend from math:MathematicalObject their disjointness is NOT entailed by their parents and is asserted directly; a node typed both is math:CalibrationSenseConflation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/acec0e84dfbfef82>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An authoring descriptor that the logic frontend expands into one canonical logic:Constraint with a reified integrity formula. A constraint-sugar record names a closed validation pattern and its parameters; it is not itself a logic:Formula AST node, so formula constructor checks never mistake validation metadata for an object-level sentence."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/aced3021f5c46a62>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Clifford algebra to one of the homogeneous basis blades induced by its ordered generator basis."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/adfa3a704beb9628>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "defining expression"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ae0530cff64a2f1d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The meaning assignment from `lcon` to the class math:LeftContraction; it deliberately carries no executable grapheme."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ae29db9e9e3d631f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A function given by an explicit closed-form expression in one formal argument over tunable parameters: the general facility for stating a parameterized curve — for example T(x) = A·x⁻ᵖ − B·(1−x)⁻q + C — natively as a math:MathematicalExpression AST rather than as an opaque string. A subclass of math:Function, so it inherits the requirement to declare its math:domain and math:codomain (an unframed one is math:UnframedFunction). It additionally names its body through math:definingExpression (the expression AST) and its abstraction variable's declaration through math:formalArgument, and it distinguishes that formal argument from its fitted parameters, each declared through math:functionParameter — so in T(x) the argument x and the parameters A, B, C, p, q are separate declarations, not conflated. A closed form missing its body or its formal argument is ill-formed (math:UnboundClosedForm). It is a general facility supporting ANY curve, not a hardwired one; a concrete curve such as T(x) is an instance authored elsewhere."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ae50977c0dda49d3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the graphrag slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ae531d0cdea450a3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The identifier of the closed Rust measurement primitive that computes this axis — both the enum key the kernel dispatches on and the symbol the axis-to-producer binding gate checks for existence. It is NOT free advice text and NOT a dimension IRI: it is the one name that binds data to code, so a renamed or removed primitive reds the binding gate rather than silently orphaning the axis (the constitution-gate integrity pattern)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ae9504e94a456ef9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "read"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/aeebfebf8cd68385>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:VectorUnbinding to the composite math:Vector it recovers an operand from — the previously bound representation the unbinding is applied to. Domain math:VectorUnbinding, range math:Vector (stated in prose). The bound vector is part of the unbinding's frame, never implicit; an unbinding missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/af08c4880757d24b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A tolerance interval: an interval that, with a stated confidence, contains at least a stated PROPORTION of the population — the two-parameter uncertainty (a confidence level over a coverage proportion) distinct from both a confidence interval on a parameter and a prediction interval on a single future value. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, deliberately left PARADIGM-NEUTRAL (under neither family) because tolerance intervals are constructed in both paradigms; it names its bounds through math:hasIntervalBound. Held apart from math:PredictionInterval (a single future observation) and math:ConfidenceInterval (a fixed parameter), because a proportion of the population is neither."@en .

