<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b0cf95fc14e2bbeb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Canonical range entailment for a property: using the property entails that its object instantiates the named type or datatype. It is not a closed-world validation constraint; it lowers to rdfs:range."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b0fee8a68f2ba9f5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Select the narrowest sugar subclass, provide its target and pattern parameters, and inspect the compiled logic:Constraint projection."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b12223d3b33680fc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:ConformalCompactification to its conformal rescaling factor Ω — a positive function that multiplies the metric so the unbounded metric distance becomes finite at the boundary while angles are preserved. Domain math:ConformalCompactification, range a positive math:Function or math:Quantity (an individual, never a bare literal — hence an owl:ObjectProperty, not a datatype property) (stated in prose). Every conformal compactification names exactly one; one without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b12536cc294be655>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "retain notice"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b172b5861fbdb90d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "the GMN direct-sum key `ds`"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b1a6c698808da02a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a mathematical analysis activity to the explicit object it analyzes. PCA uses it for a data matrix or subspace; dimensional reduction and persistent homology reuse the same grounding relation for their source object. An analysis whose class requires an input is ill-formed when this edge is absent."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b21608907e2beb4e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Forbidden Pattern Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b2a6433bb501c1fc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Hamiltonian function"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b2b7c09765f0ac31>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for logic:Closed: `closed`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b2bcc19643e99849>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — rights / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b2e35ec1a21aa676>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Interval-Kind Conflation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b2ea979a63808cd4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Experimental Design"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b2fdddf1440a15f0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: necessary modal force to nec"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b319084d15a1c675>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A sampling frame: the operational list or procedure from which a math:Sample is actually drawn — the concrete enumeration standing in for a math:StatisticalPopulation. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject related to the population it operationalizes through math:samplingFrame and to the sample drawn from it through math:sampleOf. Kept distinct from the population it approximates so under-coverage (units in the population but not the frame) and over-coverage are first-class rather than hidden: the frame is what we could reach, the population is who we mean."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b33f5b59a6ba9d4b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "License"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b33fd73cbbfee8a5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Unanchored Diagnostic"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b345a24bebcc85c1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Links a logic:Datarange to the RDF list of datatype-facet restriction records it applies. It is not a list of class restrictions; it lowers to owl:withRestrictions."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b35102aaeb43a527>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Mapper construction to the deterministic math:ClusteringRule applied to the inverse image of each cover element to produce the nerve's vertices — for example single-linkage clustering at a fixed distance threshold. Domain math:MapperConstruction, range math:ClusteringRule (stated in prose). The rule is part of the frame so the node set is reproducible; a construction whose clustering is omitted or left to convention is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b3578f2a6d8f51cf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "inform"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b35ba59cb1a4305e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "is none of"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b386bb7b05679968>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Posterior Probability"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b389ea382c43a4f1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "all values from"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b398bf85e582935a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "is any of"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b3b9e0cd744fb8fe>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The defining law of math:constant as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared constant, if f takes value u at x and v at y, then u = v — its value never changes, regardless of the order of x and y. The degenerate limit of both weak monotonicity sorts, so it carries no order atom."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b3fea61a6daff270>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "glossary concept"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b40f2b8244a36d67>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The ranking weight of this axis — used ONLY to order advice (which weakest axis to fix first), NEVER to compute the roll-up tier. The roll-up is the UNWEIGHTED lattice meet of the axis grades (the weakest axis caps the slice); a weighted meet would be an ad-hoc average and would break the ratchet-is-lattice-order law. It is therefore not a score coefficient — it is an advice priority."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b44be28b683d3d41>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Restriction Map"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b463c57388648103>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "One piece of a math:PiecewiseFunction: a domain restriction paired with the sub-behaviour that holds on it. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a piecewise function through math:hasPiece. It names EXACTLY ONE sub-domain through math:pieceDomain (a math:Interval — the sub-domain the piece governs), and, where the piece has an explicit closed form, its behaviour through math:pieceExpression (a math:MathematicalExpression); a piece whose behaviour is qualitative rather than symbolic carries instead a math:hasMonotonicity or a math:hasBound. A piece that names no math:pieceDomain does not say WHERE it applies and is ill-formed (the exactly-one math:pieceDomain gate). The piece is the case-split cell: the interval says over which points the cell holds, the expression or the qualitative marker says what the function does there."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b47b3b90f534f460>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "target time"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b4b143114402f784>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The alternating graded product, conventionally written with a wedge, that vanishes when a generator is repeated. It is not logical conjunction or the full geometric product."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b4f520eea7adca7d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a decomposition record to the mathematical object decomposed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b50c67a9ecce7197>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The abstract root of the form AST: a form that is meant to be analyzed, denoted, translated, matched, or projected is a structured object, never an opaque string. Every lang:Form names exactly one sign system through lang:inSignSystem — an unsituated form is ill-formed. Its identity is computed over structural content alone (sign system, stratum, features, slot structure with constituent keys) and is independent of encoding, script, casing, and rendering. The strata that specialize it — surface forms, morphemes and morphs, lexemes and word forms, orthographic and syntactic words, composed forms, and covert forms — each have a distinct identity criterion."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b526ca88fdb8336d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Confidence Interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b532a9cd609d8ea8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Sheaf Laplacian"@en .

