<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b771a55be64199b4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Documentation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b775f9dfd272d463>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The audited named-key ruling for the circled-plus notation associated with math:DirectSumDecomposition."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b7ca09531cb7d28e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for logic:forall: `fa`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b8054b36b0d4121d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "denotation of the GMN left-contraction key"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b81f2b6208b04337>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Dirac Operator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b852759b9bafe19b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Frequentist Result"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b89c43b098538864>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A two-sided alternative: the extremity is measured in both tails, so a departure in either direction counts against the null."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b94aa5aa47c43aa6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:PValue to the family of comparisons its multiplicity adjustment is taken over — the set of tests within which its error rate is controlled. Domain math:PValue, range the comparison-family object (stated in prose). The family scopes the adjustment: a correction is only meaningful relative to the family of comparisons it controls the error rate across."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b94ed1d0f7ed0da5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Vietoris–Rips Complex"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b96ceb951a670a62>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the concepts slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b99143885bad67da>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Statistic"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b9c6e1e4e89707e0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Hodge Laplacian"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/b9e4595bcd498d54>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "existence destruction event"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ba40ac95188ba5ee>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "How a guarded vocabulary's hand-authored constructs are recognized in a slice's TTL surface — the exact literal \"countKindShape\" (SHACL, counted by structural role), \"countKindTypedAxiom\" (a typed-axiom projection such as gUFO/BFO/DOLCE/FnO/EDOAL/SSSOM, counted by namespace-matched triples), or \"countKindNonRdfSurface\" (Datalog/Prolog/N3, structurally 0 in TTL — documentary-only, never enforced). These three literals are the closed set the shared counter's Rust dispatch resolves against; an unrecognized literal is a hard fail, not a silent skip."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ba7b7f76a55c1db8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A conformal (Penrose-style) compactification: the specialization whose math:compactifyingMap is angle-preserving (conformal), carrying a math:conformalFactor Ω that rescales the metric so the points at infinity sit at a finite conformal boundary. A subclass of math:Compactification; it additionally names its math:conformalFactor — a conformal compactification missing it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification). This is the correct general home for embedding a math:LorentzianManifold's radial chart's infinity as a finite boundary: the conformal factor sends the unbounded metric distance to a finite rescaled one while preserving the causal (angle) structure the Lorentzian metric carries. The metric and its rescaling stay math-side; a spacetime's Penrose diagram is a downstream physics reading of this math object."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/baceb067f8930a1b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a vector-symbolic operation to the math:VectorSymbolicCapacity descriptor bounding how many representations may be bound or superposed before recovery degrades. Domain math:VectorSymbolicOperation, range math:VectorSymbolicCapacity (stated in prose). The capacity is declared, never an implicit consequence of dimension; an operation missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bb35a3c9f6d2896c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Mutual Information"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bb63ee5ac22f8417>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "cover scheme"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bbdaffb5dfc53528>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Vector-Symbolic Capacity"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bc12a9d5a7fdc24f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Validate every authored formula tree before lowering it; reject a focus node unless exactly one listed constructor predicate is present."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bc31cb4caff1235c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Copyright Status"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bc6a8049d356ca88>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Underspecified Estimate"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bc8704ba1079f7f7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The data-quality dimension for maximal projection — whether a slice's content survives into every projection surface in its best configuration, with loss-ledger entries wherever a projection is lossy (Principles 4/7/17)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bcc51c3689655ff5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "reproduce"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bcedea770ba6fdd7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The exact number of logic:onProperty values required by an unqualified logic:Restriction. It does not filter fillers by class or datarange; it lowers to owl:cardinality."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bceefbea74ebfa74>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "copyright work"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bd09f2012cb42daf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "confidence level"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bd106f7eb57a7e56>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed raise-only measured-score floor for the axisMaximalProjection quality axis on the math slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured score falls below it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bd2469c8ce2c69ad>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Surface Anchor"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bd71958eff13b1b3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Randomization Scheme"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bd8976d3c050acd5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Copyright"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bd94316d3bff7979>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for lang:MorphemeBoundary: `mb`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bdacf347bed7264d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The loss-ledger boundary record backing math:smoothness: smoothness (C^∞ / real-analyticity, 'the function has derivatives of every order') is genuinely second-order — it ∀-quantifies over the INFINITE FAMILY of all derivatives {f, f′, f″, …}, a quantification over an unbounded family of functions that is not first-order axiomatizable. HiLog reflection could reify a single derivative, but 'for all n, the n-th derivative exists' ranges over the whole family, so a first-order witness would be an unsound uninterpreted predicate. Hence smoothness is carried as an honest boundary (logic:expressivenessBoundary logic:SecondOrder, logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported), residue disclosed in the ledger and never silent prose (Principle 17). Contrast its siblings math:nonAffinityLaw, math:convexityLaw, and math:boundednessLaw, which ARE first-order logic:Formula laws, exactly as math:compactnessBoundary contrasts with math:continuityLaw and math:connectednessLaw."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bddc137dbcf9ff5e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "prose floor — Maximal"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bdef9fac929cccf8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The number system an operator's operands are drawn from — the source of its signature. Domain math:ArithmeticOperation, range math:NumberSystem (stated in prose). Every math:ArithmeticOperation names exactly one; an operator without its domain is unframed (math:UnframedOperator). Distinct from math:domain (a function's or relation's source set): math:operatorDomain frames the operator symbol itself, over the number-system tower ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ (and the signed extended real line ℝ̄)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/be186dd2a91e8070>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A rule can derive ex:ancestor(x,z) from ex:parent(x,y) and ex:ancestor(y,z), with its variables bound positively in the body."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/be479e0b669e50fa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An experimental design: the first-class record of how a study's units were structured and assigned — a completely randomized, block, factorial, crossover, or split-plot design. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject; together with the math:RandomizationScheme it names, it records how units were assigned to conditions, so the design is queryable structure rather than a phrase in a methods section. Naming the design as an object is what lets an analysis's validity conditions be checked against the assignment that actually produced the data."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/be50123930ba8480>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "lower inclusion"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/be8d603ae84c7af4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The DOLCE Ultra-Lite (dul:) vocabulary guarded by the projection-vocabulary ratchet — a generated lossy projection of the logic: foundation (Principle 17), adopted by reference as a top-level alignment target rather than vendored (Principle 5). Its hand-authored constructs are counted by TYPED AXIOM (gmeow:vocabularyCountKind \"countKindTypedAxiom\": distinct triples whose predicate or object IRI falls in ANY of its asserted gmeow:vocabularyNamespace values — a Vec because DOLCE may be authored under aliased namespaces). Its declared gmeow:vocabularyAlignmentPredicate set exempts genuine by-reference foundational bridging to an EXTERNAL dul: object from the residue; an internal gmeow-to-gmeow triple under the same predicate stays in the residue."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/be924a6c7087422d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "virtual location"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/be9ac8168be22745>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has part"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/beb77be0b89ea29a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection vocabulary — Function Ontology (fno)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/becf038a49c661bf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "reconstruction residual"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bf0da1f073e605ea>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "the GMN boundary-operator key `boundary`"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bf21ecd44ab9bdea>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A qualitative analytic property a function may bear — non-affinity, convexity, boundedness, smoothness. An OPEN vocabulary of math:NamedIndividuals (never an owl:oneOf enumeration); a function declares one through math:hasAnalyticProperty. Every analytic property MUST resolve through math:definingLaw to a real first-order logic:Formula (math:nonAffinity → math:nonAffinityLaw, math:convexity → math:convexityLaw, math:boundedness → math:boundednessLaw) OR — for a genuinely higher-order property — to an honest logic:expressivenessBoundary record (math:smoothness → math:smoothnessBoundary). A bare analytic-property claim backed by no law and no boundary is ill-formed (math:UnbackedAnalyticProperty): an analytic property is a quantified statement about the function's values, never a flag."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bf3fd2f13178d209>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "prose floor — Linked"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bf496f1bef38add3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A topological-data-analysis activity that covers the range of a filter function, clusters inverse images, and forms their nerve graph or complex. It is not clustering or dimensional reduction alone: the cover and nerve construction are required."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bf4a4c8d647b0c63>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Compactification"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bf5d7a434ce8217e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The component of a Hodge decomposition lying in the image of the adjoint boundary or coboundary operator."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bf639b2f147ced21>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "review policy"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/bfd80a4b8a8f2575>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The Basic Formal Ontology (BFO) vocabulary guarded by the projection-vocabulary ratchet — a generated lossy projection of the logic: foundation (Principle 17), adopted by reference as a top-level alignment target rather than vendored (Principle 5). Its hand-authored constructs are counted by TYPED AXIOM (gmeow:vocabularyCountKind \"countKindTypedAxiom\": distinct triples whose predicate or object IRI falls in bfo:'s OBO namespace). Its declared gmeow:vocabularyAlignmentPredicate set exempts genuine by-reference foundational bridging to an EXTERNAL bfo: object from the residue; an internal gmeow-to-gmeow triple under the same predicate stays in the residue."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c013a1a58027dbc5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "language"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c01d9a192528ba03>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates an information measure to the logarithm base fixing its scale — base 2, base e, or base 10. Domain math:InformationMeasure, range math:LogarithmBase (stated in prose). The base is part of the measure's frame, never an implicit default; a measure missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteInformationMeasure)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c02bac457f22a2fe>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A p-value: P(T ≥ t | H0), the probability — framed by a null or sampling distribution — of a test statistic as or more extreme than the one observed, computed under the null hypothesis. A subclass of math:FrequentistResult; its magnitude is carried through math:pValue as a framed math:ProbabilityValue, never a bare literal. To be unambiguous it carries its test (its math:testStatistic, and/or the math:HypothesisTest whose math:pValue it is), its null hypothesis (math:nullHypothesis), its null distribution (math:nullDistribution), and its tail definition or sidedness (math:tailDefinition / math:alternativeSidedness). A p-value with a null and a statistic but no tail or sidedness is still ambiguous and ill-formed (math:IllFramedPValue), because whether the extremity is one-tailed, two-tailed, or a mid-p correction changes the value."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c06cb82aac59c193>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "purpose"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c07dc4d1f3f0cf07>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The floor tier: the slice exists, is registered, and parses — but carries no measured grounding, linkage, or exemplification. The bottom of the lattice."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c08198c62f416fb7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The English surface form a lang:DeclaredTerminologyHomograph marks as a homograph — the string the glossary-consistency gate exempts. At most one surface per declaration. Domain lang:DeclaredTerminologyHomograph, range xsd:string. Distinct from gmeow:glossarySource (which is entry-scoped and derived): this predicate is authored only on homograph declarations, so the gate's exempt-set read never picks up derived entry literals."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c0a0c4f8735613e1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:ModelDiagnostic (or the math:ModelComparison, math:InformationCriterion, math:CalibrationDiagnostic, and math:CrossValidationResult that specialize the diagnostic role over a fit) to the math:FittedModel it evaluates. Domain a model-evaluation object, range math:FittedModel (stated in prose). It is the anchoring edge that ties an evaluation to the fit it speaks about; a math:ModelDiagnostic naming no fitted model through it is ill-formed (math:UnanchoredDiagnostic). One shared edge for 'the fit this evaluation is about', never a near-synonym per diagnostic kind."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c0cbec51548a382b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Compactification to the embedding taking its original space into the compactified one — a math:Function (a math:CoordinateMap when it coordinatizes), angle-preserving for a math:ConformalCompactification. Domain math:Compactification, range math:Function (stated in prose). Every compactification names exactly one; a compactification without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c0ec85c0bd235340>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "glossary unit"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c11ac7fd49a59682>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — epistemics / sh"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c12d2b21bade3987>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:modalForcePossible: `poss`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c1354eece288f4be>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "UMAP Reduction"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c15d0a252d674a2c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — kernel / bfo"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c18232f26b6c2487>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "conflict strategy"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c189f78c20a53228>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A data transformation: the declared operation that produces a math:DerivedVariable from other variables — a log, a standardization, a recode, a ratio — carried as a math:MathematicalExpression AST rather than an opaque recipe. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject naming the transformation so a derived column's provenance is inspectable structure, never a stringly-typed note. A derived variable whose transformation is not a real expression is not a declared derivation but an unexplained new field."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c1a180a1012df886>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The local value object assigned by a sheaf to a point or cell of its base space."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c2289e681c3d2dd6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a Hodge decomposition lacks a required frame component — the signal it decomposes, its exact, coexact, or harmonic component, its boundary operator, its carrier sheaf, the exact residual witnessing reconstruction, or one of the three exact pairwise-orthogonality inner products. A Hodge decomposition is defined only relative to a complete, declared frame; a bare split whose boundary operator, reconstruction residual, or component orthogonality is implicit is ill-formed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c276ee29b8a13a35>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "metric signature"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c2c579ea34f54811>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A single dimension along which slice quality is measured — grounding, reasoner-derived inference, information, linkage, projection, testing, documentation, prose, translation, and their sub-dimensions. An open value vocabulary of individuals (never subclasses): a new axis is a new individual binding a measurement primitive, not a code fork. It is NOT the Rust primitive itself (that is named by gmeow:axisProducer) and NOT the ISO quality dimension it emits under (that is gmeow:axisDimension)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c35a63a91e0e1b39>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "coexact–harmonic inner product"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c3ea5792c7ee7170>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Estimand to the math:StatisticalPopulation it targets — the population the estimand is defined over, who the quantity being estimated speaks about. Domain math:Estimand, range math:StatisticalPopulation (stated in prose). One of the six coordinates that make an estimand well-posed; without a target population an estimand does not fix who it refers to. Distinct from math:population, which relates an estimate or sample to its population — this frames the estimand itself."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c4829f0670ceafac>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Cluster"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c4a9455d0db4e57e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The logic: property-characteristic marker for inverse functionality: P(a,c) and P(b,c) entail a = b. It is not ordinary functionality, which constrains objects per subject; the OWL projection is owl:InverseFunctionalProperty."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c508fac2e8d65523>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A vector-symbolic operation combining two representations into a representation of their association."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c514114cf526dbff>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the bfo projection vocabulary on the mentation slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c51a0a22cde27db8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "no copyright — non-commercial use only"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c52e458537dad0e5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "threshold floor"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c563b8434fdcbb2e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Axis Context Scope"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c56b101e04fe7f9c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Choice Group Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c5f5d09108af5c79>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Whether an endpoint of a math:Interval is included in or excluded from the interval, carried by each end through math:lowerInclusion and math:upperInclusion: one of math:closedEndpoint (the endpoint is a member — the square bracket of [a, …) or (…, b]) or math:openEndpoint (the endpoint is excluded — the round bracket of (a, …) or (…, b)). The inclusion is what distinguishes [0, 1] from [0, 1) from (0, 1), and is required on both ends of every math:Interval."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c6587e7cdfcc6aa0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "diagnostic method"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c6720eda8215047b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The lexical concept (sense) a glossary entry's source evokes — the sense-aware key the consistency invariant groups on. Functional: one concept per entry. Domain gmeow:GlossaryEntry, range lang:LexicalConcept. The projection mints one concept per source skeleton by default (so synonymous renderings of one term are caught), and DISTINCT concepts for a source declared a lang:DeclaredTerminologyHomograph (so a genuine homograph is not a false positive). Grouping on the concept rather than the raw string is what makes the check sense-aware, the OntoLex-Lemon ontolex:LexicalConcept peer."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c6757d77d5f483a1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A reified record of realizing content as a form: a content object (a lang:Form, a lang:Denotation, a composed form, a document node) rendered into a concrete lang:Form or lang:SurfaceForm under a declared kind and convention. Names the content it renders through lang:renderedContent, the form it produces through lang:renderingForm, its kind through lang:renderingKind (a lang:RenderingKind individual), the convention governing it through lang:renderingConvention, and — where the crossing is judged — a preservation kind through lang:renderingPreservation, which carries a logic:preservationKind rather than a lang: preservation enum. Rendering is the facet layer over a logic:Correspondence whose two sides are content and form; serializing the ontology to Turtle, lifting prose to a docs page, and transliterating a name are all renderings distinguished by kind, never a subclass ladder."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c6761f4a56b1226b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "denotation of the GMN Clifford-reversion key"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c6ba8e196591c4e6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "pending"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c6c67fe2d041473d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — mentation / bfo"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c70dd507b98e3448>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An atom's second argument can be represented by a carrier with logic:termIndex 1 and logic:termVariable 'object'."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c738905abf965a94>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "model assumption"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c73e1c478d26292d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Canonical domain entailment for a property: using the property entails that its subject instantiates the named type. It is not a closed-world validation constraint; it lowers to rdfs:domain."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c769e666dbb7539e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "share alike"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c7767ed2a713482b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Cellular Sheaf"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c7912b5fea01b33a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The provenance-honesty-axis score floor to earn the Exemplified tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c7a3de991bff45c6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "transfer"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c7becc87cc40a23a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Dimensional Reduction"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c7c9d4b845b1f14c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "text to speech"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c81dc8414efb3d66>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The reasoner-derived-axis score floor to earn the Linked tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c87bcbbf48a0bdd0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The non-negative integer that totally orders the tier ladder — a lower rank is a weaker tier, and the lattice meet of a set of tiers is the one with the least rank. It is NOT a score (scores are decimals compared against gmeow:thresholdFloor) and NOT stable across ladders — it only orders tiers within this ladder."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c8a1a260401b0890>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Provenance Honesty"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c8dd86a5a077b1c1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An explicit declaration that one English surface form (lang:homographSource) is a homograph in the terminology — it legitimately evokes two or more DISTINCT lang:LexicalConcepts (lang:homographConcept), each of which may take its own target-language rendering. It is the ontology-resident escape the glossary-consistency gate consults: a source so declared is exempted from the raw-source consistency check (its entries are projected onto distinct concepts), so a genuine homograph is never a false positive. A discrete modelled fact, never a calibrated knob: it costs naming two real concepts, and the exemption is granted only when two or more distinct lang:homographConcept senses are present — a declaration naming fewer than two grants no exemption (it is not a homograph) and the source stays under the consistency check."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c95e40a76d1fa421>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Canonical class subsumption: every instance of the subject type is an instance of the object type. It is not a lexical hierarchy hint; it lowers to rdfs:subClassOf on the OWL/RDFS projection surface."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c9799939a96eb67c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "one of"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/c9942986cb2a216e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "strict monotonic decrease: x < y entails f(x) > f(y)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ca37dddfd0da96d3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Number Literal"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ca3c39941621a2af>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "denotation of the GMN Hodge-Laplacian key"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ca455f3fbe25931f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "documentation floor — Grounded"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ca775065b64955cb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Derived Variable"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ca822749c386b4e4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "less than"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cab5c25126184094>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "copyright notice"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cac2d6af578d4de6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "minimum cardinality"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cad42e65544bbf47>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Registered"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cafa3b5dc9478822>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Links an entity to the entity that replaced it — Constantinople supersededBy Istanbul, the Soviet Union supersededBy the Russian Federation, a deprecated software release supersededBy its successor. Directional, NOT symmetric. The superseded entity is retained (never deleted) and may carry gmeow:displayable false."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cb12853926bc5753>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The data-quality dimension for optimal testing — per-term test reach, correct competency-cell modes, pinned counter-examples, and QA bits placed in their cheapest owning layer (SLICE_GUIDE §9; SLICE_QA)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cb312f209ae2ea44>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The ISO 19157 / DQV quality dimension under which this axis's score is emitted as a gmeow:QualityAssessment observation. It is NOT the axis itself and NOT the Rust primitive: it is the RDF vocabulary the report dogfoods so the assessment graph reuses the shared quality layer rather than a bespoke report schema."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cb847ef86bb11516>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Function (or a math:FunctionPiece) to the math:MonotonicityKind classifying its monotonic behaviour over its ordered domain. Domain math:Function or math:FunctionPiece, range math:MonotonicityKind (stated in prose). The declared, checkable bearer of monotonicity: monotonicity is stated here, and the named kind carries the first-order defining law (math:definingLaw) that fixes its meaning, so a monotonicity claim is always backed by a real logic:Formula, never a flag."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cbcdea93b0ccad17>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The linkage-axis score floor to earn the Linked tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cbd22c6f8a0d2472>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The nerve of a covered, clustered space: the simplicial complex whose vertices are the clusters found in each cover element's inverse image and whose k-simplices record the non-empty intersections of k+1 clusters. It is a subclass of math:SimplicialComplex; a Mapper construction's output nerve is its one-skeleton graph together with any higher simplices from multi-way cluster overlaps. It is the output of the Mapper construction, not the source complex it is computed from."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cbd3565293a29f3a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Unit Policy"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cbd518b3568483f3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The translation-coverage-axis score floor to earn the Maximal tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cbe1fd7a717ee384>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has license"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cbe4b1cc5014d701>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "compactified space"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cc0eb99817145d8e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "evaluated measure"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cc10252770088893>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Bayesian Result"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cc6185e18c1fb54d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "licensed work"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ccf2fbb743ee45ef>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: math:DirectSumDecomposition to ds"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cd1f87a70fcad96b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "strictly decreasing"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cd2a0375696cf16d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The grounding-axis score floor to earn the Exemplified tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cd6bc0757e66714d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Betti Number"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cdb7c2700bd5afc2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Hypothesis Test"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cde78c95c35d1472>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Compactification to the math:BoundaryAtInfinity it adjoins — the ideal points at infinity the original space approaches but never reaches. Domain math:Compactification, range math:BoundaryAtInfinity (stated in prose). Every compactification names exactly one; a compactification without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedCompactification)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cdf41a1e375abcd3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:StatisticalVariable whose values encode absence to the math:MissingnessMechanism (MCAR/MAR/MNAR) an analysis depending on it declares it rests on. Domain math:StatisticalVariable, range math:MissingnessMechanism (stated in prose). This is the declaration whose absence, on a variable carrying a math:hasMissingnessIndicator, is the implicit-missingness conflation the gate catches (math:ImplicitMissingness)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ce4313b77851393e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has destruction event"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ce4eca3c8c6a4cff>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a mathematical analysis activity to an explicit result object it produced; interpretation of that result remains a separate standpoint-indexed claim."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cebc4a7e41bbd330>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An inference run: the executed occurrence of an estimation or inference — the analysis activity that fits a model to data (math:fittedToData), applies an estimator, and produces result objects (a math:Estimate, a p-value) tied back through gmeow:wasGeneratedBy. A subclass of gmeow:Activity: the PROCESS half of the process / result / claim separation, distinct from the math:Estimate result objects it produces and from the gmeow:Observation that holds a claim about them from a vantage. Mirrors how math:IngestRun and math:PCAAnalysis subclass gmeow:Activity; it is held disjoint from gmeow:Observation, so a run typed as its own observation is ill-formed (math:ProcessObservationConflation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cec0a2f625d48035>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Statistical power: 1 − β, the probability that a test correctly rejects the null when a specified alternative holds — the operating characteristic answering 'how likely is this test to detect the effect it is designed for'. A subclass of math:FrequentistResult; a frequentist quantity defined against the sampling behaviour of the test under the alternative, the complement of its math:TypeIIErrorRate."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ceeb501abbf12060>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Interval to the math:EndpointInclusion of its lower end — math:closedEndpoint (the lower endpoint is a member, the square bracket of [a, …) or math:openEndpoint (the lower endpoint is excluded, the round bracket of (a, …). Domain math:Interval, range math:EndpointInclusion (stated in prose). The lower inclusion is required and never silently omitted; an interval without it is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedInterval)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cf000a31daa4fe2c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — gender / bfo"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cf36b138e6b66a3e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The slice-quality tier a slice has opted in to — the sole, ratcheting declaration of the maturity bar the slice's manifest promises to hold (Principle 16). Declared in the slice's manifest.ttl. It is NOT the measured roll-up (that is computed) and NOT gmeow:sliceTier (architectural placement): it is the floor the gate enforces. Undeclared means purely advisory; declared means enforced, and the declaration may only be raised."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cf479f1f3d26c3b5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "credible mass"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cf856c1f35e9840a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Harmonic Component"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cfaaa98ba2545b73>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has basis blade"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cfc4b25d148a5d9a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:ClosedFormFunction does not declare both its math:definingExpression (the body AST) and its math:formalArgument (the abstraction variable's declaration). A closed-form function is an explicit expression in one formal argument; a closed form missing its body or its formal argument does not say what it computes or over which variable, and is ill-formed. Its tunable math:functionParameters are 0..n and unconstrained — only the body and the formal argument are required."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/cfc77034d26ecc50>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The non-negative integer vector-space dimension of a coordinate space, tangent space, algebra carrier, or other explicitly linear mathematical object — distinct from the physical math:hasDimension (an SI dimension). A chart target and tangent space use it for manifold consistency; a Clifford algebra uses it for the exact 2^(p+q) carrier dimension."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d04601be7c29d7cc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Conversion Target"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d08e739b81c12155>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "denotation of the GMN direct-sum key"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d0a3690f0ed25e5b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "representation map"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d0a9e36882af6064>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis-floor commitment — math / axisMaximalGrounding"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d0c9851921493b3f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Mapper construction to the math:NerveComplex it produces — the simplicial complex (its one-skeleton graph plus any higher simplices) whose vertices are the per-cover-element clusters and whose simplices record cluster overlaps. Domain math:MapperConstruction, range math:NerveComplex (stated in prose). The nerve is the declared output of the construction; a construction missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d0da6764658a48c7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "left generator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d0e0064e912c497e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "trade secret"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d0f173d405e3a540>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Clifford algebra to a supported involution such as reversion, grade involution, or Clifford conjugation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d13022b40b9cd1ce>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:ArithmeticOperation does not declare both its math:operatorDomain and its math:operatorCodomain — the number system its operands are drawn from and the system its result lies in. An operator is not a bare glyph; every arithmetic operator carries its signature over the number-system tower, so an operator missing either half of its signature is ill-formed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d1792d718a4da404>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "exemption producer"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d2076bc1ae27d2e6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A dynamical system framed by a symplectic state space and a Hamiltonian function that generates its flow."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d22afcc58b5404df>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Incomplete Hamiltonian System"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d284df24b0dedfb0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "some values from"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d28f7f707ebd50b1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Missing Value Code"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d2b7fb48482d9009>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "translation floor — Grounded"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d2e89944e34e672f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Duty"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d3390b1527e51508>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "alternative hypothesis"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d3555d2676224d16>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A logic:Correspondence owned by one of the three co-foundational grounding slices (logic:, math:, or lang:) and shipped as meta-level correspondence data in graph/correspondence-laws. Unlike an ordinary consumer mapping, every grounding correspondence explicitly declares its logic:morphismClass, logic:morphismKind, and logic:preservationKind, and names both related terms through logic:sourceEndpoint and logic:targetEndpoint. It remains outside object-level closure: external vocabularies are linked by reference and their TBoxes are never silently imported."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d363c9da357b78b5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "modify"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d3704dcd9bc15477>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "subclass of"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d38083b4202c6d85>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the bfo projection vocabulary on the sexuality slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d3bfc761e9e83506>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection floor — Exemplified"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d45ee3d40d925965>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "execute"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d4b4436f2041b1f8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An operation in a declared vector-symbolic architecture that composes or retrieves distributed representations."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d505661ea525c507>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Strictly decreasing monotonicity: x < y entails f(x) > f(y) for all points x, y of the domain. Its defining law is the first-order logic:Formula math:strictMonotonicityLaw (rdfs:seeAlso), so the kind is a real quantified ordering condition on the function's values, not a bare token."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d5117cf7712889ad>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "glossary entry"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d54537c4bd39e79e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:ClusteringRule to the exact math:RationalValue of the distance threshold at which it merges points — the single-linkage cut-off carried as an exact numerator/denominator pair, never a decimal, so the clustering is reproducible. Domain math:ClusteringRule, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d558fa521aa5de4f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "move"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d56127c345740e5c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Use with logic:ImplicationConsequentConstraint to validate both halves of an implication."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d561bfd198e20fa8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Docs-panels exemption"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d57534c7118e30d7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "use"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d57b7ba64dd57ed3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a Mapper construction lacks a required frame component — its source metric space, its filter (lens) function, the cover of the filter codomain, the clustering rule applied inside each cover element's inverse image, or the output nerve complex. A Mapper construction is defined only relative to a complete, declared frame; a bare graph whose filter, cover, or clustering rule is implicit is ill-formed, because without them the node set and edge set are not reproducible."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d59e90f6f00959e6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for logic:Open: `open`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d59f1a0111ece4c9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A multiset of birth–death points summarizing the lifetimes of homological features in a filtration. It is not the filtration or the persistent-homology activity that produced it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d5aef2c4d5a2ba2f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An initialization obtained from eigenvectors of a declared graph, kernel, covariance, or Laplacian operator."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d5cef1270e89240a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "population"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d5dca622c1075a17>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Čech Complex"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d5f7b342dac778c1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Mapper Construction"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d605714c8b36deff>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An ordered slot in an atomic formula's logic:argument list or a quantifier's logic:quantifiedVariable block. It carries exactly one zero-based logic:termIndex and exactly one value kind: logic:termIri, logic:termVariable, logic:termLiteral, or logic:termSequenceMarker. It is not the term value itself; it is the RDF node that preserves the value's kind and position independently of triple order."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d62210ec00229315>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Function (or a math:FunctionPiece) to the bound ε on its magnitude — the value such that |f(x)| ≤ ε holds over the declared interval. Domain math:Function or math:FunctionPiece, range a finite non-negative numeric literal (stated in prose); an owl:DatatypeProperty, because a magnitude bound is always a finite number, never a pole. The bound is the ε of the boundedness law math:boundednessLaw; the interval over which it holds is named through math:boundOnInterval. A near-zero plateau declares a small ε here."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d62a7776a2564e6e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "ensure exclusivity"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d644b06737ea13ba>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "public domain"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d6528b3baf9061c3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Incomplete Credible Interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d6528d167a3e8107>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "diverges to −∞"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d6b52f05cb0ad6bc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The BCP-47 target-language tag a gmeow:Glossary renders into (e.g. \"fr\", \"zh\"). Functional: one glossary is one language. Domain gmeow:Glossary, range xsd:string."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d6f7a8faafeddb1a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "related rights"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d70621470bb83413>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "prose floor — Exemplified"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d73882af1a6ff8bf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "subproperty of"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d73958dc57a9638e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "observation unit"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d762206ee3ef8ad1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A credible region: the MULTIVARIATE generalization of a math:CredibleInterval — a region in parameter space carrying a stated posterior probability mass, for a vector-valued parameter (a joint highest-posterior-density region). A subclass of math:BayesianResult, held owl:disjointWith the frequentist math:ConfidenceRegion through the paradigm parents. Its mass is a posterior probability over the math:PosteriorDistribution it summarizes (math:hasPosterior, math:credibleMass), never a procedure's coverage; it is the region-valued sibling of the credible interval, not a confidence region."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d7a18312c1279c49>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "diverges without a limit"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d812b016b597761e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "piece expression"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d83d4568af9defdc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Missingness Indicator"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d8cd7bea3f236456>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "extended algebra"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d8e095ad4769b29b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "merged-closure scope"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d8e4daf02e9aca22>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The body AST of a function given in closed form: relates a math:Function to the math:MathematicalExpression that is its explicit closed-form body. Domain math:Function, range math:MathematicalExpression (stated in prose). Every math:ClosedFormFunction names exactly one; a closed form without a body does not say what it computes and is ill-formed (math:UnboundClosedForm). The body is a structured expression tree, never a display string — the argument and the parameters enter it as math:VariableExpression leaves resolving to the function's math:formalArgument and math:functionParameters."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d947c6963318ae00>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The axis for whether a slice's content survives into every projection surface in its best configuration — SHACL/ShEx from logic sources, SSSOM/EDOAL/FnO, docs pages — with a loss-ledger entry wherever the projection is lossy. It is NOT linkage (the source alignments) — this measures the derived output surfaces (Principles 4/7/17)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d975654d474aa7bc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Hodge decomposition to the exact math:RationalValue of the inner product ⟨exact, coexact⟩ of its exact and coexact components. Orthogonality of the two components makes this value exactly zero, carried as the exact pair 0/1. Domain math:HodgeDecomposition, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d989c2467812e4dc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Compact sugar for a disjunctive-requiredness constraint (P3): a logic:onClass target and a set of logic:anyOf predicates, at least one of which is required. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) → (∃p1 ∨ … ∨ ∃pn). Frontend-only authoring shortcut."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d98eddff9af503c7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The reasoner-derived-axis score floor to earn the Exemplified tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d9b33b19f4c5c1ae>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The time interval over which an entity exists. Open-ended (no end instant) when the entity is still extant. Non-functional: in a multi-source merge, different sources may give different bounds, and those claims coexist as standpoint-indexed statements. Carries its temporal frame via gmeow:hasTemporalFrame on the TimeInterval (Principle 11)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d9b414a9f966c012>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a reconstructed mathematical object to the representation, projection, or source object it attempts to recover."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d9d2925fd6f767b1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "maximum qualified cardinality"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d9ddce2782c90c5e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Sampling Frame"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d9f23bb5b49d4607>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The mass a math:MeasureEvaluation reads off — the value of μ(A), a finite non-negative number or the extended-real math:PositiveInfinity, NEVER math:NegativeInfinity because a measure is non-negative. Domain math:MeasureEvaluation, range a non-negative numeric literal or math:PositiveInfinity (stated in prose). Like math:totalMass, it is an rdf:Property, not an owl:ObjectProperty or owl:DatatypeProperty, precisely because its range spans both a datatype literal (the finite mass) and an individual (math:PositiveInfinity): neither DL property kind admits both, so the honest RDF supertype carries the extended-real range without a DL contradiction. Every evaluation names exactly one; an evaluation without its result is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation), and a result of math:NegativeInfinity is a non-negativity violation (math:MalformedExtendedReal or math:UnderspecifiedMeasureEvaluation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/d9f75a35dc026d78>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "pseudoscalar square"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/da051e82985afa92>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "relative spatial position"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/da1d1ef4a874d6b9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Grounding Correspondence"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/da1d42a33453cedf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has cover element"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/da4222cb56875887>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "exemption date"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/da46347c9bbb6d04>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The documentation-axis score floor to earn the Linked tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/da52f31c584fca06>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:VectorUnbinding to the math:Vector it produces — the retrieved estimate of the bound operand, exact when an exact algebra makes the binding invertible and a noisy approximation otherwise. Domain math:VectorUnbinding, range math:Vector (stated in prose). The recovered operand is the declared output of the unbinding; an unbinding missing it is ill-formed (math:IncompleteVectorSymbolicOperation)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/da63fc6fa45ceeca>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A function defined by pieces: a math:Function whose behaviour is given not by one closed form but by a family of math:FunctionPiece parts, each a sub-behaviour over its own domain restriction. A subclass of math:Function, so it inherits the requirement to declare its math:domain and math:codomain (an unframed one is math:UnframedFunction); it additionally names one or more pieces through math:hasPiece. A piecewise function declaring NO piece says nothing about what it computes and is ill-formed (math:UnderspecifiedPiecewiseFunction). The pieces partition (or cover) the domain; each piece names the sub-domain it governs through math:pieceDomain and, where it has an explicit form, its behaviour through math:pieceExpression — so the classic split f(x) = {x² for x < 0; e⁻ˣ for x ≥ 0} is data (two pieces over two intervals), not prose. It is not a math:ClosedFormFunction (one expression in one formal argument); it is the case-split generalization, and a piece may carry qualitative analytic behaviour (math:hasMonotonicity, math:hasBound) rather than a full expression."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/da695ce982ec79ab>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A constrained datatype expression: one logic:onDatatype plus a logic:withRestrictions list of facet constraints. It is the canonical form lowered to OWL 2 datatype restrictions when the target can represent them, not a literal value or an unconstrained datatype name."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/db0dccadde1ca29f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Mapper construction to the filter (lens) function that maps its source metric space to a codomain the cover is taken of — a real-valued height, an eccentricity, or a density estimate. Domain math:MapperConstruction, range math:Function (stated in prose). The filter is constitutive: the whole cover/clustering pipeline is pulled back through it, so a construction whose filter function is omitted has no cover to pull back and is ill-formed (math:IncompleteMapperConstruction)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/db4b62b331a4c660>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a representation or structured comparison to the explicit map proved to commute with the declared group actions."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dba04c12a7d56b35>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "provenance-honesty floor — Linked"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dbe7d5cb3684be3d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "measure value"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dbe88ec0420e4503>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "transform"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dbf2d4fea91902cd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The boundary a compactification adjoins at infinity: the ideal points — the conformal boundary — the original unbounded space approaches but never reaches, made a first-class object rather than an informal edge. Named by a math:Compactification through math:boundaryAtInfinity. For a math:ConformalCompactification it is where the math:conformalFactor vanishes; for the radial half-line r ∈ [0, ∞) it is the single ideal point r = +∞."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dc30ddd8d6db9b47>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "rights type"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dc55f4a6f7ed5cb1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when an information measure lacks a required frame component — its probability distribution, its logarithm base, its information unit, a divergence's reference distribution, a Fisher information's likelihood model or score parameter, or a surprisal's outcome. An information measure is defined only relative to a complete, declared frame; a bare uncertainty, divergence, or information token with an implicit distribution, base, or unit is ill-formed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dc893b101cbf8597>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An effect size: the standardized MAGNITUDE of a contrast — a Cohen's d, a correlation, an odds ratio, an R² — that answers 'how big is the effect' rather than 'is it distinguishable from zero'. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, deliberately PARADIGM-NEUTRAL (under neither family) because an effect size is estimated in both paradigms. To be interpretable it identifies THREE things: the comparison it measures the magnitude of through math:effectSizeContrast — the SAME shared math:StatisticalContrast object an estimand targets through math:targetContrast, one modeled contrast, never a near-synonym — the math:MeasurementScale it is expressed on through math:effectSizeScale, and its reference frame through gmeow:hasReferenceFrame (the house frame predicate, the same edge a math:ProbabilityValue is framed by). An effect size missing its contrast, scale, or frame is an uninterpretable bare number (math:UnframedEffectSize)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dd346dda051e41ef>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Cross Node Constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dd38c163ea05c21b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Use when validating ordered argument lists and quantifier binding blocks."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dd5d81d2f9ecd655>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:FunctionPiece to the math:Interval it governs — the sub-domain over which the piece's behaviour holds. Domain math:FunctionPiece, range math:Interval (stated in prose). Each piece names exactly one piece-domain; a piece without it does not say where it applies and is ill-formed. The interval is a fully-formed math:Interval (both endpoints and both inclusions), so a half-open cell [0, 1) is distinguished from the closed cell [0, 1]."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dd8354df0d17ad0b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "testing floor — Linked"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dd9f0f48a33c45e4>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Compact sugar for a guarded-implication constraint (P2): a logic:onClass target, a logic:trigger predicate (optionally pinned to a logic:triggerValue), and one or more logic:requires companion predicates. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) ∧ trigger(this, …) → ∃ companion. Frontend-only authoring shortcut."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ddaec49203abf23f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "sample of"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ddc278c04b9ec686>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Atomic constraint operand-choice constraint"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dddd08e23d75d259>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Implicit Missingness"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/de4c2ad35cb0f521>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Estimand"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dec52c624e5ef26a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "SPDX license name"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ded6170a2bbd803c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The axis for translation coverage measured per-language by per-literal-class over every localizable literal — labels, definitions, examples, usage coats, rationales, and docs prose — with full coverage requiring English, French, and Mandarin routed through the audited-translation machinery. It is NOT a single ratio: a bare parallel literal with no translation record grades below an audited one."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dee496dac62a8c03>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "plant breeders' rights"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dee7a27ea8fd091a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Requires a logic:Formula carrying logic:consequent to carry logic:antecedent as the ordered first operand of the same material implication. It is not an inverse entailment from conclusion to premise; it is the reverse structural completeness check for the serialized pair."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dfac4be331251af7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The exact scalar square of the top-grade pseudoscalar in a declared Clifford algebra and basis convention."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dfb25f99dc011823>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Underspecified Limit Result"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/dfbad53d55a23265>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:HypothesisTest to the math:AlternativeHypothesis it weighs the evidence toward. Domain math:HypothesisTest, range math:AlternativeHypothesis (stated in prose). The complement of the null; its directionality is carried on the p-value through math:alternativeSidedness."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e0116d842c96924c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: math:HodgeLaplacian to hlap"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e054c7fcb714b97c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Enumeration"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e0740ce8bae5a442>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The defining law of math:nonAffinity as a first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared non-affine, there exist domain points x, y, z with z a proper affine combination of x and y, and graph values u = f(x), v = f(y), w = f(z), such that the three plane points (x,u), (y,v), (z,w) are NOT collinear. math: expresses the law; logic: owns reasoning over it. It uses logic:exists and logic:not exactly as math:connectednessLaw does; the midpoint/affine combination and collinearity are reified as uninterpreted relations, never invented arithmetic functions."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e07a24684e42c4fa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Clifford anticommutation witness to the distinct generator occurring on the right in its forward product."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e09b4d0569c119d0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A single element of a math:Cover: one of the overlapping sets (typically an open set or interval) whose family covers the space. A subclass of math:Set. Two cover elements that overlap induce an edge between the clusters found in their inverse images; a cover element carries the concrete extent (for a real filter, an interval with its endpoints and inclusions) that makes the cover deterministic rather than a free resolution choice."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e0dc7af69b32fa9e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "relative size"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e0f7aa99851f3eaa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the lang slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e0fd5ed8c7959a23>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Linked, and additionally exemplified and tested: worked examples including the epistemically hard case, counter-examples that clash, and competency cells that need reasoning."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e0fe59d12afa0b69>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A candidate interpretation of a form — the structured result object of an interpretation act, carrying a lang:Denotation through lang:denotation and naming the form it reads through lang:readingOf. An ambiguous form holds multiple co-resident readings, each with its own denotation and its own vantage-held support; the readings are first-class data and are never structurally collapsed. A reading is a result, not a claim: the claim that a reading is correct is a separate gmeow:Observation held from a vantage."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e110dc18a4c1dfa2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "documentation floor — Linked"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e15c356801962487>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:InferenceRun (or another analysis gmeow:Activity) to the math:AnalysisPlan it followed. Domain an inference or analysis process, range math:AnalysisPlan (stated in prose). It is the process-layer edge that lets a result's claim to follow a pre-specified plan be traced from the run to the plan and its math:analysisPlanVersion, so 'which plan, at which version, this analysis ran under' is queryable rather than asserted in prose."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e1c37bda01969c67>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Underspecified Interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e1d99872cd8a1f61>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the notation slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e259b34b196209f1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "vocabulary prefix"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e26a74101176ca97>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An alternative hypothesis (H1): the complement of the null a math:HypothesisTest weighs the evidence toward — the effect-present claim whose direction fixes the test's math:alternativeSidedness. A subclass of math:Hypothesis, named by a test through math:alternativeHypothesis; its directionality (one-sided, two-sided, …) is carried on the p-value as sidedness, not left implicit."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e2985bba612d4f34>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Nerve Complex"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e2b5a29b64bf4079>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "install"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e2df81b9f5bc41a8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "GMN-projection exemption"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e31d004855eecc8c>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "non-decreasing"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e3229046827de2f6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Measurement Scale"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e355a23258815b30>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:HypothesisTest or a math:PValue to the framed math:ProbabilityValue carrying its magnitude. Domain a math:HypothesisTest or math:PValue, range math:ProbabilityValue (stated in prose). The p-value's magnitude is a framed probability object in [0, 1] naming its frame or model, never a bare literal; a test names the p-value it produces through this edge, and a math:PValue carries its own magnitude through it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e36a4751fc88c903>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An element of a Clifford algebra expressed as a sum of homogeneous blade components across one or more grades. It is not necessarily a vector or a grade-one element."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e3adabf6ee400d10>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a Clifford extension lacks its base algebra, extended algebra, or additional generator."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e3bda8ef1fd25f9a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A dimensionality-reduction analysis using the Uniform Manifold Approximation and Projection method with its metric and neighborhood parameters declared."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e410d4ea375c5b3b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:HypothesisTest or a math:PValue to the math:Statistic (a function of the data) whose observed value drives the test. Domain a math:HypothesisTest or math:PValue, range math:Statistic (stated in prose). The statistic t whose extremity under the null gives P(T ≥ t | H0); a p-value naming no test statistic is ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e41347771d850014>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The unital associative algebra generated by a quadratic space under the relation v² equals its quadratic form; its field, signature, basis, grading, and product convention must be explicit. It is not an exterior algebra because its product retains the quadratic-form contribution."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e425131c29e5c338>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A carrier with logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:integer but no logic:termLiteral violates this constraint."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e43f4e8f6d57b4e6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:PValue to the object defining which tail (or tails) of its null distribution the extremity is measured over. Domain math:PValue, range the tail-definition object (stated in prose). Together with math:alternativeSidedness it fixes how the extremity is counted; a p-value declaring neither a tail definition nor a sidedness is ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e44b29eb13ec21dd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The exact number of logic:onProperty values belonging to the qualifying logic:onClass or logic:onDataRange. It does not count fillers outside that qualifier; it lowers to owl:qualifiedCardinality."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e467cd0caae0a28e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "GMEOW Lifecycle Module"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e468be61498bc961>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "analysis output"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e493dea33374c423>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "axis weight"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e4a835c3fe797caa>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates an information measure to the unit its magnitude is expressed in — the bit (base 2), the nat (base e), or the hartley (base 10) — paired with the declared logarithm base. Domain math:InformationMeasure, range math:InformationUnit (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e4cf3e8106432dbf>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a complex, sheaf, or graded space to the Laplacian operator defined on it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e4eae03537101206>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "One distinct sense a homograph surface evokes. Domain lang:DeclaredTerminologyHomograph, range lang:LexicalConcept. Non-functional and meaningful only in the plural: the exemption is granted only when two or more distinct lang:LexicalConcepts are named (fewer than two is not a homograph and grants no exemption). The glossary projection routes each occurrence of the declared source onto the matching concept, so divergent renderings across distinct senses are legitimate."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e506ed3371604c65>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "vocabulary subsumed by"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e53eb8391e8f6d0f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A prediction interval: an interval expected to contain a FUTURE observation (a new data point), not a fixed parameter — wider than a confidence interval because it carries the sampling uncertainty of a new draw on top of the estimation uncertainty. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, deliberately left PARADIGM-NEUTRAL (under neither math:FrequentistResult nor math:BayesianResult) because a prediction interval is constructed in both paradigms — a frequentist prediction interval and a Bayesian posterior-predictive interval are the same interval kind under different frames — so forcing it into one family would misclassify the other. It names its bounds through math:hasIntervalBound and the target it predicts through math:predictionTarget."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e56216826d0fcd02>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "sheaf base complex"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e57edfb2d7628b63>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:VectorSymbolicCapacity to the exact math:RationalValue of the maximum number of representations it may bind or superpose before recovery degrades — carried as an exact numerator/denominator pair, never a decimal, so the capacity is reproducible. Domain math:VectorSymbolicCapacity, range math:RationalValue (stated in prose)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e5874c3f1687fbb1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:PValue to the distribution of its test statistic UNDER the null — the frame against which the observed value's extremity is measured. Domain math:PValue, range a math:Distribution, typically a math:SamplingDistribution (stated in prose). A p-value naming no null distribution is ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e5d4a93470d4584d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e5df9b99d5a6f78b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Sample or math:Estimate to the math:StatisticalPopulation it refers to — the target of inference the sample stands in for and the estimate speaks about. Domain a math:Sample or math:Estimate, range math:StatisticalPopulation (stated in prose). Naming the population is what keeps who-we-care-about distinct from who-we-measured; an estimate that names no population it refers to is underspecified."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e5f6a6d8cdfdb827>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The logic: property-characteristic marker for reflexivity: every individual in scope relates to itself through the property. It is not evidence that self-edges were explicitly asserted; the OWL projection is owl:ReflexiveProperty."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e619a79d74447958>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for gmeow:methodDirectObservation: `dir`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e632a506c55ad299>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A stand-off anchor locating a surface form in a source: names the source through lang:anchorSource, the span through lang:anchorStart and lang:anchorEnd, and the offset space through lang:offsetSpace (byte, codepoint, or grapheme cluster). Surface-stratum material excluded from form identity but included in surface identity; the anchor is what makes the prose-hash discipline a lookup rather than a recomputation."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e63f33d51f10838e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The destruction event associated with this existence record. Optional: an EntityExistence for a still-extant entity has no destruction event."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e69b94330fe9e40d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Spectral Initialization"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e6a7d830d680827f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Clifford extension to the additional basis generator, including its grade and exact square."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e72ce203c57d7c6f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Surface Form"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e72dd4cbad143bdb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a mathematical representation to the group, algebra, or structured object it represents."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e7410d6e192b0e3b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Estimand to the math:StatisticalContrast it targets — the comparison between conditions (a difference, ratio, odds ratio, hazard ratio of the outcome) the estimand quantifies. Domain math:Estimand, range math:StatisticalContrast (stated in prose). The contrast is the SHARED modeled object also referenced by an effect size, so the estimand's target and the effect-size's scale name the same comparison; an average treatment effect estimand targets the treatment-minus-control contrast of its outcome."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e77e06327bc4dadb>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "inferential density"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e7f0d1b05442119a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Function Piece"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e80a4ed5532cd342>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "extended real line (ℝ̄)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e8181f866e7b3cff>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "has monotonicity"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e863be244aad819e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A map from a reduced or embedded representation toward a source-space reconstruction, with exactness, approximation, and round-trip loss declared rather than assumed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e8ac08de0f83eaf8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The reified, time-scoped fact that an entity existed over an interval — a gufo:Situation that carries its period via gmeow:duringInterval (inherited from TimeScopedRelation). Use when the existence claim is contested (two sources disagree on when a place ceased to exist), when evidence must be attached, or when standpoint indexing is needed. Flat-first: the common case uses gmeow:hasCreationEvent / gmeow:hasDestructionEvent / gmeow:existenceInterval directly on the entity."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e8d33c38e9317db9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Hamiltonian Flow"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e8e0045e63b9727d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The outcome of a limit that decreases without bound: f runs off to the negative pole, so the math:LimitResult carries math:NegativeInfinity as its math:limitResultValue. The case lim_{x→a} f(x) = −∞ — the dual of math:divergesToPositiveInfinity, a definite point on ℝ̄."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e925e60d102b88be>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "target population"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e926de26bdc08d40>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An estimand: the target quantity a study is actually trying to learn — the thing an estimate speaks about, distinct from any coefficient inside a particular model. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject framed by the six coordinates that make it well-posed: the target population it refers to (math:targetPopulation), the outcome measured on that population (math:targetOutcome), the contrast between conditions it compares (math:targetContrast, a math:StatisticalContrast), the time or horizon it is defined at (math:targetTime), the intervention condition it conditions on (math:interventionCondition), and the missing-data policy under which it is defined (math:missingDataPolicy). This framing is load-bearing for causal inference, surveys, trials, and policy models, where the same estimand (an average treatment effect) can be targeted by different parameters under different models. An estimate names its estimand through math:estimatesEstimand; an estimand held apart from the model parameter is what keeps the target of inference from being read off a coefficient."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e956b68a99ffe91a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the music slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e96d5d39b0db70ae>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The prose-quality-axis score floor to earn the Grounded tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e97f41583b6cf8ce>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Clifford algebra to a calculated witness for one distinct-generator anticommutation law."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e9986f4e8e869d90>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Statistical Population"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e99d1d8d10d8f790>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Hodge Decomposition"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/e9f8351fc2f582bc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Value restriction requiring the logic:onProperty relation to contain one named IRI or literal. It is not a range declaration; it lowers to owl:hasValue."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ea1529d109c50bcc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "device"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ea37d50c66b84152>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Compact sugar for an aggregate-comparison constraint (P6): a logic:onClass target, an aggregate over a path (logic:aggFunction, optional logic:aggDistinct, logic:aggPath), a logic:aggComparator, and a logic:aggCompareTo right-hand side (a compared property IRI, or a literal). Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint carrying both the honest reified FOL integrity and a structured aggregate satellite, lowered to a SELECT $this … GROUP BY $this HAVING(…) sh:SPARQLConstraint. Frontend-only authoring shortcut."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ea3bbe8ccd9f8022>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the fno projection vocabulary on the music slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/ea58d3b3076680ec>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The rank of a homology group in a specified degree, counting independent topological features of that degree. It is not a simplex count or an Euler characteristic."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/eb3f02726dce3196>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "ex:memberType a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Team ; logic:valuePath ex:member ; logic:valueClass ex:Person ."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/eb5cdac6b50a21cc>
