    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "anonymize"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f0b8b36785eeef94>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A frequentist inference result: the family of result objects whose semantics rest on the behaviour of a procedure under repeated sampling — a p-value, a sampling distribution, a confidence interval, statistical power, and the Type I / Type II error rates. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject and one of the two inference-paradigm result families, held owl:disjointWith math:BayesianResult so a single result is never read as both frequentist and Bayesian. The paradigm axis is a PARTIAL classification: only paradigm-exclusive kinds are placed under it, so a paradigm-neutral object (a math:Estimate, a math:Residual) is left free of either family rather than forced into one."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f0d20c7d319745d8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Cell Complex"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f11ef13bcf9a3e65>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Model Diagnostic"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f140052e91a194d0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "rule action"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f1532d1ac2986b3d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "right operand reference"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f15775279730e109>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Faithful Representation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f1754420876cfcdc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "limit outcome"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f17ae8c933770500>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Requires a logic:Formula carrying logic:antecedent to carry logic:consequent as the ordered second operand of the same material implication. It is not a rule that derives a consequent; it is a structural integrity condition on the implication node."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f1a8cbe1bb1766e3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a Hamiltonian system to the scalar function whose symplectic gradient generates its evolution."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f1c9112389462e2e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Do not use a sugar class when the integrity condition needs a formula shape the selected closed pattern cannot preserve."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f1e2d4e27f1806c5>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The information-axis score floor to earn the Linked tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f2210ac0966e3f43>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "denotation of the GMN boundary-operator key"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f2485fa2c1c0acee>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Requires a carrier with logic:termLiteralDatatype to carry logic:termLiteral, so a datatype IRI can never float without the lexical literal it types. It does not require a datatype for every literal; absence denotes a plain literal."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f25dcc5d54e93332>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The documentation-axis score floor to earn the Grounded tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f2cc1aa396878b89>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:PValue to its math:Sidedness — the enumerated value (one of the six math:Sidedness individuals) fixing whether the extremity is one-sided, two-sided, greater, less, exact, or mid-p. Domain math:PValue, range math:Sidedness (stated in prose). A closed value carried by sh:in; a p-value declaring neither a sidedness nor a math:tailDefinition is ill-framed (math:IllFramedPValue), and a value outside the six is not a lawful sidedness."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f2fcaeeb16120bd2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An estimate: a produced value that estimates an estimand (math:estimatesEstimand) and, where relevant, a model parameter (math:estimatedParameter), carrying its value (math:estimateValue) and the estimator that produced it (math:estimator). A subclass of math:MathematicalObject and the structured result object of the process / result / claim separation — neither the analysis activity nor the held claim, and never a bare number: it fixes both WHAT it estimates (its estimand and/or its estimated parameter) and HOW (the estimator that produced it), and one naming neither its target quantity nor a model parameter, or naming no estimator, is underspecified (math:UnderspecifiedEstimate). The R broom tidy triple lifts model coefficients onto these objects."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f304271dc6142554>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "information floor — Linked"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f31549a29dc04fda>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "distribute"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f344acc70edb9efd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Tolerance Interval"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f3a7ef92ac3c48e1>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The defining law of math:nonIncreasing as a universally-quantified first-order logic:Formula over the reified real/value signature: for a function f declared non-increasing, if x < y and f takes value u at x and v at y, then u ≥ v — the function never rises. The non-strict counterpart of math:strictMonotonicityLaw."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f3d7f467376b7b90>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Scalar Field"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f3dce38e607d5302>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: math:Division to div"@en .

