    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Do not read the required edge as logical modus ponens; it only completes the serialized constructor."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f7168121652c9c22>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The unary prefix GMN named-key form `rev` for math:Reversion; tilde remains non-executable display notation because it is confusable with approximation, negation, and programming operators."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f758fb13972369fc>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates an equivariant map to the group action or symmetry with which it commutes."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f78210678ce0d8fd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "negation"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f7c6179e1f43d526>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A compatible assignment of local stalk values over a region of a sheaf's base space."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f7da1084d69048ff>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The audited named-key ruling for the conventional partial-sign notation of math:BoundaryOperator."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f85ae95abc8c7f87>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A carrier with both logic:termIri ex:a and logic:termVariable 'a' violates this constraint even though the spellings resemble one another."@en .

