<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f8a72d8512cc48ca>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An element of a declared spin representation or spinor module associated with a quadratic space."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f8c8146827d8f43a>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Clifford Involution"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f8f807e598b102e3>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "unregistered (™)"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f9534afd199299a7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Sample"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f97f3c123358f172>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The date the exemption was minted — making every exemption dated so a stale escape is visible and auditable. It is NOT an expiry (the staleness gate, not a calendar, retires the exemption when the producer lands)."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f98b9fcbdc8380d8>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Negative infinity as an extended-real value: the negative pole of the signed extended real line math:ExtendedRealLine, the dual of math:PositiveInfinity. It is the extended-real point that lets an unbounded-below quantity — a limit diverging downward, the infimum of a set with no lower bound — be declared without a finite literal. It is NOT a finite number (it lives nowhere in ℝ); NOT an error, exception, or missing value; and NOT the undefined/indeterminate result that math:PositiveInfinity + math:NegativeInfinity or 0 · ∞ would give — an extended real is a definite point on ℝ̄, never a NaN. A signed-extended-real slot (math:extendedRealValue) holds either a finite number, math:PositiveInfinity, or this individual."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f9a074328434ddb2>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The meaning assignment from `boundary` to the class math:BoundaryOperator; it deliberately carries no executable grapheme."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f9f17f612624415e>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Inference Run"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/f9f782cc411af0ae>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Graded Algebra"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fa421574fbc6df74>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The failure raised when a math:ConfidenceInterval does not carry the structure that makes it an interval estimate — its bounds through math:hasIntervalBound (a two-sided interval names its lower AND upper endpoint) or its coverage through math:confidenceLevel (a framed math:ProbabilityValue over the sampling procedure). A confidence interval with no bounds, or with no confidence level, is not a coverage statement but a bare pair of numbers, and is ill-formed."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fa70871048d8c6a6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "GMN candidate: Clifford reversion"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/faaf90628d885238>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "An order-two operation on a Clifford algebra, with its action on grades and product order declared. It is not an arbitrary algebra endomorphism: applying it twice must return the input."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fb07e2db7aa226ca>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The cohomological invariants measuring obstructions to gluing local sheaf data into global sections."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fb1e1c028ffbeb6b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The projection-axis score floor to earn the Maximal tier."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fb2d3a0c4b5b85cd>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The slice whose terminology a gmeow:Glossary gathers. Functional: exactly one slice per glossary. Domain gmeow:Glossary, range the slice's owl:Ontology IRI."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fb7bf33b3b3ad680>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The coeffect grade of the axis: how much graph the measurement primitive may READ — slice-local, the slice plus its dependency closure, or the whole merged closure. Advice output is ALWAYS constrained to the single target slice regardless of scope; the scope governs reads only, and a slice-local axis that touches the merged graph is a gated invariant violation. It is NOT a permission to advise cross-slice."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fc0ec5092237539b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection-ceiling commitment — affect / bfo"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fc1306d237ff7cc6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "One term-grain binding in a glossary: relates one term's English source literal (gmeow:glossarySource) for one predicate (gmeow:glossaryPredicate) on one term (gmeow:glossaryTerm) to its target-language rendering (gmeow:glossaryTranslation), carrying the OntoLex Frege triangle — a lang:Sense (gmeow:glossarySense) that lang:evokes the entry's lang:LexicalConcept (gmeow:glossaryConcept) — and the crossing's law-spine through gmeow:glossaryUnit (a lang:TranslationUnit whose logic:Correspondence holds the honest logic:preservationKind). A gmeow:Glossary holds zero or more entries through gmeow:glossaryEntry. Two distinct terms the projection assigns one concept carry two distinct senses that both evoke that concept, so synonymy is DERIVED (two senses evoking one concept) rather than asserted flat. The consistency invariant is stated over gmeow:glossaryConcept, so two entries the projection assigns one concept must agree on their translation; a declared homograph (lang:DeclaredTerminologyHomograph) is projected onto DISTINCT concepts (its senses evoke distinct concepts) and legitimately renders each differently."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fc1badd72ad56c13>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "prose quality"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fc6bf2859437319f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "tail definition"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fc81407449cd6e49>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:VectorSpace, math:QuadraticSpace, or math:CliffordAlgebra to a math:Basis of its carrier. Range math:Basis (stated in prose). A space or algebra may carry several bases; a Clifford basis fixes the ordered generators used by its exact products and blade witnesses."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fcb53644b3e9494b>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates a math:Function (or a math:FunctionPiece) to a math:AnalyticProperty it bears — its non-affinity, convexity, boundedness, or smoothness. Domain math:Function or math:FunctionPiece, range math:AnalyticProperty (stated in prose). The declared bearer of a qualitative analytic claim; because the named property carries its defining law or boundary (math:definingLaw), the claim is always backed by a real logic:Formula or an honest recorded boundary, never a bare flag."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fcc1ecc1af7e6dc6>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The version-3 alias binding for math:Division: `div`, retained unchanged from version 2."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fcf8519583791bda>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The audited named-key ruling for the conventional delta notation of math:CoboundaryOperator."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fd0f1de1b32cff2d>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "projection floor — Maximal"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fd114f885accb5ea>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Rights Action"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fd43d8026c2932e0>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Relates an iterative mathematical analysis to the explicit initialization from which its optimization or iteration begins."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fd46652585b7867f>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "homograph concept"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fd47a397aac12196>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A bilinear product operation defined within a declared Clifford algebra and governed by its quadratic form."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fd58afc96281de75>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "The committed lower-only ungrounded-residue ceiling for the sh projection vocabulary on the learning slice; the gate reds if the slice's measured residue rises above it."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fdce3ecde77af2a7>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "A function assigning to each point of a manifold a vector in the tangent space at that point."@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fded2bd8e9352106>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "dict-v3 entry: actual modal force to act"@en .

<http://example.org/lang/glossary-vartrans/form-src/fdfc6470e04fccb9>
    a ontolex:Form ;
    ontolex:writtenRep "Persistent Homology"@en .

